Smecna conjecit Palackius in libro Würdigung, etc
p 23.</NOTE> . Haec fuit inter feminas una <NOTE N="156" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0061" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0061"></COL> mira 1. 7.</NOTE>  prorsus
femina in consilio provida, in sermone strennua,
corpore casta, moribus proba, ad dirimenda populi
judicia nulli secunda, omnibus affabilis set plus
amabilis, feminei sexus decus et gloria, dictans
negotia providenter virilia. Set quia nemo ex omni
 <COL N="0063A"></COL> parte beatus <NOTE N="157" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(256)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063D"></COL> Hor., Od. II, 16, 27.</NOTE> , talis ac tantae laudis femina,
heu dira conditio humana! fuit phitonissa <NOTE N="158" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> fitonissa 2. phytonissa 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . phitonissa 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Et
quia populo multa et certa praedixit futura, omnis
illa gens commune consilium iniens <NOTE N="159" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> inigens  <HI REND="ITALIC">deleto</HI>  g A.</NOTE> , patris ejus
post necem hanc sibi praefecit in judicem <NOTE N="160" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Et quia populo
—in judicem  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa in</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Ea <NOTE N="161" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Et 1.</NOTE> 
tempestate inter duos cives, opibus et genere eminentiores
et qui videbantur populi esse rectores,
orta est non modica litigio agri contigui de termino <NOTE N="162" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> continui determinio A.</NOTE> .
Qui in tantum proruperunt in mutuam
rixam, ut alter alterius spissam unguibus volaret in
barbam, et nudis convitiis semetipsos turpiter digito
sub nasum confundentes, intrant bachantes curiam,
ac non sine magno strepitu adeunt dominam, et ut
ratione justitiae dubiam inter eos dirimat <NOTE N="163" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> diremit  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  dirimat A.</NOTE>  causam
suppliciter <NOTE N="164" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> supliciter
1.</NOTE>  rogant. Illa interim, ut est lasciva
 <COL N="0063B"></COL> mollities mulierum quando non habet <NOTE N="165" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> lit A.</NOTE>  quem timeat
 <NOTE N="166" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> timeat A.</NOTE>  virum, cubito subnixa, ceu puerum enixa,
alte in pictis stratis <NOTE N="167" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> thoris A.</NOTE>  nimis molliter accubabat <NOTE N="168" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> acubabat 1.</NOTE> .
Cumque <NOTE N="169" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> cum A.</NOTE>  per callem justitiae incedens <NOTE N="170" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr. al.
manus in 4. pro</HI>  indecens; indecens 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , personam
hominum non respiciens <NOTE N="171" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> aspiciens 2.</NOTE> , totius controversiae
inter eos ortae causam ad statum rectitudinis perduceret,
tunc is, cujus causa in judicio non <NOTE N="172" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">manu secunda</HI>  A.</NOTE>  obtinuit
palmam, plus justo indignatus terque <NOTE N="173" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> ter 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  quaterque
caput concussit, et more suo terram ter baculo
 <NOTE N="174" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> baculis
2.</NOTE>  percussit, ac barbam pleno ore saliva
conspergens <NOTE N="175" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> conspuens A. aspergens 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  exclamavit <NOTE N="176" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> exclamat 2. 3. 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(257)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063D"></COL> In carmine populari Judicium Libussae (cfr.
librum quem ediderunt viri clariss. Safarik et Palacky:
Die ältesten Denkmäler der Bohmischen
Sprache. Prag 1840), de cujus fide inter summos
viros maxima exorta est contentio, haec leguntur
l. l. p. 47:

 <POEM COM="0063"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Und vor Wuth erbebten alle Glieder,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Schwingt den Arm und brüllet gleich dem Ure.</HI></L> <L><COL N="0064D"></COL> ——</L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Weh den Mannern, wenn ein Weib gebietet!</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">O injuria viris
haud toleranda! femina rimosa virilia judicia mente
tractat dolosa. Scimus profecto quia femina sive
stans</HI> <NOTE N="177" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> stat 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">seu in solio residens</HI> <NOTE N="178" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> resideat  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al.
manus in</HI>  4. licet  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">parum sapit</HI> <NOTE N="179" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> sapiat 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , 7.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quanto minus cum in stratis accubat? Revera tunc
 <COL N="0063C"></COL> magis est ad accessum mariti apta, quam dictare
militibus jura. Certum est enim, longos esse crines
omnibus set breves sensus mulieribus. Satius est mori,
quam viris talia pati. Nos solos obprobium nationibus
et gentibus destituit natura, quibus deest rector et
virilis censura, et quos premunt feminea jura.</HI>  Ad haec
domina <NOTE N="180" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> domna 1. Lubossa  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  illatam sibi contumeliam dissimulans, et
dolorem cordis femineo pudore celans, subrisit et:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Ita est,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut ais; femina sum, femina vivo, set
 <COL N="0064A"></COL> ideo parum sapere vobis videor, quia vos non in virga
ferrea judico</HI> <NOTE N="(258)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0064" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0064D"></COL> In carmine populari p. 48:

 <POEM COM="0064"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Wahlt den Mann euch unter eures gleichen,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Der euch herrsche mit dem Eisen.</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI> <NOTE N="181" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> sed 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quonian sine timore</HI> <NOTE N="182" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> sine dolore et timore 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vivitis,
merito me despicitis. Nam ubi timor est, ibi</HI> <NOTE N="183" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">manu secunda</HI>  A.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI> <NOTE N="184" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> est  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  3. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">honor. Nunc autem necesse est valde, ut habeatis</HI> 
 <NOTE N="185" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1. 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">rectorem femina fortiorem</HI> <NOTE N="186" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> ferociorem
1. 4. 7.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sic et columbae
olim albiculum</HI> <NOTE N="(259)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0064" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0064D"></COL> Num legendum  <HI REND="ITALIC">albidulum?</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">milvum</HI> <NOTE N="187" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> milvium 7.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quem</HI> <NOTE N="188" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> que 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sibi elegerant</HI> 
 <NOTE N="189" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> elegerunt 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in regem, spreverunt, ut vos me spernitis, et
accipitrem multo fortiorem</HI> <NOTE N="190" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> ferociorem 1. 4. 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sibi ducem praefecerunt,
qui fingens culpas tam nocentes quam innocentes coepit
necare et ex tunc usque hodie vescitur columbis
accipiter. Ite nunc domum, ut quem vos cras eligatis
in dominum, ego assumam mihi</HI> <NOTE N="191" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> mihi  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A. 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in maritum.</HI>  Interea
praedictas advocat sorores, quas non impares
agitabant furores, quarum magica arte et propria
ludificabat populum per omnia; ipsa enim Lubossa
 <COL N="0064B"></COL> fuit, sicut praediximus, phitonissa, ut Chumaea Sybilla,
altera venefica ut Cholchis <NOTE N="192" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Cholhis A. Chcohis 1.</NOTE>  Medea, tertia
malefica ut Aeaeae <NOTE N="193" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> AE AE AE 2. 2 <SUP>a</SUP>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Circes <NOTE N="194" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. 1.</NOTE> . Illa nocte quid consilii
inierint illae tres Eumenides, aut quid secreti
egerint, quamvis ignotum fuerit, tamen omnibus
luce clarius mane patuit, cum soror earum Lubossa
et locum ubi dux futurus latuit, et quis esset, nomine
indicavit. Quis enim crederet quod de aratro sibi
ducem praerogarent? Aut quis sciret, ubi araret qui
rector populi fieret? Quid enim phitonicus furor
nescit? Aut quid est, quod magica ars non efficit <NOTE N="195" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> sufficit 2.</NOTE> ?
Potuit Sybilla Romano populo seriem fatorum fere
usque in diem judicii praedicere, quae etiam, si fas
est credere, de Christo vaticinata est, sicut quidam
doctor in sermone suae praedicationis versus Virgilii
 <COL N="0064C"></COL> <NOTE N="196" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Virgili 1. Vigilii 2.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(260)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0064" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0064D"></COL> Cf. Augustini exposit. ep. ad Roman. Opp. III,
2, p. 629, et Virg., Eclog. IV ad Pollionem.</NOTE>  ex persona Sibyllae de adventu Domini
compositos introducit. Potuit Medea herbis <NOTE N="197" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> cibis 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  et
carmine saepe e coelo Hyperionem <NOTE N="198" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Yporionem A.</NOTE>  et Berecinthiam
 <NOTE N="199" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Herecinthiam 1. 2.</NOTE>  deducere; potuit ymbres, fulgura et <NOTE N="200" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE> 
tonitrua elicere <NOTE N="201" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> ducere 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  de nubibus; potuit regem Eiacum
 <NOTE N="202" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Egacum
1. 2. 4. 7.</NOTE>  de sene facere juvenem. Carmine Circes <NOTE N="203" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Cirnis 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
socii Ulixis <NOTE N="204" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> Ulixes 1. 2.</NOTE>  conversi sunt <NOTE N="(261)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0064" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0064D"></COL> Virg., Eclog. VIII, 69, 70.</NOTE>  in diversas ferarum
formas, et rex Picus in volucrem, quae <NOTE N="205" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0063" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0063"></COL> qui 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  nunc
dicitur picus. Quid mirum? Quanta egerunt artibus
 <COL N="0065A"></COL> suis magi in Aegipto? qui pene totidem mira carminibus
suis fecerunt, quot Dei famulus Moyses ex
virtute Dei exhibuisse <NOTE N="206" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> hab.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  exh. A.</NOTE>  perhibetur. Hactenus haec.</P> <P COM="0065">5. Postera die, ut jussum fuerat, sine mora convocant
coetum, congregant populum; conveniunt
simul omnes in unum, femina <NOTE N="207" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> Lubossa  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4.</NOTE>  residens in sublimi
solio concionatur ad agrestes viros <NOTE N="208" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> dicens  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">O plebs
miseranda nimis, quae libera vivere nescit, et quam
nemo bonus nisi cum vita amittit, illam vos non inviti
libertatem fugitis, et insuetae servituti colla sponte
submittitis. Heu tarde frustra vos poenitebit, sicut
poenituit ranas</HI> <NOTE N="209" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> s. p. r.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum</HI> <NOTE N="210" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> que  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI> 
cum A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">yárus</HI> <NOTE N="211" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> ydrus  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  ydra A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quem</HI> <NOTE N="212" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> quam A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">manu secunda.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sibi
fecerant regem, eas necare coepit. Aut si nescitis,
quae sunt</HI> <NOTE N="213" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> sint A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jura ducis, temptabo vobis ea verbis
dicere paucis. Inprimis</HI> <NOTE N="214" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> Inprime  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  Inprimo 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">facile est ducem ponere, set
 <COL N="0065B"></COL> difficile est positum deponere; nam qui</HI> <NOTE N="215" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> namque 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">modo est
sub vestra potestate, utrum eum constituatis ducem
an non, postquam vero constitutus fuerit, vos et omnia
vestra erunt ejus in potestate. Hujus in conspectu
vestra febricitabunt</HI> <NOTE N="216" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> febricita habet 1. febricitata labentur 3. 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">genua, et muta sicco palato
adhaerebit lingua. Ad cujus vocem prae nimio pavore
vix respondebitis: «Ita domine, ita domine</HI> <NOTE N="217" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> i. d.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semet legit</HI>  A.</NOTE> ,»  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum
ipse</HI> <NOTE N="218" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> ipse  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">solo suo nutu sine vestro praejudicio hunc
dampnabit, et hunc obtruncabit, istum in carcerem
mitti, illum praecipiet in patibulo suspendi. Vos
ipsos</HI> <NOTE N="219" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A. vos ipsos—tollet  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ex vobis quos sibi libet, alios servos, alios
rusticos, alios tributarios, alios exactores, alios tortores,
alios</HI> <NOTE N="220" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> alios  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">praecones, alios cocos seu pistores</HI> <NOTE N="221" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> piscatores 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aut</HI> <NOTE N="222" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> alios 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">molendinarios faciet. Constituet etiam sibi tribunos,
centuriones, villicos, cultores vinearum simul
 <COL N="0065C"></COL> et agrorum, messores segetum, fabros armorum, sutores
pellium diversarum et coriorum. Filios vestros
et filias in obsequiis suis ponet; de bubus etiam et
equis sive equabus seu peccoribus vestris optima quaeque
 <COL N="0066A"></COL> ad suum palatium</HI> <NOTE N="223" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> placitum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">exceptis</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et 1. rel.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tollet. Omnia vestra quae
sunt potiora</HI> <NOTE N="224" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> quaeque pecora sunt 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">in villis, in campis, in agris, in pratis,
in vineis auferet, et in usus suos rediget. Quid
multis moror? Aut ad quid</HI> <NOTE N="225" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> ad q. ad h. 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">haec, quasi vos</HI> <NOTE N="226" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> vos uterream 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut
terream, loquor? Si persistitis in</HI> <NOTE N="227" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> in
cepto 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">incepto et non
fallitis voto, jam vobis et nomen ducis et locum ubi
est indicabo.</HI>  Ad haec vulgus ignobile confuso exultat
 <NOTE N="228" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> exaltante 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  clamore; omnes uno ore ducem sibi poscunt
dari. Quibus illa:  <HI REND="ITALIC">En,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">en ultra illos <NOTE N="229" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> vos A.</NOTE> 
montes</HI> —et monstravit digito montes— <HI REND="ITALIC">est</HI> <NOTE N="230" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> ubi 2.</NOTE>  fluvius
non adeo magnus nomine Belina <NOTE N="231" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> Belena 7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(262)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065D"></COL> Bilin in regione Lutomericensi, qui apud
Aussig in Albim exundat.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cujus
super ripam dinoscitur esse</HI> <NOTE N="232" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">villa, nomine Stadici</HI> 
 <NOTE N="233" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> Ztadiczi 1. 3. 7.
Ztadici 2. 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(263)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065D"></COL> Staditz.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hujus in territorio</HI> <NOTE N="234" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> teriorio A. teritorio 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">est novale unum, in
longitudine et in latitudine</HI> <NOTE N="235" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> in  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> . et in lat.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  22 <NOTE N="236" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> XII. 1. 2. 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">passuum, quod
mirum in modum, cum sit inter tot</HI> <NOTE N="237" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> tantos
2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">agnos in medio
 <COL N="0066B"></COL> positum, ad nullum tamen pertinet agrum</HI> <NOTE N="(264)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065D"></COL> Campus nostris etiam diebus Konigsfeld a populo
 <COL N="0066D"></COL> vocatur. Cf. Palacky Geschichte von Bohmen I, 87.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ibi
dux vester duobus variis bubus arat; unus bos praecinctus
est albedine et albo capite</HI> <NOTE N="238" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">alter a fronte
post tergum</HI> <NOTE N="239" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> tegrum 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">albus, et pedes posteriores habens
albos. Nunc, si vobis placet, meum accipite thalarium</HI> 
 <NOTE N="240" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. thalitarium 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et clamidem ac mutatoria</HI> <NOTE N="(265)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0066" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0066D"></COL> Scilicet indumenta.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">duce digna,
et pergite ac mandata populi atque</HI> <NOTE N="241" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> ac A. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mea referte
viro, et adducite vobis ducem et mihi maritum. Viro
nomen est</HI> <NOTE N="242" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> est  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Premizl</HI> <NOTE N="243" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A.
Primizl  <HI REND="ITALIC">alii excepto</HI>  2. Prziemysl  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic porro.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui super colla et capita
vestra jura excogitabit plura</HI> —nam hoc nomen latine
sonat praemeditans vel superexcogitans <NOTE N="(266)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0066" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0066D"></COL> Cf. Dobner ad Hajecium II, 158.</NOTE> —
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Hujus proles postera</HI> <NOTE N="244" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> postea 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hac</HI> <NOTE N="245" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> haec. 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in omni terra in aeternum
regnabit</HI> <NOTE N="246" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et ultra.</HI></P> <P COM="0066">6. Interea destinantur qui jussa dominae et plebis
ad virum perferant nuncii; quos ut vidit domina
 <COL N="0066C"></COL> quasi inscios de via cunctari:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">cunctamini?
Ite securi, meum equum sequimini, ipse vos
ducet</HI> <NOTE N="247" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> adducet A.
deducet 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">recta via et reducet, quia ab illo non semel
illa via est trita.</HI> 

 <POEM COM="0066"><L>Vana volat fama, nec non et <NOTE N="248" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  opinio falsa, quod ipsa domina</L> <L>equitatu phantasmatico semper in noctis conticinio</L> <L>solita sit ire illo, et redire prae gallicinio:</L></POEM> 

quod Judaeus credat <NOTE N="249" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7.</NOTE>  Apella <NOTE N="(267)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0066" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0066D"></COL> Hor. serm. I, 5, 100.</NOTE> . Quid tamen <NOTE N="250" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> tamen A. dum 7.</NOTE> ?
Procedunt nuncii sapienter indocti, vadunt scienter
nescii, vestigia sequentes equi. Jamque montes transierant,
jam <NOTE N="251" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> i. i. a. v. a. q. i.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE>  jamque adpropinquabant villae ad
 <COL N="0066C"></COL> quam ibant, tum <NOTE N="252" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> tunc
4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . dum 7.</NOTE>  illis puer unus obviam currit,
quem <NOTE N="253" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  interrogantes aiunt <NOTE N="254" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> ad illum  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Heus bonae indolis
puer, estne villa ista nomine Stadici</HI> <NOTE N="255" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0065" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0065"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. Ztadici  <HI REND="ITALIC">alii.</HI>  Ztadiczi 7 <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">aut si est
in illa vir nomine Premizl?—Ipsa est,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quam
 <COL N="0067A"></COL> quaeritis villa, et ecce vir Premizl prope in agro boves
stimulat, ut, quod agit, citius opus</HI> <NOTE N="256" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> opus  <HI REND="ITALIC">omittit</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">peragat.</HI>  Ad
quem nuncii accedentes inquiunt:

 <POEM COM="0067"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Vir fortunate, dux nobis</HI> <NOTE N="257" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> nobis  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">diis generate!</HI></L></POEM> 

Et, sicut mos est rusticis, non sufficit <NOTE N="258" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> sufficiunt 1.</NOTE>  semel dixisse,
set inflata bucca ingeminant

 <POEM COM="0067"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Salve dux, salve</HI> <NOTE N="259" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> dux  <HI REND="ITALIC">repetunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">magna dignissime laude,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Solve boves, muta vestes, ascende caballum!</HI></L></POEM> 
Et <NOTE N="260" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> Et—caballum  <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine
codicis</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">scripta, desunt in</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . sternutantemque  <HI REND="ITALIC">omnes except.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  monstrant vestes sternuntque caballum.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Domina nostra Lubossa et plebs universa</HI> <NOTE N="261" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> immensa 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mandat,
ut cito venias, et tibi ac tuis nepotibus fatale regnum
accipias. Omnia nostra et nos ipsi in tua manu sumus,
te ducem, te judicem, te rectorem, te protectorem,
te solum nobis in dominum eligimus.</HI>  Ad quam
vocem vir prudens <NOTE N="262" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> Primizl
 <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , quasi futurorum inscius <NOTE N="263" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> praescius  <HI REND="ITALIC">subducto</HI>  inscius 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
 <COL N="0067B"></COL> substitit, et stimulum quem manu gestabat in terram
fixit, et solvens boves:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ite illuc inde venistis!</HI> 
dixit; qui statim citius dicto ab oculis evanuerunt,
et nusquam amplius comparuerunt. Corilus autem <NOTE N="264" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE> ,
quam humi fixit, tres altas propagines, et
quod est mirabilius, cum foliis et nucibus produxit.
Viri autem illi <NOTE N="265" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  videntes haec talia ita <NOTE N="266" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> ibi A.</NOTE>  fieri,
stabant obstupefacti. Quos ille grata vice hospitum
invitat ad prandium, et de pera subere <NOTE N="267" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> subure
4.</NOTE>  contexta
excutit <NOTE N="268" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> ccutit A.</NOTE>  mucidum <NOTE N="269" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. 1. 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  3. nucidum  <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine</HI>  muscidum  <HI REND="ITALIC">manu antiqua</HI>  2. muscidum 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> ,
mucidum vel muscidum 7.</NOTE>  panem et formatici partem,
et ipsam peram in cespite pro mensa et super rude
textum ponit et caetera <NOTE N="270" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> 7' <SUP>c</SUP>  A.</NOTE> . Interea dum prandium
sumunt <NOTE N="271" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> dum prandium sumunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , dum aquam de amphora bibunt, duae
propagines sive <NOTE N="272" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> seu 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  sive
virgulta duo  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>  virgulta duo aruerunt et ceciderunt,
set tertia multo altius et latius <NOTE N="273" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> altius A.</NOTE>  accrescebat.
 <COL N="0067C"></COL> Unde hospitibus major excrevit admiratio <NOTE N="274" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> ammir- <HI REND="ITALIC">constanter</HI>  A. 4.</NOTE> 
cum timore. Et ille:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quid admiramini?</HI>  inquit.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sciatis
ex nostra progenie</HI> <NOTE N="275" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> propagine A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">multos dominos nasci, set
unum semper dominari. Atqui</HI> <NOTE N="276" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> at 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">si domina vestra
non adeo de hac re</HI> <NOTE N="277" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> re  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">festinaret, set</HI> <NOTE N="278" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> si 7. p. m. t.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">per</HI> <NOTE N="279" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> per  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">modicum
tempus</HI> <NOTE N="280" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> dum  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">currentia fata expectaret, ut pro
me tam cito</HI> <NOTE N="281" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> numeret 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">non mitteret: quot natos heriles natura
proferret, tot dominos terra vestra haberet.</HI></P> <P COM="0067">7. Post haec indutus veste principali et calciatus
calciamento regali, acrem ascendit equum arator;
tamen suae sortis non inmemor, tollit secum suos
coturnos ex omni parte subere consutos, quos fecit
servari in posterum, et servantur Wissegrad <NOTE N="282" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> WISSEGRAR. A. Wisegrad 1, 4, 7.</NOTE>  in
camera ducis usque hodie et in sempiternum. Factum
 <COL N="0067D"></COL> est autem, dum per compendia <NOTE N="283" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> compita  <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine</HI>  2.</NOTE>  viarum
irent, nec tamen <NOTE N="284" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> tamen  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. nec non 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  adhuc illi nuncii ceu ad novitium
 <COL N="0068A"></COL> dominum familiarius <NOTE N="285" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> familiaris 7.</NOTE>  loqui auderent, set
sicut columbae, si quando aliqua peregrina ad eas
accedit, inprimis eam pavescunt, et mox in ipso
volatu eam assuefaciunt <NOTE N="286" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> asuefaciunt 1.</NOTE>  et <NOTE N="287" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> et e: tamquam A. 1. p. f.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine addita</HI>  A.</NOTE>  eam quasi propriam
faciunt et diligunt; sic illi cum fabularentur
equitantes et sermocinationibus iter adbreviarent,
ac jocando <NOTE N="288" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> jocundo
A.</NOTE>  per scurilia verba laborem fallerent,
unus, qui erat audacior et lingua promptior:  <HI REND="ITALIC">O domine,
dic,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nobis, ad quid hos coturnos subere
consutos et ad nichilum nisi</HI> <NOTE N="289" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> nisi  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut projiciantur</HI> <NOTE N="290" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> propiciantur 1.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">aptos nos servare fecisti, non satis possumus admirari.</HI> 
Quibus ille:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad hoc</HI> <NOTE N="291" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> haec. 1.</NOTE>  inquit  <HI REND="ITALIC">eos feci et faciam
in aevum servari, ut nostri posteri sciant, unde sint</HI> <NOTE N="292" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> st. A.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">orti, et ut semper vivant pavidi et suspecti, nec</HI> <NOTE N="293" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  ne 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  2, 4, neu 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">homines
a Deo sibi commissos</HI> <NOTE N="294" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> deditos A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">injuste opprimant per
 <COL N="0068B"></COL> superbiam, quia facti sumus omnes aequales per naturam.
Nunc autem et mihi liceat vos vicissim</HI> <NOTE N="295" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> vos vicissim  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2 vos invicem percunctari 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">percontari
utrum magis laudabile est, de paupertate ad
dignitatem provehi, an de dignitate in paupertatem
redigi? Nimirum respondebitis</HI> <NOTE N="296" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> respondetis 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mihi, melius esse
provehi ad gloriam, quam redigi ad inopiam. Atqui
sunt nonnulli parentela geniti ex nobili, set post ad
turpem inopiam redacti et miseri facti; cum suos parentes
gloriosos fuisse et potentes aliis praedicant,
haud ignorant, quod semetipsos inde plus confundunt
et deturpant, cum ipsi per suam hoc amiserunt ignaviam,
quod illi habuerunt per industriam. Nam fortuna
semper hanc ludit aleam sua rota, ut nunc hos
erigat ad summa, nunc illos mergat in</HI> <NOTE N="297" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> ad
A. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">infima.
Unde fit, ut dignitas terrena, quae erat aliquando ad
 <COL N="0068C"></COL> gloriam, amissa sit ad ignominiam. At vero paupertas
per virtutem victa, non se celat sub pelle lupina, set
victorem suum tollit ad sydera, quem olim secum traxerat
ad infera</HI> <NOTE N="298" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> infima 2. inferna 5.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0068">8. Postea vero quam <NOTE N="299" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> cum 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  iter emensi fuerant, et
jam jamque prope ad urbem venerant, obviam eis
domina stipata suis satellitibus accelerat, et inter
se consertis dextris cum magna laetitia tecta subeunt,
thoris discumbunt, Cerere et Bacho corpora
reficiunt, cetera noctis spatia Veneri <NOTE N="300" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> veri A.</NOTE>  et Himenaeo
 <NOTE N="301" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067"></COL> imineo 1.</NOTE>  indulgent. Hic vir, qui vere ex virtutis merito
dicendus est vir, hanc efferam gentem legibus
frenavit, et indomitum populum imperio domuit, et
servituti qua nunc premitur subjugavit, atque omnia
 <COL N="0068D"></COL> jura quibus haec terra utitur et regitur, solus
cum sola Lubossa dictavit <NOTE N="(268)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0067" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0067D"></COL> Eadem fabella in vetustissimis etiam legum Bohemicarum collectionibus reperitur.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0068"><COL N="0069A"></COL> 9. Inter haec primordia legum quadam die praedicta
domina, phitone concitata, praesente viro suo
Premizl et aliis senioribus populi <NOTE N="302" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> populis 1.</NOTE>  astantibus, sic
est vaticinata <NOTE N="303" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> vocitata 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :

 <POEM COM="0069"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Urbem conspicio fama quae sydera ianget,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Est locus in silva, villa</HI> <NOTE N="304" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> willa 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">qui</HI> <NOTE N="305" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> quae 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">distat ab ista</HI> <NOTE N="306" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> illa 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Terdenis stadiis, quem Wlitava</HI> <NOTE N="307" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. Wiltava 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .
Wiltava  <HI REND="ITALIC">rel.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">terminat undis.</HI></L></POEM> 

 <HI REND="ITALIC">Hunc</HI> <NOTE N="308" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> Hanc 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . Nunc. 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ex parte aquilonali</HI> <NOTE N="309" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> aquilonari 4, 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">valde munit</HI> <NOTE N="310" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> munitur 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">valle</HI> <NOTE N="311" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> valde 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">profunda rivulus Brusnica</HI> <NOTE N="312" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI> 
A. Bruzinca 2. Bruznice 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . Bruznica  <HI REND="ITALIC">rel.</HI></NOTE> ;  <HI REND="ITALIC">at australi ex latere
latus mons nimis petrosus, qui a petris dicitur Petrin</HI> 
 <NOTE N="313" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> Paetrin 1. Petrin 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , 5. Petrun 7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(269)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069D"></COL> Hodie mons S. Laurentii; Dobner ad Hajec.
II, 119.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">supereminet loca. Loci autem mons curvatur
in modum delphini marini porci, tendens usque
in</HI> <NOTE N="314" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> ad A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">praedictum amnem. Ad quem cum</HI> <NOTE N="315" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> dum 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">perveneritis,
invenietis hominem in media</HI> <NOTE N="316" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> medii 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">silva limen
domus operantem. Et quia ad humile limen etiam
 <COL N="0069B"></COL> magni domini se inclinant, ex eventu rei</HI> <NOTE N="317" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> regi  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  rei A. 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">urbem
quam aedificabitis, vocabitis Pragam</HI> <NOTE N="(270)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069D"></COL> Limen enim Bohemice sonat  <HI REND="ITALIC">prag.</HI>  cfr. Palacky
I, 88. Vid. etiam Pelzelii commentatio Ueber
Ursprung und Namen der Stadt Prag. Neuere
Abhandlungen der königl. Böhmischen Gesellschaft
der Wissenschaften II, 112.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hac in
urbe olim in futurum binae</HI> <NOTE N="318" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> columne  <HI REND="ITALIC">additum delet</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aureae ascendent olivae,
quae cacumine suo usque ad septimum</HI> <NOTE N="319" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> sempiternum
A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">penetrabunt
coelum, et per totum mundum signis et miraculis coruscabunt.
Has in hostiis et muneribus colent et adorabunt
omnes tribus terrae Boemiae nationes reliquae.
Una ex his vocabitur</HI> <NOTE N="320" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> vocabitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. Wiceslaw  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  Woytiech  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit manus seculi XV in</HI>  1. Wechlava, latine  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserit</HI> 
3. Weceslava 3 <SUP>a</SUP> . Weczlava  <HI REND="ITALIC">corrigit D.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Major Gloria, altera</HI> <NOTE N="321" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> Tressivoya, latine  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserit</HI>  3. Tiessiwoya  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. D.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Exercitus
Consolatio</HI> <NOTE N="(271)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069D"></COL> Innuit SS. Wenseslavum et Adalbertum;
conf. de his etymologiis Dobnerum ad Hajec. III,
 <COL N="0070D"></COL> 413. IV, 206.</NOTE> . Plura locutura erat, si non
fugisset <NOTE N="322" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> fuisset
2, 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , 7.</NOTE>  spiritus pestilens et <NOTE N="323" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> sed 7.</NOTE>  prophetans a
plasmate Dei. Continuo itur in antiquam silvam, et
reperto dato signo in <NOTE N="324" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  praedicto loco urbem, totius
Boemiae dominam, aedificant <NOTE N="325" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> aedificavit 3, 7.</NOTE>  Pragam. Et quia
ea tempestate virgines hujus terrae sine jugo pubescentes,
veluti Amazones militaria arma affectantes
 <COL N="0069C"></COL> et sibi ductrices facientes, pari modo uti tirones <NOTE N="326" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> thyornes A.</NOTE> 
militabant, venationibus per silvas viriliter insistebant,
non eas viri, set ipsaemet <NOTE N="327" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> semet A.</NOTE>  sibi viros, quos
et quando voluerunt, accipiebant; et sicut gens
Scitica Plauci <NOTE N="328" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. 1,
2, 4, 7. Planci  <HI REND="ITALIC">alii.</HI></NOTE>  sive <NOTE N="329" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> seu  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  sive 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Picenatici, vir et femina
in habitu nullum discrimen habebant. Unde in tantum
 <COL N="0070A"></COL> feminea <NOTE N="330" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> femina  <HI REND="ITALIC">addito</HI>  rum 1.</NOTE>  excrevit <NOTE N="331" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> exercuit 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in marg. manu
antiqua</HI>  excrevit.</NOTE>  audacia, ut in quadam
rupe, non longe a praedicta urbe, oppidum <NOTE N="332" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> opidum A.</NOTE>  natura
loci firmum sibi construerent, cui a virginali vocabulo
inditum est nomen Divin <NOTE N="333" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> Devin 1, 7. Dewin 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(272)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0070" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0070D"></COL> Devin igitur Bohemice idem est quod apud
nostrates Magdeburg i. e. Parthenopolis. In Fuldensibus
Annalibus 864. haec leguntur:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Rasticen in
quadam civitate, quae lingua gentis illius Dewin, id
est puella, dicitur, obsedit.</HI></NOTE> . Quod videntes
juvenes, contra eas nimio zelo indignantes,
multo plures insimul conglobati non longius quam
unius buccinae <NOTE N="334" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> bucinae A. 1.</NOTE>  in altera <NOTE N="335" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> altâ  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  alta
1.</NOTE>  rupe inter arbusta
aedificant urbem, quam moderni nuncupant Wissegrad,
tunc autem ab <NOTE N="336" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> ab  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest in</HI>  7.</NOTE>  arbustis traxerat nomen
Hrasten <NOTE N="337" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> Huasten  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  Hrasten A. 5. Hurasten 1, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 7. Nurasten 3. Wrasten 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(273)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0070" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0070D"></COL> A Bohemico  <HI REND="ITALIC">Chrast.</HI>   <ED>DOBROW</ED> .</NOTE> . Et quia saepe virgines solertiores
ad decipiendos juvenes <NOTE N="338" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> virgines  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  juvenes 1.</NOTE>  fiebant <NOTE N="339" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> f. s. a. i.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine addita</HI>  A.</NOTE> , saepe autem
juvenes virginibus fortiores <NOTE N="340" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> ferociores 7.</NOTE>  existebant, modo
bellum, modo pax inter eos agebatur. Et dum interposita
pace potiuntur, placuit utrisque partibus ut
componerent <NOTE N="341" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> componeret 7.</NOTE>  cibis <NOTE N="342" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> et
cibis 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et potibus simbolum, et per
 <COL N="0070B"></COL> tres dies sine armis sollempnem insimul agerent ludum
in constituto loco. Quid plura? Non aliter juvenes
cum puellis ineunt convivia, ac si lupi rapaces
quaerentes edulia <NOTE N="343" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> edilia 2,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ab antiqua manu</HI>  u  <HI REND="ITALIC">appositum.</HI></NOTE> , ut <NOTE N="344" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">in 2, erasum.</HI></NOTE>  intrarent ovilia.
Primum diem epulis et nimiis potibus hylarem <NOTE N="345" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> hilarem  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
ducunt.</P> <P COM="0070">Dumque volunt sedare sitim, sitis altera crevit,</P> <P COM="0070">Laetitiamque suam juvenes vix noctis <NOTE N="346" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> noctu A. 1, 2, noctu  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  noctis 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , noctis 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ad horam <NOTE N="347" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> ad horam  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE> 
differunt:</P> <P COM="0070">Nox erat et coelo fulgebat luna sereno <NOTE N="(274)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0070" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0070D"></COL> Hor., Epod. 15, 1.</NOTE> ;</P> <P COM="0070">Inflans tunc lituum, dedit unus eis ita signum,
dicens:

 <POEM COM="0070"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Lusistis satis, edistis satis atque</HI> <NOTE N="348" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> satisque 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">bibistis;</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Surgite, vos rauco clamat Venus aurea sistro</HI> <NOTE N="349" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> sitro
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addito</HI>  s A.</NOTE> .</L></POEM> 

Moxque <NOTE N="350" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> M. s. r. p.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine addita</HI>  A.</NOTE>  singuli singulas rapuere puellas. Mane
 <COL N="0070C"></COL> autem facto, jam pacis inito pacto, sublatis Cerere et
Bacho ex earum oppido <NOTE N="351" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> opido 1.</NOTE> , muros Lemniaco vacuos
indulgent Vulcano. Et <NOTE N="352" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> et A 1, 2, 4.</NOTE>  ex illa tempestate, post
obitum principis Lubossae, sunt <NOTE N="353" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> erant 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  mulieres nostrates
virorum sub potestate. Sed <NOTE N="354" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0069" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0069"></COL> et 7.</NOTE>  quoniam omnibus

 <POEM COM="0070"><L><COL N="0071A"></COL> Ire quidem restat, Numa quo devenit <NOTE N="355" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> venit  <HI REND="ITALIC">addito al. manu</HI>  de A. venit 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, nimia quo venit 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , pervenit 7.</NOTE>  et Ancus
 <NOTE N="(275)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071C"></COL> Hor., Epp. I, 6, 27.</NOTE> ,</L></POEM> 

Premizl jam plenus dierum, postquam jura instituit
legum, quem coluit vivus <NOTE N="356" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3,
4, 7, invisum deum A. nimis 2, unus 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ut deum, raptus est ad
Cereris generum <NOTE N="(276)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071C"></COL> Juvenal., X, 112.</NOTE> . Cui Nezamizl <NOTE N="357" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Nezamil 1, Nezamysl 2.</NOTE>  successit
in regnum. Hunc ubi mors rapuit, Mnata principales
obtinuit fasces. Quo decedente ab hac <NOTE N="358" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> hac  <HI REND="ITALIC">restituit alia manus</HI>  1.</NOTE>  vita, Vogen
 <NOTE N="359" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Voyn 1, 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , 3, 5, 7, Vogin 2, Moyen 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Voin 7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  suscepit rerum gubernacula. Hujus post fatum
Unezlau <NOTE N="360" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Unizlu 1, Winzlau 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Vitozlau 4,
4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Unizlau 5, 7.</NOTE>  rexit ducatum. Cujus vitam dum
rumpunt Parcae, Crezomisl <NOTE N="361" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Crezomizl 1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 7, Crezomysl 2, Kresomizl 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Creczomiczl 7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  locatur sedis in
arce <NOTE N="362" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> s.
i. a. l. A.</NOTE> . Hoc sublato e <NOTE N="363" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> in 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  medio, Neclan <NOTE N="364" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Neklan 2.</NOTE>  ducatus
potitur solio. Hic ubi vita <NOTE N="365" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> vira 1.</NOTE>  decessit <NOTE N="366" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> discessit  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  decessit A. discessit 1.</NOTE> , Gostivit <NOTE N="367" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Hostivit
2, Goztivit 4.</NOTE> 
throno successit. Horum igitur principum de vita <NOTE N="368" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> de vita  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE> 
aeque <NOTE N="369" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> aeque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , 7.</NOTE>  et morte siletur, tum <NOTE N="370" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> tuum 1.</NOTE>  quia ventri <NOTE N="371" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Veneri 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et
somno dediti, inculti et indocti assimilati sunt peccori,
 <COL N="0071B"></COL> quibus profecto contra naturam corpus voluptati,
anima fuit oneri <NOTE N="(277)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071C"></COL> Sallust., Catil., c. 2.</NOTE> ; tum quia non erat illo
in tempore, qui stilo acta eorum commendaret <NOTE N="372" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
memoriae. Set sileamus de quibus siletur, et redeamus
unde paulo deviavimus <NOTE N="373" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> paulo digressi sumus 4, 4 <SUP>d</SUP> .</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0071">10. Gostivit autem genuit Borwoy <NOTE N="374" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. Borivoy 1, 3, 7, Borziwoy 2, Boriwoy 4.</NOTE> , qui primus
dux baptizatus est <NOTE N="375" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> e. b. A.</NOTE>  a venerabili Metudio <NOTE N="376" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Methodio 3, Methudio 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  episcopo
in Moravia, sub temporibus Arnolfi <NOTE N="377" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Arnulfi 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  imperatoris,
et Zuatopluk <NOTE N="378" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Zuatoplik 1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 7, Zwatoplk 2, Zvatopluc 4.</NOTE>  ejusdem Moraviae regis <NOTE N="(278)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071C"></COL> In chronologia constituenda erravit; obiit
Methodius die 6 m. April. 885, Arnulfus regnum
adeptus est a. 887, et Zuatopluk Marahensium dux
mortuus est a. 894, testibus Fuldens. Annalibus.
Eorumdem auctoritate, qua confirmatur Bohemorum
ducis filiam a Marahensibus in matrimonium ductam
esse a. 871, haud inmerito rerum Bohemicarum
scriptoribus effici videbatur Borwoy ducem eodem
fere tempore baptizatum esse; etsi aliter videbatur
Dobnero III, 252. Cf. Dobrowski libellum Versuche
die alteste Böhmische Gesch., etc., p. 49.</NOTE> .
Nec superfluum esse judicavimus <NOTE N="379" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> judicamus A. 7.</NOTE> , quod referente
fama audivimus, huic operi nostro hoc in loco summatim
literarum apicibus inserere bellum, quodque
 <NOTE N="380" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> quidem 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  olim antea retro dierum, tempore ducis
 <COL N="0072A"></COL> Neclan <NOTE N="381" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Neclam 7.</NOTE>  in campo qui <NOTE N="382" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> quod 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  dicitur Turzco <NOTE N="383" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Turzko 1, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Jurzko 7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(279)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071C"></COL> Haud procul a Praga urbe septentrionem
versus Dobner ad Hajecium II, 68, hunc locum sibi
reperisse visus est.</NOTE> 
consertum est inter Boemos et Luczanos <NOTE N="384" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Lutzanos
7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(280)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071C"></COL> Ex Cosmae opinione Luczani igitur non
erant Bohemi.</NOTE> ,
qui nunc a modernis ab urbe Satec <NOTE N="385" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. Satc 1,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ita deinceps</HI>  Sate 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Satz 3, Sathec 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Satx 7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(281)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0072" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0072C"></COL> Saaz urbs ad Egram in circulo Saazensi.</NOTE>  vocitantur
Satcenses <NOTE N="386" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Satcenses 3, 7,
Sathcenses 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Unde autem antiquitus <NOTE N="387" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> antiquius A.</NOTE>  nuncupetur
 <NOTE N="388" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> nuncupentur 7.</NOTE>  ea <NOTE N="389" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> hec A.</NOTE>  natio Luczano, nolumus praeterire
 <NOTE N="390" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> volumus praeteriri 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  sub silentio. Quippe illa distinguitur provincia
quinque regionibus locorum per compendia.
Prima regio est sita circa rivum nomine <NOTE N="391" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
A.</NOTE>  Gutna <NOTE N="392" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. Buntua 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , Guntna  <HI REND="ITALIC">rel.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(282)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0072" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0072C"></COL> Vix certi aliquid de his regionibus et fluviis
afferri posse videtur; cf. tamen Dobner ad Hajecium
III, 78. Gutna vel Gunta fluviolum Dobner in praecepto
quodam Joannis regis a. 1332 dato deprehendit.</NOTE> .
Secunda ex utraque parte est fluvii Uzka <NOTE N="393" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Uzkca 1, Utkca 3, 7, Uzca 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Uztka 5.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(283)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0072" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0072C"></COL> Si Dobnerum audis est Saa rivus qui paulo
infra Satec in Egram exundat.</NOTE> .
Tercia extenditur per circuitum torrentis
Bocnica <NOTE N="394" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Broczinka 2,
Brocnisa 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Briznica 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Brocnice 5.</NOTE> . Quarta, quae et silvana dicitur, sita est
infra terminos fluminis Msa <NOTE N="395" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Mzie 2.</NOTE> . Quinta <NOTE N="396" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> quincta 1.</NOTE> , quae in
medio est, dicitur <NOTE N="397" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Luka <NOTE N="398" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Luca 1,
2, 4.</NOTE> : pulcherrima visu et
utillima <NOTE N="399" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> utilissima 3, ultima 7.</NOTE>  usu ac uberrima satis, nec non habundantissima
pratis, unde et nomen ipsa regio traxit,
 <COL N="0072B"></COL> quia luca latine pratum dicitur <NOTE N="(284)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0072" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0072C"></COL> Wlaztizlavi terram in Sacensi, Raconicensi
et Lutomericensi circulis quaerendam esse conjicit
Palacky.</NOTE> . Et quoniam <NOTE N="400" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> quando 7.</NOTE> 
haec regio primum, longe antequam Satec <NOTE N="401" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Satech 4 <SUP>a</SUP> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">reliqui ut supra.</HI></NOTE>  urbs
condita foret, est inhabitata hominibus, recte ejus
incolae sunt a <NOTE N="402" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> a  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7.</NOTE>  regione Luczane <NOTE N="403" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> L. a.
r. A. 2, Luczene 1.</NOTE>  nuncupati <NOTE N="404" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> nuncupatae 1, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , 7, nuncii patere 2.</NOTE> .
His praefuit dux nomine Wlaztizlav <NOTE N="405" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> Wlaztizlau 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Wratizlav 3, 7,
Wlatizlaus 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , vir bellicosus
et in bellicis armis animosus <NOTE N="406" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> et in—animosus  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt in</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , imbecillis armis animosus 7.</NOTE> , ac <NOTE N="407" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> hac 1.</NOTE>  consiliis
supra modum dolosus, satisque in praeliis felix potuisset
dici, si sors suprema non clausisset eum fine
infelici. Nam contra Boemos frequenter susceperat
bellum, et semper Marte secundo atque diis auspicibus
praevaluerat, terramque eorum saepe ingressus
cedibus, incendiis ac rapinis crudeliter devastarat
 <NOTE N="408" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0071" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0071"></COL> devastaverat
7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(285)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0072" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0072C"></COL> Haud superfluum videtur hoc loco apponere
quosdam versus ex carmine populari, in codice reginae
aulae reperto, quo idem praelium Wlaslawi et
Cestmiri (qui Cosmae est Tiro) lingua Bohemica describitur;
nonnulli enim versus cum verbis auctoris
nostri nescio quomodo concinere videntur. In laudandis
versibus secutus sum librum: Königinhofer
Handschrift aufgefunden und herausgegeben von W.
Hanka, verdeutscht von Swoboda. Prag. 1829. Cum
 <COL N="0073C"></COL> hoc loco hi conferendi sunt versus p. 91:

 <POEM COM="0073"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Brach</HI>  (scil. Wlaslaw)  <HI REND="ITALIC">mit Feuer und mit Schwert</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Oft herein in Neklans Land.</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> , et ipsos populi primates in tantum
 <COL N="0073A"></COL> praesidiis attenuaverat <NOTE N="409" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> attenuerat  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. eadem manu</HI>  attenuaverat 1, atenuarat 2, 7.</NOTE> , ut parvo clausi in oppido,
quod dicitur Levigradec <NOTE N="410" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> Levigradek 2.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(286)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073C"></COL> Lewy Hradek castrum in sinistra ripa Moldavae
fluvii, haud procul a Praga urbe. Cfr. Dobrowski
Versuche p. 95.</NOTE> , hostium incursiones
timerent oppido. Hic condidit urbem, quam appellavit
nomine suo Wlaztizlav <NOTE N="411" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> Wlastislaw 2,
Wlatizlau 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 5,  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserto tamen</HI>  s  <HI REND="ITALIC">ante</HI>  t 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Wlatzizlau 3, 7.</NOTE> , inter duos montes
Meduez <NOTE N="412" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> Meduiz 1. Meduel 2.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(287)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073C"></COL> Hodie Netluk in circulo Lutomericensi;
cfr. Schaller Topographie des Königreichs Bohmen
 <COL N="0074C"></COL> 86.</NOTE>  et Pripek <NOTE N="413" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> Przipek
2, Pripec 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(288)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0074" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0074C"></COL> Hodie Prisen; cf. ibid.</NOTE> , scilicet in confinio
 <NOTE N="414" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. 1, rubro atramento.</HI></NOTE>  duarum provinciarum Belina <NOTE N="(289)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0074" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0074C"></COL> Bilin ad Bilam in circulo Lutomericensi.</NOTE>  et <NOTE N="415" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
Lutomerici <NOTE N="416" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> Luthomirici 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(290)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0074" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0074C"></COL> Leitmeritz.</NOTE> , et posuit in ea viros <NOTE N="417" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> muros  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.
alia manu</HI>  viros 1.</NOTE>  iniquos,
ob insidias utriusque populi, quia hii adjuvabant
partes Boemorum. Et sicut in omni vicissitudine
rerum prosperitas elevat, adversitas humiliat
cor hominum, ex nimia quam semper obtinuit in
praeliis prosperitate <NOTE N="418" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> prosperitatem 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , exaltatum est cor ducis et
elevatum, ut mente feroci exardesceret omnem Boemiam
ad obtinendum. Ah <NOTE N="419" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> Ah! ah! 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ! mens hominum ignara
futurorum saepe suo fallitur augurio, saepe fit, quod
 <COL N="0073B"></COL> ante ruinam <NOTE N="420" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. 1, minio.</HI></NOTE>  cor extollitur <NOTE N="421" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> exaltatur 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , sicut ante letitiam
saepe humiliatur. Mox tumido inflatus fastu <NOTE N="422" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> fatu 4.</NOTE>  superbiae,
scire volens virtus sua quantae sit potentiae,
mittit gladium per omnes fines tocius provinciae, hac
conditione <NOTE N="423" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> convincie 1.</NOTE>  principalis sentenciae, ut quicunque <NOTE N="424" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> qui 7.</NOTE> 
corporis statura praecellens gladii mensuram segnius
jusso <NOTE N="425" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> jussu 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  egrederetur ad pugnam, procul dubio puniretur
gladio. Quos <NOTE N="426" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> quo 1.</NOTE>  cicius <NOTE N="427" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> totius 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  dicto ut vidit <NOTE N="428" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> ut vidit  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia
manu</HI>  A.</NOTE> 
in condicto coadunatos <NOTE N="429" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  1.</NOTE>  loco, stans in medio aggere,
corona vulgi septus, clippeo <NOTE N="430" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> quae  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  subnixus,
manu <NOTE N="431" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> mano 1.</NOTE>  ensem vibrans, sic est exorsus:  <HI REND="ITALIC">O milites,
quibus ultima in manibus est victoria</HI> <NOTE N="432" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> v. i. m. e. A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">olim non
semel vicistis, jam actum agitis. Quid opus est armis?
Arma ad</HI> <NOTE N="433" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> et 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">speciem militiae portare faciatis. Quin potius
falcones</HI> <NOTE N="434" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nisos, herodios et omne</HI> <NOTE N="435" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> omnis 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hujusmodi genus
 <COL N="0073C"></COL> volatilium, quod magis aptum est ad jocunditatem et
ludum, tellite vobiscum, quibus carnes</HI> <NOTE N="436" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> canes  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  carnes A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">inimicorum,
si forte sufficient, dabimus</HI> <NOTE N="437" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> dapibus 1. 7.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ad vescendum. Teste
Marte deo et mea domina Bellona, quae mihi fecit omnia
bona, per capulum ensis mei juro quem manu teneo,
quod pro infantibus eorum catulos canum ponam
ad ubera matrum. Levate signa, tollite moras;
semper nocuit differre paratis</HI> <NOTE N="(291)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0074" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0074C"></COL> Lucan., Phars. I, 281.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ite jam velociter
 <COL N="0074A"></COL> et vincite feliciter.</HI>  Exoritur clamer ad aethera <NOTE N="438" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> hethera 1.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(292)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0074" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0074C"></COL> Virg., Aen. II, 313, 338.</NOTE> 
utilis et inutilis <NOTE N="439" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  1.</NOTE> , fortis et vilis <NOTE N="440" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> f. et v.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1.</NOTE> , potens et inpotens,
perstrepunt arma <NOTE N="441" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> arma  <HI REND="ITALIC">repetunt</HI>  1. 3. 7.</NOTE> , saltat scabiosa <NOTE N="442" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> scabio 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  equa,
ut acer equus <NOTE N="443" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> u  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit alia manus</HI>  A.</NOTE>  in pugna.</P> <P COM="0074">11. Interea quaedam mulier, una de numero
Eumenidum, vocans ad se privinum <NOTE N="444" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et corr.</HI>  2.</NOTE> , qui jam iturus
erat ad praelium.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quamvis,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non est naturale
novercis, ut benefaciant suis privignis, tamen non
immemor consortii tui patris, cautum te faciam, quo</HI> 
 <NOTE N="445" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> ut 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">possis vivere si vis. Scias Boemorum strigas sive</HI> 
 <NOTE N="446" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> sine 1. sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">lemures nostras praevaluisse votis Eumenides, unde
nostris usque ad unum interfectis, dabitur Boemiis
victoria</HI> <NOTE N="447" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> v. B. A.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0074"><HI REND="ITALIC">Hanc tu, quo tandem valeas evadere cladem,
quem in primo congressu interficies</HI> <NOTE N="448" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tibi adversantem,
 <COL N="0074B"></COL> utramque sibi abscidens</HI> <NOTE N="449" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> abscindens 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aurem, mitte in tuam
bursam, et inter utrosque pedes equi in modum crucis
evaginato ense terram lineabis. Hoc enim faciens invisibiles
ligaturas laxabis, quibus ira deorum vestri
equi obligati</HI> <NOTE N="450" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> invisibiles—obligati  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">deficient</HI> <NOTE N="451" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> invicient 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et cadent</HI> <NOTE N="452" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> c. et d. A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quasi ex
longo itinere fatigati, moxque</HI> <NOTE N="453" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> que  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">insiliens equum,
terga vertes</HI> <NOTE N="454" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> vertens  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI> 
vertes 1.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et si magnus post te fragor</HI> <NOTE N="455" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> magnus terror ingruerit A. m. p. t. vel fragor vel timor 1. timor vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa in</HI>  2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . m. p.
t. timor vel fragor 3. 4. 7. ut fragor 5.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ingruerit,
nunquam retro aspicias, fugam sed acceleres,
atque ita tu solus vix</HI> <NOTE N="456" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> vix  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">effugies. Nam qui dii vobiscum</HI> 
 <NOTE N="457" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> nobiscum 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">comitabantur</HI> <NOTE N="458" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> comitantur 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in praelium, versi sunt in
auxilium inimicis vestris</HI> <NOTE N="459" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> nostris
7.</NOTE> . A contra Boemis resistere
non valentibus, hostibus quippe jam tociens
triumphantibus <NOTE N="460" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> trihuphantibus 1.</NOTE> , una
Salus <NOTE N="461" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> soli  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu superscr.</HI>  salus 1.</NOTE>  erat victis nullam sperare salutem <NOTE N="(293)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0074" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0074C"></COL> Virg., Aen. II, 354.</NOTE> .
Sed sicut semper infideles homines, et eo ad malum
 <COL N="0074C"></COL> proniores <NOTE N="462" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> promciores  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  1.</NOTE> , ubi deficiunt vires et bonae artes, ilico
ad deteriores pravitatis vertuntur partes: haud <NOTE N="463" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> aut
 <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  haud A.</NOTE> 
aliter gens ista vanis <NOTE N="464" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> vallis 1.</NOTE>  sacris dedita, plus mendaciis
credula, jam desperantes viribus et armis militaribus,
quandam adeunt sortilegam et consulunt
eam atque instant ut edicat <NOTE N="465" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0073" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0073"></COL> et d. 1.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0074">Quid opus sit facto in tali discrimine rerum,</P> <P COM="0074">Aut quos eventus futurum obtineat bellum.
 <COL N="0075A"></COL> Illa, ut erat plena Phitone, ambigua <NOTE N="466" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> ambiguitate  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa voce</HI>  ambage 7.</NOTE>  non tenuit
eos diu verborum ambage:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si vultis,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">triumphum
victoriae consequi, oportet vos prius</HI> <NOTE N="467" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> prius  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jussa
Deorum exsequi. Ergo litate</HI> <NOTE N="468" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> libate 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">diis vestris asinum,
ut sint et ipsi vobis in asylum. Hoc votum fieri summus
Jupiter, et ipse Mars sororque ejus Bellona,
atque gener Cereris jubet.</HI>  Queritur interim miser
asellus et <NOTE N="469" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  occiditur, et, ut jussum fuerat, in
mille millies frusta conciditur, atque ab universo
exercitu cicius dicto consumitur <NOTE N="470" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> . Quibus ita esu
animatis asinino <NOTE N="471" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> asineo 7.</NOTE> —res similis prodigio—cerneres
laetas phalanges et viros mori promptos ut silvaticos
porcos; et sicut post <NOTE N="472" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> per 7.</NOTE>  aquosam nubem fit sol
clarior et visu jocundior, ita post nimiam inerciam
exercitus ille fuit alacrior et ad pugnam audatior.</P> <P COM="0075"><COL N="0075B"></COL> 12. Interea dux eorum Neclan <NOTE N="473" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> Niclan 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , tepore pavidior
et pardo <NOTE N="474" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  A. partho  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. m.
superscr.</HI>  pardo 1.</NOTE>  fuga velocior, pugnam inminentem pertimuit,
et ficta infirmitate in castro supradicto
delituit. Quid facerent membra sine capite, aut milites
in praelio sine duce? Erat ea tempestate quidam
vir praecipuus honestate corporis, aetate et nomine
Tyro, et ipse post ducem secundus inperio <NOTE N="475" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> i. s. A.</NOTE> , qui
ad occursum mille obpugnantium in praelio nullum
timere, nemini scivit cedere. Hunc dux clam ad se
vocat et praecipit ut arma sua induat, et paucis clientibus
id scientibus <NOTE N="476" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> id scientibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , herilem equum jubet ut ascendat,
atque vice sui <NOTE N="477" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> sua A.</NOTE>  milites ad pugnam praecedat,
quae non longe ab urbe, sed quasi duobus
stadiis distabat. Ventum erat ad campum ab utrisque
 <COL N="0075C"></COL> exercitibus condictum; sed prius Boemi praeoccupant
collem in medio campo eminentem, unde et
hostes praeviderent adventantes <NOTE N="(294)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075C"></COL> In carmine populari, p. 103:

 <POEM COM="0075"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Dort in weiter Flache harret ihrer</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Kriegesfreudig Wlaslaw.</HI></L></POEM> 

Et paulo infra verba Cestmiri:

 <POEM COM="0075"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Hier vom Berge kann uns Wlaslaw sehen;</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Rasch hinab rings um den Berg gezogen.</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> , et is qui <NOTE N="478" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> his  <HI REND="ITALIC">omisso</HI> 
qui 7.</NOTE> 
aestimabatur <NOTE N="479" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  dux, stans in eminentiori loco,
concionaretur <NOTE N="480" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> concionatur  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  concionaretur A.</NOTE>  ad milites Tyro:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si fas,</HI>  inquit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">esset duci verbis addere virtutem militibus</HI> <NOTE N="(295)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075C"></COL> Sallust., Cat. 58.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">multiplicibus
vos tenerem sermonum</HI> <NOTE N="481" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> sermone 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . verborum
7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ambagibus. Sed
quia hostis ad oculum stat, et breve tempus ad exortandum</HI> 
 <NOTE N="482" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> ad exhort.  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa</HI>  7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">extat</HI></P> <P COM="0075"><HI REND="ITALIC">Fas mihi sit vos vel paucis succendere dictis.
Omnibus in bello dimicandi par est devotio, sed impar
vincendi ratio</HI> <NOTE N="483" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> conditio vel ratio  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt 1. 3. 7. In 2. 5. supra vocem</HI>  conditio
 <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manus antiqua adscripsit</HI>  vel ratio. conditio A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et rel.</HI></NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Illi paucorum pugnant pro
 <COL N="0076A"></COL> gloria, nos pro patria dimicamus et populi atque
nostra libertate</HI> <NOTE N="(296)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0076" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0076C"></COL> Sallust., ibid.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et salute ultima; illi ut rapiant
aliena, nos ut defendamus dulcia pignera et cara
connubia. Confortamini</HI> <NOTE N="484" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> et nolite  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  1.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et estote viri. Nam deos
vestros quos actenus habuistis offensos, placastis votis
quibus placari voluerunt. Ergo timorem eorum ne
timueritis, quia</HI> <NOTE N="485" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> quia  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quibus in praelio</HI> <NOTE N="486" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> t. i. pr. A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">timor</HI> <NOTE N="487" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> timor  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">officit</HI> 
 <NOTE N="488" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> efficit. 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">animo, maximo</HI> <NOTE N="489" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> mox uno A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">versantur in periculo;
audatia autem habetur pro muro</HI> <NOTE N="(297)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0076" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0076C"></COL> Sallust., ibid.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">audacibus et
ipsi dii</HI> <NOTE N="490" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">auxiliantur. Credite mihi, ultra illa castra
vestra</HI> <NOTE N="491" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> vestra  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">salus posita est et gloria. At si terga hostibus
vertitis, mortem tamen non effugietis. Set utinam
mortem! verum pejus morte agetur; conjuges vestras
in conspectu vestro violabunt, et in sinu earum infantes
ferro trucidabunt, et ad lactandum eis catulos dabunt,
 <COL N="0076B"></COL> quia victis una est virtus, victoribus nil denegare.</HI> 
Interea dux Lucensis, ferocissimus mente, cum superbissima
gente, quibus et hodie a malo innatum est
superbire <NOTE N="492" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  1.</NOTE> , veniens ex adverso, ut vidit hostes non
cedere loco, jubet suos paulisper stare illico, et
quasi condolens super fata <NOTE N="493" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  inimicorum, his dictis
acuit animos suorum <NOTE N="494" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> eorum 7.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">O miserabiles</HI> <NOTE N="495" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> mirabiles 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">timidorum
hominum manes, frustra prendunt</HI> <NOTE N="496" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> pendunt 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">colles,
quibus desunt vires et bellicae artes, nec juvat collis,
si est virtus debilis. Cernitis, quia in planis vobis non
audent occurrere</HI> <NOTE N="497" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> occurre 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">campis, nimirum si non fallor,
jam fugere parant. Sed vos, priusquam fugiant</HI> <NOTE N="498" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">irruite super eos inpetu repentino, et sub pedibus vestris
ceu frivola stipularum ut conterantur, faciae
more solito. Parcite ne ignavorum sanguine polluatis
 <COL N="0076C"></COL> fortia tela, sed pocius submittite</HI> <NOTE N="499" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> submittite  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">quae portatis
volatilia, ut</HI> <NOTE N="500" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> in 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">perterrefaciatis</HI> <NOTE N="501" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> perire faciatis A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">falconibus pavidas
acies ut columbas.</HI>  Quod ut factum est, tanta fuit
densitas diversarum <NOTE N="502" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  avium, ut sub pennis earum
obscuraretur aer velut sub aquosa nube, vel nigrae
tempestatis tempore. Hoc cernens intrepidus Tyro,
coeptum interrumpens colloquium ad suos dixit <NOTE N="503" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> d. a. s. A.</NOTE> :
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Si forte contigerit me mori in praelio, sepelite me in
hoc colliculo, et construite mausoleum mihi</HI> <NOTE N="504" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> mihi  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in
secula</HI> <NOTE N="505" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> i. s. nominativum A. vel memoriale nominativum 1. n. vel m. 2. 3. 7. vel mem.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">manu recentiori adscripta in</HI>  5. nominatum 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">memoriale.</HI>  Unde et hodie nominatur militis
acerrimi bustum Tyri <NOTE N="(298)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0076" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0076C"></COL> Ostenditur in hunc diem crudi et abrupti
saxi moles super sterilibus campis ad Tursko, quae
in busti hujus memoriam huc advoluta dicitur, quam
et ipse spectavi oculis. DOBNER ad Hai. III, 108.</NOTE> . Moxque prosiliens
ceu maxima moles rupis, quae <NOTE N="506" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> rupisque 1.</NOTE>  fulmine <NOTE N="507" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0075" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0075"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  1.</NOTE>  rupta
 <COL N="0077A"></COL> de summitate alti montis fertur per abrupta loca,
sternens omnia obstacula, haud aliter ruit fortissimus
 <COL N="0078A"></COL> heros <NOTE N="508" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> eres  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu</HI>  heros 1.</NOTE>  Tyro in confertissimos hostium cuneos <NOTE N="(299)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077C"></COL> In carmine populari, p. 105.

 <POEM COM="0077"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Tras bricht mit hervor aus Waldesschatten,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Tras erfasst des Feinds zahllose Haufen.</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> .

 <POEM COM="0078"><L><COL N="0077A"></COL> Ac veluti, si quis in horto <NOTE N="509" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> orto 4.</NOTE>  tenera papavera succideret ferro,</L> <L>ita obstantium metit ense capita hostium;</L> <L>donec plenus astilibus, quasi herinatius,</L> <L>in media strage super magnam struem <NOTE N="510" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  A. stragem A. strugem 1.</NOTE>  occisorum cecidit.</L> <L>Incertum est, quis, a quo, vel quali vulnere quisque</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0077A"></COL> ceciderit, nisi hoc solum scimus pro certo, quia <NOTE N="511" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> quod
2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
Boemi potiti sunt <NOTE N="512" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu</HI>  A.</NOTE>  triumpho, Lucensibus <NOTE N="513" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> Luccensibus 2. Luczensibus 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  omnibus
 <NOTE N="514" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> hominibus 1.</NOTE>  interfectis usque ad unum <NOTE N="515" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> hunum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  unum 1.</NOTE> , praeter illum
videlicet quem noverca olim praemonuerat euntem
ad praelium. Isque dum jussa peregit novercae praepeti
 <NOTE N="516" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> praeceti  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  prae ceteris 1.</NOTE>  elapsus fuga, dumque <NOTE N="517" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deletum</HI>  que A.</NOTE>  concitus venerit ad
domum, ecce uxor sua plangebatur defuncta. Quam
ut videret vir suus, dum discooperuisset faciem ejus
 <COL N="0077B"></COL> —res similes fictae—visum est funus habere in femineo
pectore vulnus et abscisas <NOTE N="518" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> abscissas 2.
2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3. 7.</NOTE>  aures. Tunc
vir <NOTE N="519" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>  recolens quod factum fuerat <NOTE N="520" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> erat 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  in praelio,
protulit aures de bursa cruentis <NOTE N="521" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> cruentas 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  cum inauribus,
atque recognovit hanc fuisse in specie illius <NOTE N="522" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> ejus 1.</NOTE>  quem
adversantem occidit in bello.</P> <P COM="0077">13. Post haec intrantes Boemi in terram illam <NOTE N="523" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> B. intr. t. i. A. 4.
B. t. i. intr.  <HI REND="ITALIC">relig.</HI></NOTE> 
et nullo resistente devastantes eam <NOTE N="524" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>  civitates destruxerunt,
villas combusserunt, spolia multa acceperunt
 <NOTE N="(300)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077C"></COL> In carmine populari, p. 107:

 <POEM COM="0077"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Und die reiche Beute</HI></L> <L><COL N="0078C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Blinkt vor Neklaus freudehellem Auge.</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> . Inter quae filium <NOTE N="525" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE>  herilem apud
quandam vetulam mulierem inveniunt latitantem.
Quem dux ut <NOTE N="526" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0077" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0077"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  vidit, quamvis paganus, tamen ut
catholicus bonus, misericordia super eum motus
