et omni plebe prae laeticia modulante <NOTE N="843" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0091" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0091"></COL> kyrieleyson  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE> , episcopalem
obsedit kathedram. Hujus tam praeclari pastoris
Adalberti consilio et praedictae atque dilectae suae
sororis abbatissae Mariae <NOTE N="844" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0091" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0091"></COL> Mariae ab. A.</NOTE>  interventu dux Bolezlaus,
quicquid praesul Pragensis usque hodie in suo possidet
vel obtinet episcopio, vel quicquid abbatissa optavit
 <COL N="0093A"></COL> dari et fieri utilitatis in suo coenobio, gratuita utrique
 <NOTE N="845" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> utrisque A.</NOTE>  concessit pietate et canonum sacra confirmavit
auctoritate <NOTE N="846" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Reliqua usque ad annum 994 desunt in</HI>  7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> .</P> <LIST COM="0093"><ITEM>27. Anno dominicae incarnationis 970.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 971.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 972 sanctus Oudalricus
migravit a seculo <NOTE N="847" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec verba desunt</HI>  A. 2 <SUP>a</SUP> . 5.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(340)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Obiit die 4 mens. Julii 973. Cfr. Gerhardi
Vita S. Udalrici, c. 27, Mon. Germ SS. IV, p. 414.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 973.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 974.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 975.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 976.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 977 <NOTE N="848" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae sequuntur, ad priorem annum leguntur in Frehero.</HI></NOTE>  obiit Dubrauca,
quae, quia nimis improba fuit, jam mulier
provectae aetatis cum nupsisset Poloniensi duci <NOTE N="(341)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Miseconi; conf. quae apud Thietmarum IV,
35, 36. de Dubrauca illa, filia Bolezlavi I, ducis Bohemorum,
leguntur, et Roepell, Geschichte von Polen
I, 622.</NOTE> ,
peplum capitis sui deposuit, et puellarem coronam
 <COL N="0093B"></COL> sibi imposuit: quod erat magna dementia mulieris.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 978.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 979.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 980.</ITEM></LIST> <P COM="0093">Anno dominicae incarnationis 981 obiit Slavnic <NOTE N="849" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Zlaunik 1. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Slawnik 2. Zlaunik dux 4.</NOTE> ,
pater sancti Adalberti <NOTE N="850" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> XV Kal. Apr.  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE> , cujus de moribus et vita
licet plurima eniteant memoriae <NOTE N="851" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> memoria 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  digna, ex quibus
tamen ut referamus <NOTE N="852" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> refferamus 1.</NOTE>  pauca, coepta intermittimus
nostra. Erat enim <NOTE N="853" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  vir laetissimus ad
omnes facie, in consiliis serenissimus mente <NOTE N="854" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> vitae 3.</NOTE> ,
alloquiis blandissimus <NOTE N="855" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> a. b.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI> 
5.</NOTE> , locuples diviciis quam
secularibus tam spiritualibus. In domo <NOTE N="856" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> in domo—defensio  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>  illius honestas
 <NOTE N="857" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> honesta 4.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et corrector</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  fulgebat et sincera dilectio, judiciorum
rectitudo et procerum multitudo <NOTE N="858" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  1.</NOTE> . In operibus
ejus erat legum cognitio, pauperum refectio, moerentium
 <COL N="0093C"></COL> consolatio, peregrinorum receptio, viduarum
et orphanorum <NOTE N="859" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> et orph.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4.</NOTE>  defensio <NOTE N="(342)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Conf. Vita S. Adalberti c. . .</NOTE> . Hujus <NOTE N="860" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> hius 1.</NOTE>  tam
insignis ducis metropolis fuit Lubio <NOTE N="(343)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Libicz in circulo Bidschowensi, cfr. Schaller
XVI, 21.</NOTE> , sita loco
 <COL N="0094A"></COL> ubi amnis Cydlina <NOTE N="861" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Cidlina 1. 3. Cidlinia 2. Cydlina 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(344)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Czidlina fluvius qui prope Libicz in Albim
cadit. Ibid.</NOTE>  nomen perdit suum, intrans
liberioris aquae <NOTE N="862" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> atque 1.</NOTE>  in fluvium Labe. Habuit
autem sui principatus hos <NOTE N="863" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> os  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  hos 1.</NOTE>  terminos. Ad occidentalem
plagam contra Boemiam rivulum Surina
 <NOTE N="864" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Sirina  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1. Surma 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(345)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Bila qui prope Aussig in Albim exundat.
Ibid, V, 14.</NOTE>  et castrum quod est situm in monte
Oseca <NOTE N="865" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Ossieka 2.</NOTE>  juxta flumen Msam <NOTE N="866" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Mzie 2.</NOTE> . Similiter plagam
ad australem contra Teutonicos orientales has urbes
habuit terminales: Hinov <NOTE N="867" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Chinov. 1. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4. Hinou 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(346)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Cheynow.</NOTE> , Dudlebi
 <NOTE N="(347)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093D"></COL> Daudleb.</NOTE> , Netolici <NOTE N="868" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Netholici
1. Notoliczi 2. Notholici 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">prius, sed correctum</HI>  Netholici  <HI REND="ITALIC">et deleto ultimo</HI>  i  <HI REND="ITALIC">supra scriptum</HI>  e. Netholici 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(348)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Netolitz.</NOTE>  usque ad mediam silvam.
Item solis ad ortum contra Moraviae regnum castrum
sub silva situm, nomine Luthomisl <NOTE N="869" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Lutomisl 1. 4. Liutomysl 2. Lutomizl 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Lutomis vel,  <HI REND="ITALIC">omisso</HI>  nomine 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(349)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Leutomischl.</NOTE> , usque
ad rivulum Svitawa <NOTE N="870" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Zuitava 1. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Zuitawa 2.
Suttava 3. Zwitana 4.</NOTE>  qui est in media silva. Item
ad aquilonalem plagam contra Poloniam castellum
Cladzco <NOTE N="871" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Kladzcho 1. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Kladsko 2. Kladsco 3. Glecz  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit man. rec.</HI>  5.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(350)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Glatz.</NOTE> , situm juxta flumen nomine Nizam
 <NOTE N="872" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> Nisam
 <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  Nizam 1. Mzam 2. Nizzam 3. Nizan 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(351)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Neisse.</NOTE> . Hic dux Slavnic, quamdiu vixit, feliciter
 <COL N="0094B"></COL> vixit.</P> <LIST COM="0094"><ITEM>28. Anno dominicae incarnationis 982.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 983.</ITEM></LIST> <P COM="0094">Anno dominicae incarnationis 984 obiit <NOTE N="(352)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Constat eum anno praecedenti obiisse.</NOTE>  Romae
caesar Otto secundus. Huic imperatori <NOTE N="873" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> secundus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(353)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Potius Ottoni tertio; cf. Vita S. Adalberti,
c. 22.</NOTE> 
Adalbertus praesul Pragensis adeo fuit familiaris et
carus obsequiis, ut in pascha Domini <NOTE N="874" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE> , quod celebravit
rex Aquisgrani in palatio coram omnibus
episcopis, hac eum <NOTE N="875" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> cum 2.</NOTE>  officii celsitudine sublimaret,
quo sibi coronam imponeret et majorem missam
celebraret, quod solum fas erat ut archiepiscopus
faceret <NOTE N="(354)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0094" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0094D"></COL> Minime de coronatione Ottonis III, sed de
impositione coronae, quae in diebus festis fieri solebat,
cogitandum esse, ex ipsis auctoris verbis satis
apparet; quod quo tempore factum sit non liquet.
Ottonem, a. 995, Pascha Aquisgrani celebrasse tabulae
ejus probant ap. Boehmer reg., n. 746; eodem
fere tempore S. Adalbertum in Germania fuisse, auctor
Vitae ejus innuere videtur c. 19, 20.</NOTE> . Post festum vero, cum jam acciperet
 <NOTE N="876" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> accepisset 3.</NOTE>  a caesare licentiam redeundi ad patriam
sevocat <NOTE N="877" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> clam vocat 4.</NOTE>  eum caesar in secretarium, et faciens
suorum confessionem peccaminum, commendat se
 <COL N="0094C"></COL> piis recordationibus ejus orationum. Insuper dat ei
paramenta, in quibus missam celebrarat <NOTE N="878" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0093" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0093"></COL> celebravit 4. celebraret 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">cum correctore</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  in pascha,
scilicet albam, dalmaticam, casulam, cappam
 <COL N="0095A"></COL> et faciterium <NOTE N="879" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> facitersium  <HI REND="ITALIC">corrector</HI>  2. facitergium 3.</NOTE> , quo ea habeat sui ob memoriam.
Quae usque hodie in Pragensi ecclesia honorifice
habentur et dicuntur paramenta sancti Adalberti.</P> <LIST COM="0095"><ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 985 <NOTE N="880" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Numerus alia manu in margine</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">adscriptus.</HI></NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 986.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 987 obiit Streziziliva
 <NOTE N="881" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Zrezizlava
1. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4. Strziezislawa 2. Zrezizlana 3. Ztrelizizlava 5.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(355)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095C"></COL> Ex claro genere Sclavorum nobilissima;
conf. Brunonis Vita S. Adalberti, c. 1.</NOTE> , sancti Adalberti mater venerabilis et
Deo acceptabilis matrona, tantae et tam sanctae sobolis
 <NOTE N="882" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  dici mater et esse digna.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 988.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 989.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 990 <NOTE N="(356)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095C"></COL> Jam tempore Nativitatis Christi, a. 988,
S. Adalbertus Romae commoratus esse videtur;
conf. Wilmans Otto III, p. 92.</NOTE>  sanctus
Adalbertus Romae ad sanctum Alexium, inscio abbate
quis esset, factus est monachus.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 991.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="0095B"></COL> Anno dominicae incarnationis 992.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 993.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 994.</ITEM></LIST> <P COM="0095">29. Nec <NOTE N="883" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Hic iterum incipit cod.</HI>  7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  transsiliendum censeo quod ab aliis
praetermissum video. Nam praesul Adalbertus videns,
quod grex sibi commissus semper in praecipicium
iret, nec eum ad rectam viam convertere quiret,
timens ne et ipse cum pereunte <NOTE N="884" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> perheunte 1.</NOTE>  plebe periret,
non ausus est cum eis amplius stare, nec passus est
suam ulterius incassum praedicandi operam dare <NOTE N="885" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> .
Sed cum jam jamque <NOTE N="886" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> jamque  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1. 3.</NOTE>  Romam iter arripere vellet
 <NOTE N="(357)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095C"></COL> Primum erat S. Adalberti iter Romanum;
 <COL N="0096C"></COL> itaque cum Cosma minime ad annum 994 referri
potest.</NOTE> , forte fortuna tempore in ipso Strahquaz
 <NOTE N="887" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Ztrahquaz 1. 4</NOTE> , de quo supra retulimus, sui abbatis cum
licentia venerat de Radisbona <NOTE N="888" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Radispona 1.</NOTE> , post multos annos
visere patriam dulcem et cognatos atque fratrem
 <COL N="0095C"></COL> suum Boemiae ducem. Cum quo vir Dei praesul Adalbertus
secretum peciit et colloquium tenuit, multa
conquestus de infidelitate et nequicia populi, de incesta
copula et super illicita discidia <NOTE N="889" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> dissidia 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.
4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(358)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0096" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0096C"></COL> Vita S. Adalberti, c. 12.</NOTE>  inconstantis
conjugii, de inobedientia et negligentia cleri,
de arrogantia et intollerabili potencia comitum. Ad
ultimum omnem intencionem sui cordis sibi aperuit
 <NOTE N="890" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> aperit A. A*.</NOTE> , quod vellet Romam apostolicum <NOTE N="(359)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0096" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0096C"></COL> Joannem XVI annis 985-996 sedentem.</NOTE>  consultum
ire, et ad gentem apostatricem <NOTE N="891" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> apostaticam 3.</NOTE>  nunquam
redire. Inter haec et ad <NOTE N="892" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  haec haec addidit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Et bene
 <COL N="0096A"></COL> est,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod tu frater nosceris esse ducis, et hujus
terrae ex</HI> <NOTE N="893" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  ex 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dominis</HI> <NOTE N="894" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> dominis  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  domini 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">originem ducis</HI> <NOTE N="895" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> et hujus—ducis  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A. A*.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">te
plebs ista mavult</HI> <NOTE N="896" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> magis vult 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dominari, et tibi magis obedire
quam mihi. Tu</HI> <NOTE N="897" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> tu consilio—poteris  <HI REND="ITALIC">desiderantur in</HI>  4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">consilio et auxilio tui</HI> <NOTE N="898" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A A*.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fratris
superbos comprimere, negligentes arguere, inobedientes
corrigere, infideles increpare poteris. Tua dignitas
et scientia, tui habitus sanctimonia multum</HI> <NOTE N="899" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> multum  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">concordant,
ad pontificalia regimina. Quod ut fiat ego
tibi cum</HI> <NOTE N="900" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Dei voluntate et mea potestate concedo, et
ut liceat me vivente istic episcopus ut sis, aput apostolicum
omnibus votis intercedam</HI> <NOTE N="901" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> intendam 3.</NOTE> . Et quem forte
manu tenebat episcopalem baculum, ponit sibi in
sinum. Quem ille, quasi furibundus, in terram projecit,
et haec verba insuper adjecit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Nolo ut</HI> <NOTE N="902" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A, 1. 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aliquam
dignitatem habeam</HI> <NOTE N="903" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest in omnibus cod., alia manu
superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in mundo</HI> <NOTE N="904" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> possideam 4.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">honores
 <COL N="0096B"></COL> fugio</HI> <NOTE N="905" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">A verbis</HI>  nores fugio  <HI REND="ITALIC">continuatur chronicon in cod.</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pompas seculi despicio: indigno me judico
episcopali fastigio, nec tantum pondus pastoralis
curae ferre sufficio. Monachus sum, mortuus sum:
mortuos sepelire non possum.</HI>  Ad haec praesul <NOTE N="906" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Adalbertus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  respondit:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Scias, frater</HI> <NOTE N="907" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Ztrahquaz  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">scias, quod modo non facis
cum bono, facies autem postea, sed cum tuo maximo</HI> 
 <NOTE N="908" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A, A*.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">malo.</HI>  Post haec praesul <NOTE N="909" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Adelbertus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE> , ut proposuerat,
Romam iter arripit, et gentem suis praeceptis inobedientem
relinquit <NOTE N="910" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> reliquit 2.</NOTE> . Et quia tunc temporis dux
non erat suae potestatis, sed comitum <NOTE N="911" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> ducum
A, ducis A*.</NOTE> , comites
versi in Dei odium, patrum iniquorum pessimi alii,
valde malum operabantur facinus <NOTE N="912" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> scelus 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et iniquum.
Nam sub quadam festiva die <NOTE N="913" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> die festivo A, A*, festivitate 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(360)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0096" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0096C"></COL> S. Wenceslai; cfr. Brunonis Vita S. Adalberti,
c. 21; sed hoc post secundum ejus iter Romanum
factum est anno 996.</NOTE>  furtim irrumpunt
urbem Lubic, in qua fratres sancti Adalberti
et milites urbis universi velut oves innocentes
 <COL N="0096C"></COL> assistebant sacris missarum solempniis festa celebrantes.
At illi ceu lupi immanes urbis moenia irrumpentes,
masculum et feminam usque ad unum
interficientes, quatuor <NOTE N="914" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> universis 3.</NOTE>  fratribus sancti Adalberti
cum omni prole ante ipsum altare decollatis, urbem
 <NOTE N="915" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> Lubic
 <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  comburunt, plateas sanguine perfundunt, et
cruentis spoliis ac crudeli praeda onerati <NOTE N="916" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  1</NOTE>  hilares
ad proprias <NOTE N="917" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A, 1.</NOTE>  redeunt <NOTE N="918" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> recedunt A, A*.</NOTE>  lares. Interfecti sunt
autem in urbe Lubic quinque fratres sancti Adalberti
 <NOTE N="919" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> praesulis  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  anno dom. incarn. 995, quorum nomina <NOTE N="920" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0095" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0095"></COL> quorum nomina  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest 2. Per verba:</HI>  Anno dom. incarn. 995  <HI REND="ITALIC">linea alio atramento ducta est</HI></NOTE> 
 <COL N="0097A"></COL> sunt haec: Sobebor, Spitimir <NOTE N="921" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">olim</HI>  Spitimur 2. Sptimir 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , Dobrazlav <NOTE N="922" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Bobrazlau 1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Bobraslau  <HI REND="ITALIC">olim in 2. mutatum vero alterum</HI>  b  <HI REND="ITALIC">in</HI>  h,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deletum</HI>  ra  <HI REND="ITALIC">et suprascriptum</HI>  II,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita correctum</HI>  Bobuslau. Bohrazlau  <HI REND="ITALIC">collator</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Drobozlau 3. Pobrazlau 4,
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , Porey
 <NOTE N="923" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Poreii 3.</NOTE> , Caslav <NOTE N="924" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Cazlav 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">rel.</HI>  Czaslau 2, Chazlaw 5.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0097">30. His ita <NOTE N="925" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> itaque 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  peractis, dux Bolezlaus inito consilio
cum clericis, Maguntinum praesulem <NOTE N="926" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  his
sollicitat verbis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aut nostrum pastorem Adalbertum
ad nos revoces, quod magis volumus, aut alium nobis
in loco sui ordines, quod inviti poscimus</HI> <NOTE N="927" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> possimus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  poscimus 1.</NOTE> .
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Nam</HI> <NOTE N="928" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> nam—edulia  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Christi ovilia adhuc in hac gente fidei novicia,
nisi eis assit vigilans pastoris custodia, cruentis</HI> 
 <NOTE N="929" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> rapidis vel rabidis cruentis 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">lupis opima recta</HI> <NOTE N="930" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> recte 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fiunt</HI> <NOTE N="931" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> fient 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">edulia</HI> <NOTE N="932" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> edilia 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">correctum alia manu</HI>  edulia.</NOTE> . Tunc
 <COL N="0098A"></COL> metropolita Maguntinus sollicitus ne populus nuper
 <NOTE N="933" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> a  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2.</NOTE>  Christo adquisitus, relapsus in antiquos
pereat sacrilegos ritus, mittens legatos ad apostolicum
clamat ut aut viduatae Pragensi ecclesiae maritum
remittat <NOTE N="(361)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097C"></COL> Vita S. Adalberti, c. 18.</NOTE> , aut alium in loco sui ordinari <NOTE N="934" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> suo ordinare 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
permittat. Et quoniam servus Dei Adalbertus, jussu
apostolici factus liber a custodia gregis dominici,
in coenobio sancti Alexii <NOTE N="935" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> confessoris  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  cum senatoribus coeli
infra amoenam curiam terreni conversabatur <NOTE N="936" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> conversabantur  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  -batur 1.</NOTE> 
Elisii,

 <POEM COM="0098"><L><COL N="0097"></COL> Hunc domnus papa, suus et pius insimul abba <NOTE N="(362)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097C"></COL> Leo abbas monasterii S. Alexii.</NOTE> ,</L> <L>Talibus alloquiis <NOTE N="937" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> aloquuiis
1.</NOTE>  moestum solantur amicis:</L></POEM> 

 <POEM COM="0097"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">O fili dulcissime et frater amantissime</HI> <NOTE N="938" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Adalberte  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,</L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">per caritatem Dei te deprecamur</HI> <NOTE N="939" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> deprecor 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et per amorem proximi obtestamur,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">ut ad tuam parrochiam</HI> <NOTE N="940" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">littera</HI>  c.  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dignanter redeas</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">regimenque tuarum ovium diligenter recipias.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Si te audierint, Deo gratias: si te non audierint, fugientes te</HI> <NOTE N="941" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fugias,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">ne cum pereuntibus pereas, et ad nationes exteras praedicandi licentiam habeas.</HI></L> <L>Hac praesul <NOTE N="942" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Adalbertus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  valde exhylaratus <NOTE N="943" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">alia man. superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  sententia,</L> <L>quod sibi sit <NOTE N="944" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> est 1.</NOTE>  data docendi exteras gentes licentia,</L> <L>non sine magna moesticia fratrum dulcia linquit <NOTE N="945" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> liquit 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  consortia.</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0097B"></COL> Et cum viro summae discretionis praesule <NOTE N="(363)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097C"></COL> Leodiensi; cfr. Vita S. Adalberti, c. 21;
 <COL N="0098C"></COL> sed quod factum est in secundo itinere Romano,
a. 996; auctor duo illa itinera in unum confundit.</NOTE> , nomine
Nothario <NOTE N="946" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Votharino  <HI REND="ITALIC">corrector</HI> 
2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Notario 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , adiens <NOTE N="947" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  archiepiscopum Maguntinae
 <COL N="0098B"></COL> urbis, in palatio rogat, quo per ejus missos scire
posset, si se suus grex <NOTE N="948" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Verba</HI>  grex—suus  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu in margine</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">apposita.</HI></NOTE>  recipere vellet <NOTE N="949" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.
al. man.</HI>  1.</NOTE> .

 <POEM COM="0098"><L><COL N="0097"></COL> Quo facto, quid sibi suus grex responderit,</L> <L>aut quam ob causam eum non receperit,</L> <L>vel ad quas gentes inde transierit,</L> <L>quantae etiam frugalitatis omnibus diebus sui episcopii fuerit,</L> <L>quanta morum honestate enituerit,</L> <L>scire poterit, qui vitam ejus seu <NOTE N="950" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> sive 2.</NOTE>  passionem legerit.</L> <L>Nam mihi jam dicta bis <NOTE N="951" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> biis 1.</NOTE>  dicere non placet ista.</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0097B"></COL> Tunc Ztrahquaz <NOTE N="952" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Strahquas 2  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic deinceps.</HI></NOTE>  frater ducis, de quo supra meminimus,
videns episcopum quasi jure et regulariter
 <NOTE N="953" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> regaliter 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  a sua plebe repudiatum, tumido fastu exarsit
in episcopatum. Et quia facile est volentem cogere,
protinus hunc ydiotam et sicophantam populus nequam
in episcopalem levat <NOTE N="954" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> locat 3.</NOTE>  kathedram. Sic enim,
 <COL N="0097C"></COL> sic Deus saepe <NOTE N="955" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> Deus
sic saepe 3, saepe  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , 5.</NOTE>  permittit per sui providentiam
 <COL N="0098B"></COL> pravorum hominum invalescere potentiam, sicut in
hac inregulari <NOTE N="956" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">syllaba</HI>  in  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  A. regulari 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  electione ludicra <NOTE N="957" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> ludrica A. ludicitus
3.</NOTE>  praevaluere <NOTE N="958" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> praevalere  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia man.</HI>  praevaluere A. praevalere 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
Cereris generi <NOTE N="959" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> genere  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  generi A.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(364)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0098" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0098C"></COL> I. e. diaboli.</NOTE> . Nam fuit hic Ztrahquaz veste
compositus, mente tumidus, actibus dissipatus,
oculis vagus, verbis vanus, moribus ypocrita, et
tocius erroris mandrita, atque in omnibus operibus
 <COL N="0098C"></COL> malis iniquorum archigeronta <NOTE N="960" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0097" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0097"></COL> archigeron
4</NOTE> .

 <POEM COM="0098"><L><COL N="0097"></COL> Plura referre pudet Ztrahquaz de praesule pseudo.</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0099A"></COL> Sufficiunt <NOTE N="961" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> sufficiant 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4.</NOTE>  pro multis pauca. Ventum erat Maguntinae
sedis ad <NOTE N="962" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  archipraesulem <NOTE N="963" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> episcopum 3.</NOTE> : ubi peractis
omnibus quae agenda erant per ordinem, sicut fieri
solet, post examinationem episcopalem, choro letaniam
 <COL N="0100A"></COL> <NOTE N="964" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> laetamini  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  laetaniam
2 <SUP>b</SUP> . laetamina 3.</NOTE>  modulante, dum procumbit super tapecia
archipraesul infulatus ante altare, et post eum inter
duos suffraganeos

 <POEM COM="0100"><L>qui ordinandus erat Ztrahquaz dum <NOTE N="965" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  prosternitur in medio,</L> <L>heu dira condicio, arripitur atroci daemonio:</L> <L>et quod servus <NOTE N="966" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> serus  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  servus 1.</NOTE>  Dei <NOTE N="967" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> Adalbertus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  olim sibi praedixerat clanculo,</L> <L>palam fit coram clero et omni populo.</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0099A"></COL> Hactenus haec inseruisse sufficiat <NOTE N="968" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> sufficiant 3. hactenus—sufficiat  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5. hactenus—996  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  7 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(365)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099C"></COL> Meram hoc fabellam esse Pubitschka probare
conatus est III, 224.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0099">31. Anno dom. inc. 996 <NOTE N="(366)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099C"></COL> S. Adalbertus obiit anno 997; cfr. Palackv
Wurdigung, p. 28.</NOTE>  postquam insignis
signifer Christi, praesul Adalbertus, retibus fidei
cepit Pannoniam simul et Poloniam, ad ultimum,
 <COL N="0099B"></COL> dum in Pruzia <NOTE N="969" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> Brussia 2, 3.</NOTE>  seminat verbum Dei, hanc praesentem
vitam pro Christo feliciter terminavit martiro
9 Kalendas Maii, feria 6 <NOTE N="970" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Reliqua
hujus libri pars penitus desideratur in</HI>  7 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sequitur fundatio ecclesiae Wissegradensis a.</HI>  1070.</NOTE> . Eo anno fuit pascha
7 Kalendas <NOTE N="971" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> VI Cal.
3.</NOTE>  Maii <NOTE N="(367)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099C"></COL> Vita S. Adalberti, c. 30. Pascha anni 996,
die 12 mensis Aprilis celebratum est.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0099">Anno dom. inc. 997 saepe memoratus dux Bolezlaus
videns Pragensem ecclesiam suo pastore viduatam,
dirigit legatos suos ad imperatorem tercium
Ottonem, rogans <NOTE N="972" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE> , ut Boemiensi ecclesiae sponsum
meritis dignum daret, ne <NOTE N="973" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> ut—non redeat 2.</NOTE>  grex Christo noviter
mancipatus redeat ad pristinos vanitatis ritus et ad
iniquos actus; quippe profitetur non haberi in tota
Boemia tunc temporis clericum episcopatu dignum.
Mox caesar <NOTE N="974" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">addid. al. man.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  augustus Otto sicut <NOTE N="975" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  erat in divinis
humanisque rebus prudentissimus, annuens peticioni
eorum coepit curiosius cogitare, quem de suis
 <COL N="0099C"></COL> potissimum in hoc tam arduum opus dirigeret clericum.
Forte aderat in regali curia <NOTE N="(368)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099C"></COL> Non in imperatoris sed in Bolezlavi II ducis
aula versabatur Theadagus, qui monachus Novae
Corbeiae arte medica peritus, duci sanitatem restituerat;
cfr. Thietmar VII, 41; qui vero confirmat
 <COL N="0100C"></COL> ab Ottone Theadagum sedem Pragensem regendam
accepisse.</NOTE>  capellanus
nomine Theadagus <NOTE N="976" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> Thegdagus 1,
3  <HI REND="ITALIC">et deinceps; corr.</HI>  Thedgadus 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , actibus probis et moribus
decoratus, liberalibus studiis adprime eruditus, genere
de Saxonia, lingua perfecte <NOTE N="977" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> proferre 1, 3.</NOTE>  imbutus Sclavonica
 <NOTE N="978" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> Slavica 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Hunc quia sors obtulerat, omnis regiae
aulae senatus et ipse caesar valde laetificatus in pontificem
Pragensis ecclesiae eligit et collaudat, et mittens
ad Maguntinum archipraesulem, quo eum celeriter
in episcopum consecret, mandat.</P> <P COM="0099">Anno dom. inc. 998 Nonis Julii consecratus est
Teadagus, honeste a clero et populo <NOTE N="979" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> et populo  <HI REND="ITALIC">omittit</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Pragensis ecclesiae
 <COL N="0100A"></COL> recipitur, atque cum magno gaudio ad cornu
altaris sancti Viti intronisatur. Dux valde congratulatur
quia pastor bonus suo gregi arridet, et
grex laetus pastori novo <NOTE N="980" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> suo 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  alludit.</P> <P COM="0100">32. Rexit autem iste excellentissimus princeps
 <COL N="0100B"></COL> Bolezlaus post patris obitum 32 annis ducatum, quia
quae justiciae. quae catholicae <NOTE N="981" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> chatolice 1.</NOTE>  fidei, quae christianae
religionis sunt, erat ardentissimus executor, apud
quem <NOTE N="982" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> christianae  <HI REND="ITALIC">repetit</HI>  1.</NOTE>  nullus ecclesiasticam, nullus mundanam
dignitatem obtinuit per pecuniam <NOTE N="983" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> pro pecunia 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3. 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Fuit etiam <NOTE N="984" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> et 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
ut res probat, in praeliis victoriosissimus victor, sed
victis clementissimus indultor atque praecipuus pacis
amator. Cui erant maximae opes, bellica instrumenta
et dulcia armorum studia. Nam plus diligebat <NOTE N="985" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> diligebant  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI> —bat. 1.</NOTE> 
ferri rigorem, quam auri fulgorem, in cujus oculis
nemo utilis displicuit, nunquam inutilis placuit, suis
mitis, hostibus terribilis fuit. Habuit autem hic gloriosissimus
dux <NOTE N="986" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> Bolezlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Hemmam sibi in matrimonio
junctam, quae genere fuit caeteris nobilior <NOTE N="(369)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0100" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0100C"></COL> Dobner IV, 432, eam filiam Conradi regis
Burgundiae fuisse conjicit.</NOTE> ,
 <COL N="0100C"></COL> sed, quod magis laudandum est, nobilitate morum
multo <NOTE N="987" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  praestancior. Ex qua duos <NOTE N="(370)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0100" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0100C"></COL> Quatuor potius; praeter nominatos Jaromirus
et Udalricus, quos Bolezlavi III filios fuisse falso
opinatur Cosmas, erant filii Bolezlavi II, teste Thietmaro
V, 15.</NOTE>  filios suscepit
elegantissimae indolis, scilicet Wencezlaum et
Bolezlaum; sed Wencezlaus ab ineunte aetate hanc
 <NOTE N="988" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> hanc  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.</NOTE>  fragilem vitam mutavit aeternitate. Bolezlaus
autem post discessum patris sedis suscepit gubernacula
principalis, ut in sequentibus declarabitur <NOTE N="989" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> declaratur A.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0100">33. Factum est autem, cum appropinquarent <NOTE N="990" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> appropinquaret 3.</NOTE> 
dies supra memorati ducis <NOTE N="991" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> ducis  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.</NOTE>  Bolezlay, quo jam
aeternam commutaret morte vitam <NOTE N="992" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> com. m. v. aet. A.</NOTE> , vocat aequivocum
suum et superstitem natum <NOTE N="993" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> natu 4.
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , et adstante
coniuge Hemma <NOTE N="994" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0099" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0099"></COL> Hemina 2.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(371)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0100" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0100C"></COL> Valde vexavit Emmae hujus origo satis obscula
rerum Bohemicarum indagatores. Vid. Pubitschka
III, 153; Palacky I.</NOTE> , et multa procerum turma
 <COL N="0101A"></COL> <NOTE N="995" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> turoa 2.</NOTE> , jam interrumpente <NOTE N="996" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> interrupente A.</NOTE>  singultu verba, prout
potuit, his dulcem affatur filium dictis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si fas esset
matri sui</HI> <NOTE N="997" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> suae utit infantis 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">uteri infanti, ut lactis ubera, sic sapientiae
dare munera, non natura, sed homo creatus dominaretur
in creatura. Attamen nonnulla Deus sua
concessit hominibus dona, sicut Noe, Ysaac, Thobiae
atque Mathatiae, ita duntaxat, ut quos illi benedixerunt</HI> 
 <NOTE N="998" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> benedixerit 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  erunt 3.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">benedixit illis Deus, et quos praeordinaverunt</HI> 
 <NOTE N="999" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> praeordinaverit
3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ad bonae conversationis vitam, contulit et illis
Deus perseverantiam. Sic et hodie, fili mi, si non
assit sancti Spiritus clementia, parum prodest meorum
verborum jactancia. Ducem te, inquit Deus, constitui</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1000" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manus addit</HI>  1. 2.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">noli extolli, sed esto quasi unus ex illis</HI> <NOTE N="1001" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> eis 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">id est</HI> <NOTE N="1002" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> i. A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">si te caeteris sublimiorem sencias, mortalem
tamen</HI> <NOTE N="1003" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> tamen  <HI REND="ITALIC">add. alia man.</HI>  A.
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3. 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">te esse</HI> <NOTE N="1004" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> esse  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cognoscas, nec</HI> <NOTE N="1005" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> ne 2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dignitatis
 <COL N="0101B"></COL> gloriam, qua in seculo sublimaris, aspicias, sed
opus, quod tecum ad inferos deportes, intendas. Haec
praecepta Dei in corde tuo scribe, et haec mandata
patris tui non omitte. Ecclesiae limina frequenter visita,
Deum adora, sacerdotes ejus honora, ne sis sapiens
apud temetipsum, sed consule plures, si sapiant
in id ipsum</HI> <NOTE N="1006" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> sed—ipsum  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pluribus ut placeas, sed qualibus
stude.</HI></P> <P COM="0101"><HI REND="ITALIC">Omnia cum amicis, sed prius de ipsis tracta.
Juste judica, sed non sine misericordia. Viduam et
advenam ne despice ad tuam</HI> <NOTE N="1007" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.
al. man.</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">stantes januam.</HI> 

 <POEM COM="0101"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Dilige denarium, sed parce dilige formam.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Res enim publica, licet sit</HI> <NOTE N="1008" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nimis adaucta,</HI></L></POEM> 

 <HI REND="ITALIC">per formam</HI> <NOTE N="1009" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">minio superscripsit recentior manus</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nummismais falsam cito erit ad nihilum
redacta. Est aliquid, fili mi, quod Karolus,
 <COL N="0101C"></COL> rex sapientissimus et manu</HI> <NOTE N="1010" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">potentissimus, haud</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1011" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Verbis</HI>  haud—humilibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscriptae sunt in 2. hae glossae Bohemicae</HI>  gesto mi nizizi hide
nemnozem si geczin wronelati.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aequiperandus</HI> <NOTE N="1012" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  A. equipperandus 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nobis hominibus valde humilibus,
cum filium suum Pipinum post se in solio sublimandum
disponeret, cur terribili eum</HI> <NOTE N="1013" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> cum terribili eum 2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . eum
terribili cum 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sacramento
constringeret, ne in regno suo subdola</HI> <NOTE N="1014" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscripta glossa Bohemica</HI>  chytra.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et prava
taxatio</HI> <NOTE N="1015" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">glossa Boh.</HI>  czena.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ponderis</HI> <NOTE N="1016" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">glossa Boh.</HI> 
promiena.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aut monetae fieret. Certe nulla
clades</HI> <NOTE N="1017" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gl. Boh.</HI>  wahy zahuba.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nulla pestilentia</HI> <NOTE N="1018" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gl. Boh.</HI>  mor.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nec mortalitas, nec non
si</HI> <NOTE N="1019" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> si 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , non  <HI REND="ITALIC">a correctore 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , subductum.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hostes totam terram rapinis</HI> <NOTE N="1020" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3,  <HI REND="ITALIC">gl. Boh.</HI>  lupezem.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">incendiis devastarent</HI> <NOTE N="1021" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> devastantes 3.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">magis populo Dei nocerent, quam frequens
mutacio</HI> <NOTE N="1022" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">In 2 difficilis lectio, ita ut potius</HI>  invitatio
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quam</HI>  immutatio  <HI REND="ITALIC">legas. In margine vero</HI>  mutatio.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et fraudulenta pejoratio nummi. Quae
 <COL N="0102A"></COL> pestis, aut quae infernalis Herinis inclementius spoliat,
perdit et attenuat christicolas, quam fraus in
nummo herilis? Atqui</HI> <NOTE N="1023" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> aut qui 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">post haec senescente justicia
et invalescente nequicia surgent non duces, sed fures
non rectores populi Dei, sed nequam exactores, avarissimi
sine misericordia homines, Deum omnia cernentem
non timentes</HI> <NOTE N="1024" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> metuentes 3.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui ter vel quater in anno
monetam mutando</HI> <NOTE N="1025" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">erunt</HI> <NOTE N="1026" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> ruunt 3, eunt 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in laqueum</HI> <NOTE N="1027" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gl. Boh.</HI>  kosidla.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">diaboli</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1028" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">gl. Boh.</HI>  diablowa.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ad perdicionem populi Dei. Talibus enim nequam
artibus et per legum insolentiam coangustabunt
hujus regni terminos, quos ego dilatavi usque ad
montes, qui sunt ultra Krakov</HI> <NOTE N="1029" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Crakov 1,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic deinceps.</HI>  Krakou
3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nomine Triti</HI> <NOTE N="1030" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Triti A, Trytri 1, Tryu 2, Tryti 2 <SUP>b</SUP> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed corrector</HI>  Trnin. Triti 3, Tritri 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">per Dei gratiam</HI> <NOTE N="1031" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> misericordiam
A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et populi oppulentiam. Nam</HI> 

 <POEM COM="0102"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Diviciae plebis sunt laus et gloria regis,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nec sibi sed domino gravis est, quae servit</HI> <NOTE N="1032" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> premit  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. recentior manus</HI>  1, quem gravat qui s. 3, 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">egestas</HI> <NOTE N="(372)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101C"></COL> Lucan., Phars. III, 152.</NOTE></L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0102B"></COL> Plura locuturus erat: sed extrema hora diriguerunt
 <NOTE N="1033" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> diriguerat 3.</NOTE>  principis ora, et cicius dicto obdormivit in Domino,
atque magnus super eum factus est planctus;
dies autem sui obitus est 7 Idus Februarii anno
Dom. inc. 999.</P> <P COM="0102">34. Eodem anno Gaudentius <NOTE N="1034" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> archiepiscopus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , qui et Radim
 <NOTE N="1035" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Radun 3.</NOTE> , frater sancti Adalberti ordinatus est episcopus
 <NOTE N="1036" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> episcopus  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ad titulum Gnezdensis <NOTE N="1037" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Genezdensis 1.</NOTE>  ecclesiae <NOTE N="(373)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101C"></COL> Jam in tabula anni 999 Gaudentii archiepiscopi
mentio fit; cfr. Wilmans Otto III, p. 113.</NOTE>  Hic
gloriosissimus dux secundus Bolezlaus, vere et hodie
haud <NOTE N="1038" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  plangendus satis <NOTE N="1039" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> satis  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
A, 1, 2, 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , 5, haud  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  satis  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> , cujus memoria in
benedictione est, in quantum ampliando dilataverit
 <NOTE N="1040" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> dilatando ampliaverit 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  ferro sui terminos ducatus, apostolica testatur
auctoritas in privilegio ejusdem Pragensis episcopatus
 <NOTE N="(374)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101C"></COL> Dubito num Cosmas ex descriptione dioecesis
Pragensis in privilegio pontificis merito conjecerit,
Bolezlavum ferro regni fines ampliasse.</NOTE> . Post cujus obitum filius ejus, tercius Bolezlaus
 <COL N="0102C"></COL> <NOTE N="(375)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0102C"></COL> Cognomento Rufus, teste Thietmaro V, 7.</NOTE> , ut supra relatum est <NOTE N="1041" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> retulimus 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , successit in
ducatum; sed non eisdem rerum successibus, nec
paternis auspiciis terminos adquisitos obtinuit. Nam
dux Poloniensis Mesco <NOTE N="1042" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Mesko
1,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ita porro.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(376)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0102C"></COL> Imo Bolezlaus cognomine Chrabry, filius
Mesconis.</NOTE> , quo non fuit alter
dolosior homo, mox urbem Kracov <NOTE N="(377)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0102C"></COL> Krakan.</NOTE>  abstulit
dolo, omnibus quos ibi invenit Boemiis <NOTE N="1043" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  extinctis
gladio. Fuerunt autem duci <NOTE N="1044" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest A.</HI></NOTE>  Bolezlav <NOTE N="1045" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Bolezlao 1.</NOTE>  ex
conjuge nobili duo fratres <NOTE N="1046" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> duae,  <HI REND="ITALIC">omisso</HI>  fratres 3.</NOTE> , foecundae <NOTE N="1047" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> secundae 2, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  matris
gloria nati <NOTE N="(378)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0102" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0102C"></COL> Hoc falsum esse vide supra.</NOTE>  scilicet Udalricus <NOTE N="1048" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0101" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0101"></COL> Oodaldricus 1, Udalricus 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Oalrilcus 3,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic deinceps.</HI>  Odelricus 4. Oudalricus 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Dedalricus 5.</NOTE>  et Jaromir.
Sed Jaromir juvenis patris est nutritus in aula, Udalricus
 <COL N="0103A"></COL> <NOTE N="1049" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Odaldricus 1.</NOTE>  autem a pueritia <NOTE N="1050" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> a pueritia  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE>  traditus erat imperatoris
Heinrici <NOTE N="1051" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Henrici A.</NOTE>  in curiam, quod addisceret mores
 <NOTE N="1052" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  1, morem A,  <HI REND="ITALIC">rel.</HI></NOTE>  et eorum <NOTE N="1053" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  astuciam ac Teutonicam linguam
 <NOTE N="(379)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103D"></COL> Aufugerant in Germaniam, quia Bolizlavus
Jaromirum evirari, Udalricum in balneis suffocari
jusserat; cfr. Thietmar. V, 15. Ex ipso rerum ordine
patet Heinricum illo tempore minime imperatorem,
sed Bavariae ducem fuisse.</NOTE> . Post haec transacto non longo tempore <NOTE N="(380)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103D"></COL> I. e. anno 1003; fugit Cosmam, Bolezlaum
a. 1002 Bohemia expulsum et anno 1003 a Bolezlavo
Polono restitutum esse, cum medio tempore Wladiboi
Polonus et Jaromir regnum paucos menses
obtinuissent. De his omnibus cf. Thietmar. l. l.</NOTE> 
supradictus uterque dux Mesco et Bolezlaus in condicto
 <NOTE N="1054" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> concilio 1.</NOTE>  loco conveniunt ad colloquium, et data
fide ac juramento firmata inter se pace, dux Mesco
invitat Bolezlaum, quo dignaretur venire ad suum
 <NOTE N="1055" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> ad s. ven A.</NOTE>  convivium. At ille, sicut erat vir columbinus et
sine felle <NOTE N="(381)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103D"></COL> Thietmaro V, 7, est immensae impietatis
auctor; et merito; confer quod idem narrat V, 18.</NOTE> , suorum consilio familiarium dixit se
omnia facturum velle. Sed quae pestis nocentior
quam familiares inimici? Quorum quia non potuit
contraire dolosis consiliis, immo jam suis fatis, hah
mens praesaga ducis! vocat ad se nobiliores, et quos
relicturus erat in regno, qui videbantur sibi fideliores,
 <COL N="0103B"></COL> et his eos affatur dictis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si quid forte
mihi,
quod absit! alter et praeter fidem atque spem in Polonia
evenerit, hunc</HI> <NOTE N="1056" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">erasum</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">meum natum Jaromir vestrae
fidei committo, et mei in loco ducem vobis relinquo.</HI> 
Sicque dispositis regni negotiis it cariturus lumine,
et intrat urbem Kracov sinistro omine <NOTE N="1057" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> homine 1.</NOTE>  perfidi ducis
Mesconis ad <NOTE N="1058" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> ad  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  convivium. Nam mox inter prandendum
pax, fides, jus hospitale rumpitur, dux Bolezlaus
capitur atque oculis privatur <NOTE N="(382)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103D"></COL> Obiit anno demum 1037, ut testantur Annales
Pragenses.</NOTE> , suosque omnes
alios trucidant <NOTE N="1059" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> alios trucidant
desunt 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , alios obtruncant, alios carceri
tradunt. Interea iducis Bolezlai domestici et familiares
inimici, gens invisa, generatio mala, Wrisovici <NOTE N="1060" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Wirsovici 1, Wirssevici 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Versovici 3, Wrssovici 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <NOTE N="(383)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0104" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0104D"></COL> Est patronymicum,  <HI REND="ITALIC">filii, posteri Wrs;</HI>  cfr.
Palacky Gesch. Bohmens, I, 163. 363.</NOTE> , operabantur <NOTE N="1061" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> operantur 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  abhominabile malum et
antea retro seculis inauditum <NOTE N="(384)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0104" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0104D"></COL> Quod quo tempore factum sit non satis
liquet. Dobner V, 57 ad annum 1012 celus revocat.</NOTE> . Quorum primus
et quasi caput tocius iniquitatis erat Kochan <NOTE N="1062" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> c.  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. man.</HI>  A. Kohan 1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . Cohan 3.</NOTE> ,
 <COL N="0103C"></COL> vir sceleratissimus et omnium malorum hominum
pessimus. Hic et sui propinqui, homines iniqui <NOTE N="1063" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> homines iniqui  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A, 1.</NOTE> ,
ducis cum filio Jaromir venientes venationis ad locum,
qui dicitur Weliz <NOTE N="1064" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Veliz 2,
Weliz 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(385)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0104" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0104D"></COL> Postero tempore hoc loco praepositura exstabat
S. Joanni Baptistae dedicata, quae haud procul
a Rakonicz sita in bello Hussitico diruta est.
Cfr. Pubitschka III, 205.</NOTE> , postquam referente
fama perceperunt <NOTE N="1065" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> perceperat 3.</NOTE>  quae facta sunt de duce
in Polonia:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quis iste est,</HI>  inquiunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">homuncio</HI> <NOTE N="1066" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> h  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr al. manu</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0104A"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">alga vilior</HI> <NOTE N="(386)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0104" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0104D"></COL> Hor. serm. II, 2, 8.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui super nos debeat</HI> <NOTE N="1067" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> debet A, 2, 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">esse major
et dominus vocari? An non invenitur inter nos melior,
qui et dignior sit dominari?</HI>  Ah! mala mens, malus
animus! Quod ruminant sobrii, palam faciunt ebrii.
Nam iniquitas eorum ut <NOTE N="1068" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  incaluit et assumpsit cornua
mero, capiunt dominum suum et crudeliter ligant,
atque nudum et resupinum per brachia et pedes
ligneis <NOTE N="1069" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> ligneis
 <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  clavis affigunt humi, et saltant saltu
 <NOTE N="1070" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ludentes militari, saltantes in equis trans corpus
sui <NOTE N="1071" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omittunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  heri <NOTE N="1072" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> eri  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  heri  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. man.</HI>  1.</NOTE> . Quod videns unus de conversis <NOTE N="1073" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> suis  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit.</HI>  3.</NOTE> 
nomine Dovora <NOTE N="1074" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Hovora 2 <SUP>a</SUP> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic deinceps.</HI>  Dowora 4.</NOTE> , velociter currens in Pragam,

 <POEM COM="0104"><L>Quod factum fuerat ducis <NOTE N="1075" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> duci 2.</NOTE>  nunciavit <NOTE N="1076" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> nunctat A, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  amicis:</L></POEM> 

et eadem hora <NOTE N="1077" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> ora  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI> 
hora 1.</NOTE>  deducit eos ad turpe bravium sine
mora. Quos <NOTE N="1078" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Quod 4.</NOTE>  ubi <NOTE N="1079" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2</NOTE>  viderunt iniquitatis operarii
 <COL N="0104B"></COL> armatos super se repente irruere, diffugiunt ut vespertiliones
per silvarum latebras <NOTE N="1080" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> tenebras A.</NOTE> . At illi, ut
invenerunt <NOTE N="1081" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> viderunt 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ducem male muscis laceratum, seminecem,
nam <NOTE N="1082" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  ut examen apum, sic ascendebat
agmen muscarum super corpus nudum, solventes
eum et vehiculo ponentes deferunt Wissegrad
 <NOTE N="1083" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Wisegrad
1, Wissograd 2.</NOTE>  in urbem. Servo autem Dovorae, omni laude
digno ducis amico, talis gratia redditur <NOTE N="1084" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  pro
merito. Nam voce <NOTE N="1085" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">falso repetit</HI>  1. pro merito.</NOTE>  praeconica <NOTE N="1086" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> praeconia A, 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  indicitur ubique
per fora, ut quam ipse Dovora tam ejus proles
postera, sit inter nobiles et ingenuos <NOTE N="1087" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> ducis amicos
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addit corr.</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  in aeternum
et ultra. Insuper dant ei et dignitatem venatoriam,
quae pertinet ad curtem Stebecnam <NOTE N="1088" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Stebecznam 2, Sthecnam 3, Stbecnam, 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <NOTE N="(387)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0104" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0104D"></COL> Zbecna in circulo Sacensi.</NOTE> , quam ex tunc et usque modo per generationes
ejus possident nepotes.</P> <P COM="0104"><COL N="0104C"></COL> 35 Dum haec geruntur in Boemia, dux Mesco
veniens cum valida manu Polonica invasit urbem
Pragam, et per duo spacia annorum, scilicet anno
dom. inc. 1000, anno dom. inc. 1001 obtinuit
eam <NOTE N="(388)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0104" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0104D"></COL> Annis 1003 et 1004 tenuit Pragam dux Pooniae,
vid. Annal. Quedlinburgenses et Thietmar.
VI, 9.</NOTE> . Sed Wissegrad <NOTE N="1089" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> Wissehrad 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  urbs duci suo fidelis
 <NOTE N="1090" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0103" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0103"></COL> fideliter
3.</NOTE>  mansit imperterrita et inexpugnabilis. Hisdem
 <COL N="0105A"></COL> <NOTE N="1091" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> isdem 1.</NOTE>  vero diebus idem <NOTE N="1092" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> i,  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu</HI>  isdem A.</NOTE>  dux Mesco mittit legatos
ad imperatorem, dans ei et promittens <NOTE N="1093" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> et promittens  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE>  infinitam
pecuniam, quo filium ducis Bolezlai, nomine Udalricum
 <NOTE N="1094" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Oaldricum 1.</NOTE>  qui erat ejus in obsequio, catenatum mitteret
 <NOTE N="1095" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> filius ducis Boleslai—catenatus mitteretur 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  in custodiam <NOTE N="(389)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Aliter rem se habuisse narrat Thietmar.
V, 19; non a Polonorum parte stetit Heinricus, sed
ex sules Bohemorum principes adjuvit.</NOTE> . O invictissima fames
auri! ubi est potentissimum jus Romani imperii?
Ecce possessor auri pressus ponderibus auri ducis
obtemperat jussis, et tortor fit ac carceris mancipator
auro corruptus imperator. Nec mirum, si ille
paruit duci <NOTE N="1096" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> ducis suasionibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> , e  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al.
man.</HI></NOTE> : cum nostris temporibus <NOTE N="(390)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Anno 1110; cfr. infra III, 32.</NOTE> 
Wacek <NOTE N="1097" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Wacec 1, Wack 2, 2 <SUP>a</SUP>  Wak 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Vecek 3.</NOTE> , sub mola rusticana natus, tertium Heinricum
 <NOTE N="(391)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Quintus est Heinricus.</NOTE>  regem potentissimum—o indignum
 <NOTE N="1098" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> ob indignum 2, o dignum 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE>  facinus <NOTE N="1099" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> scelus 4,
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> !—catena aurea ut molossum traxit
in Boemiam; et quod jubet famulorum famulus,
paret dominorum dominus, atque Borivoy <NOTE N="1100" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Udalricum  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP>   <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  5.</NOTE>  ducem
 <COL N="0105B"></COL> justi tenacem <NOTE N="(392)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Hor., od. III, 3, 1.</NOTE> , virum veracem, usque ad genua
compeditum rex mittit in custodiam, ceu iniquum
 <NOTE N="1101" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> inimicum  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu superscr.</HI>  iniquum A.</NOTE>  hominem et mendacem. Sed haec in suo <NOTE N="1102" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al manu superscr.</HI> 
A.</NOTE>  loco
plenius exarabuntur stilo.</P> <P COM="0105">36. Factum <NOTE N="1103" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> actum 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>  est autem anno dom. ine 1002
 <NOTE N="(393)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Anno 1004.</NOTE>  jam Christo Boemos respiciente <NOTE N="1104" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> s s  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al manu</HI>  1.</NOTE> , et sancto
Wencezlao suis auxiliante, incertum est nobis,
utrum clam fuga elapsus an jussu imperatoris dimissus,
dux Oudalricus <NOTE N="(394)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Thietmaro teste V, 9, Iaromirus erat qui
Pragam expugnavit.</NOTE>  rediens in <NOTE N="1105" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> ad A, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>  patriam,
intrat munitissimum <NOTE N="1106" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> invictissimum 3.</NOTE>  castrum, nomine Drevic
 <NOTE N="1107" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Drevis 3, Drewic 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(395)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> Situm erat inter Rocow et Kornhaus, Palacky
I, 259.</NOTE> , unde militem mittit <NOTE N="1108" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> mittit mil. A.</NOTE>  sibi fidelem, et ammonet,
quo intrans urbem Pragam per noctem clangore
 <NOTE N="1109" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> clangorem 2.</NOTE>  bucinae perterrefaciat incautum hostem.
Mox fidelis cliens jussa facit, et ascendens noctu in
media urbe eminenciorem locum, qui dicitur <NOTE N="1110" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> qui dicitur  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0105C"></COL> Zizi <NOTE N="1111" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Zizi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">cum punctis super</HI>  z  <HI REND="ITALIC">utrumque</HI>  2. Sizi 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , Zizi 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Corr. in margine addit:</HI>  modo Strahow vocitatur. Zicis
4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(396)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui nunc Strahovia dicitur.</HI>  Pulkawa.</NOTE> , tuba intonat et clara voce clamans
ingeminat <NOTE N="(397)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105D"></COL> In carmine populari  <HI REND="ITALIC">Udalrich und Jarmir,</HI> 
p. 155:

 <POEM COM="0105"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Geht ein Hirt als früh der Morgen dämmert,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Ruft hinauf, dass man das Thor ihm öffne.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Hört des Hirten lauten Ruf die Wache,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Oeffnet ihm das Thor am Moldaustrome.</HI></L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0106D"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Auf die Brücke tritt der Hirt, laut bläster,</HI> —
Teste Thietmaro campanis Wissegradensibus seditionis
signum datum est.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fugiunt</HI> <NOTE N="1112" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> fugiunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">semel</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">fugiunt Polonii</HI> <NOTE N="1113" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Poloni 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">confusi
 <COL N="0106A"></COL> turpiter, irruite, irruite armati Boemi acriter.</HI>  Ad
quam vocem irruit super eos formido et pavor,
quod erat mira Dei permissio et sancti Wencezlai
intercessio. Diffugiunt omnes, alius oblitus sui,
et <NOTE N="1114" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  armorum, nudus nudum insilit <NOTE N="1115" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> in  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  A.</NOTE>  equum et
fugit, alius ut dormivit, etiam <NOTE N="1116" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> et 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  3.</NOTE>  sine bracis <NOTE N="1117" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> braccis  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE> 
accelerat fugam. Fugientesque nonnulli praecipitantur
de ponte, quia pons erat interruptus ad insidias
hostibus: aliis fugientibus per <NOTE N="1118" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> per  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  praeruptam viam,
viam, quod vulgo dicitur per caudam urbis, in arta
posterula prae angustia exitus ibi innumeris oppressis
 <NOTE N="(398)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0106" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0106D"></COL> In carmine populari, l. l., 

 <POEM COM="0106"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Schreck ergreift die Polenkrieger alle:</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Ha, die Polen greifen nach den Waffen,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Ha, die Grafen führen mächt'ge Streiche!</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Und die Polen sprengen hierhin, dorthin,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Rennen im Gedräng' zum Thor durch Gräben,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Rennen, rennen vor den tapfern Streichen.</HI></L></POEM></NOTE> , 

vix ipse dux Mesco cum paucis evasit.
Sicque fuit, ut solet fieri, quando homines fugiunt
 <NOTE N="1119" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> prae t, f, A.</NOTE>  prae timore—etiam ad motum aurae pavent, et
ipse pavor timorem sibi auget,—ita, hos <NOTE N="1120" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> ita ut hos  <HI REND="ITALIC">eraso</HI>  ut A, ut hos 1, ita
homines 2, ita hos  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  nemine
 <COL N="0106B"></COL> persequente <NOTE N="1121" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> prosequente 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  3.</NOTE> , videbantur eis saxa et parietes
post se clamare et fugientes persequi. Postera
luce dux <NOTE N="1122" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> dux l, A.</NOTE>  Oudalricus <NOTE N="1123" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Odaldicus 1.</NOTE>  intrat urbem Pragam,
et isdem <NOTE N="1124" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> His 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>  familiaribus inimicis, de quibus supra
retulimus, fraudulenter suggerentibus <NOTE N="(399)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0106" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0106D"></COL> Gente Wrissovici, cfr I, 34.</NOTE> , fratrem
suum Iaromir tercia die privat lumine <NOTE N="(400)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0106" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0106D"></COL> Octo annos Iaromirus Bohemiae regnum
tenuit, anno demum 1012 a fratre expulsus, lumine
a 1034 privatus est. Thietmar. VI, 45, et Ann. Hildesheim.</NOTE> .
Huic ex legitimo matrimonio non est nata soboles
propter infecunditatem conjugis; sed ex quadam
femina nomine Bozena <NOTE N="1125" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Boziena 2.</NOTE> , quae fuit Cresinae <NOTE N="1126" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Kresine 1, 2, Krezmae 3, Krizine 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,
filium praestantissimae formae suscepit, quem Bracizlau
 <NOTE N="1127" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> Brzieczislaum 2, Bratizlau 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Brecislaum
3, Brazizlau 4 <SUP>a</SUP> , Bratislaw 5.</NOTE>  appellari fecit <NOTE N="(401)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0106" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0106D"></COL> Cum Cosmae hoc post ducatum adeptum
factum esse videretur, Udalrici nuptiae cum Bozena
sine dubio cum Dobnero post annum 1012 rejiciendae
sunt.</NOTE> . Nam quadam die de
venatu cum <NOTE N="1128" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  rediret per villam rusticanam, hanc,
quam praediximus, feminam ad puteum lavantem
pannos vidit, et intuitus eam a vertice usque ad
talos, hausit pectore ignes amoris non modicos.
 <COL N="0106C"></COL> Erat enim corporis ejus habitudo <NOTE N="1129" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0105" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0105"></COL> abitudo  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  albitudo 1, habitudo  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  insignis, nive
candidior, mollior cygno, nitidior ebore antiquo,
 <COL N="0107A"></COL> pulchrior saphiro. Hanc continuo mittens dux tulit
in sua, nec tamen antiqua solvit conubia, quia tunc
temporis, prout cuique placuit, binas vel ternas
conjuges <NOTE N="1130" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu in margine</HI>  A,  <HI REND="ITALIC">appositum</HI></NOTE>  habere licuit: nec nefas fuit viro
rapere alterius uxorem, et uxori alterius nubere
marito. Et quod nunc ascribitur pudori, hoc tunc
fuit magno dedecori <NOTE N="1131" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, decorari  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  decori A. decori 2, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">sed in posterioribus</HI>  de  <HI REND="ITALIC">erasum.</HI></NOTE> , si vir una conjuge aut
conjunx uno viro contenti viverent. Vivebant <NOTE N="1132" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> videbant A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  vivebant.</NOTE> 
enim quasi <NOTE N="1133" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia
manu appositum.</HI></NOTE>  bruta animalia, conubia habentes
communia.</P> <P COM="0107">37. Eodem anno

 <POEM COM="0107"><L>Caesar ab hoc mundo migravit tercius Otto,</L> <L>Vivat ut <NOTE N="1134" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  in coelis, ubi vivit quisque fidelis.</L></POEM> 

Huic successit filius ejus <NOTE N="1135" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> filius ejus  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(402)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107C"></COL> Quam longe Cosmas hic a veritate aberraverit,
neminem latet. Unde sequentem fabellam
hauserit nescio. Eamdem paulo ante Cosmam Leo
Ostiensis II, 47, non de S. Georgio sed de S. Laurentio
narravit, et post eum Adalbertus in Vita
S. Heinrici, c. 33. Ambo eamdem fere rem longe
aliis expresserunt verbis, ita ut nullum societatis
vinculum inter tres hos auctores intercedere possit.
At eamdem narratiunculam iisdem ut apud
Cosmam verbis legimus apud Crusium in Annalibus
 <COL N="0108C"></COL> Suevicis II, 186, qui haec testatur:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Haec in illo
magno volumine, quibus ecclesiastica et monastica
gens non tantum pro summa liberalitate grata esse
erga benefactorem voluit, sed etiam alios proceres et
divites ad similem et parem beneficentiam invitare.</HI> 
Sed monasterium ubi hic libellus scriptus sit tacet.
At cum Cosmae sermo rhythmicus in eodem fragmento
legatur, sine dubio non genuinum sed ex
ipsius Chronico est desumptum.</NOTE>  Heinricus imperator,
qui inter caetera <NOTE N="1136" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> cuncta 2.</NOTE>  quae fecit in vita sua pro
 <COL N="0107B"></COL> Christi nomine magnalia, construxit claustrum <NOTE N="1137" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> castrum 1, 2,
2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
in quodam monte, non modico sumptu empto a
possessore loci, nomine Pabo, unde traxit nomen
 <NOTE N="1138" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> n. tr. A.</NOTE>  Bamberk <NOTE N="1139" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> Babenberk 1, Pabenbergk 3, Babenberg 4.</NOTE> , quod est Pabonis mons. Ibi
etiam constituit <NOTE N="1140" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> construxit 1.</NOTE>  episcopatum, quem in tantum
ampliavit facultatibus et dignitatibus pontificalibus,
ut in tota orientali Francia non ultimum, sed secundum
post primum habeatur episcopium <NOTE N="1141" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> episcopatum
2.</NOTE> . Aedificavit
etiam <NOTE N="1142" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> aedificavit etiam—monasterio  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>  ibi et templum mirae magnitudinis
 <COL N="0108A"></COL> in honore <NOTE N="1143" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> honorem 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>  sanctae Mariae Virginis et sancti Georgii
Christi martiris, quod similiter in tantum adauxit
dotalibus ecclesiae et ornatibus auri et argenti
et coeteris regalibus <NOTE N="1144" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. regaliter
 <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  aparatibus, ut mihi videatur
de his tacere melius, quam dicere minus et
quam habeatur in re.</P> <P COM="0108">Utile de multis factum referam tamen <NOTE N="1145" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  unum.
Haud <NOTE N="1146" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  longe ab urbe praedicta quidam erat anachoreta
 <NOTE N="1147" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> anachorita 1.</NOTE> , sanctarum virtutum archimandrita,
ad <NOTE N="1148" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> at A.</NOTE>  quem imperator, saepe fingens quasi venatum
ire vellet, saepe <NOTE N="1149" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita additis verbis</HI>  ad venacionem
1. saepe ad venationem faciens A. 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">erronee</HI>  adventationem 2. ad venationem iter 3. ad
venatum ire vellet 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  faciens aliquam occasionem,
clam cum solo cliente veniebat et se ejus orationibus
commendabat. Hunc cum intellexisset caesar <NOTE N="1150" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> Heinricus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE> 
quia <NOTE N="1151" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> quod 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  causa orationis Hierosolymam <NOTE N="1152" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> Hierosolimam 1, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . Ierozolymam 2. 4.</NOTE>  ire vellet,
committit ei dominici corporis et sanguinis
 <COL N="0108B"></COL> calicem aureum, qui pro sui magnitudine, ut facile
possit a quoquam levari, duas ex utroque latere habuit
ansas, quod nos vulgo dicimus aures, quem ut
intingat <NOTE N="1153" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> intingat 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>  sub trina <NOTE N="1154" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> terna 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  mersione in Jordane,
ubi <NOTE N="1155" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> Jesus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE>  Christus baptizatus est a Johanne, praecipit
imperator et rogat, dans ei pecuniam quantum sufficeret
ad viam. Quid multa? Homo Dei vadit Ierosolimam,
jussa facit ter mergens calicem Jordanis in
unda <NOTE N="1156" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> undam 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> .</P> <POEM COM="0108"><L>Post rediens per Constantinopolim, transibat <NOTE N="1157" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> transiebat A. 4.</NOTE>  per Bulgariam.</L> <L>Ibi quidam erat <NOTE N="1158" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> er. quidam A.</NOTE>  heremita, sancta degens vita <NOTE N="1159" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> sanctam gerens vitam A. sanctam degens vitam 3.</NOTE> ,</L> <L>ad quem ille veniens Hierosolimita,</L> <L>post multa et dulcia atque sancta colloquia,</L> <L>suppliciter rogabat eum, ut pro incolomitate imperatoris Heinrici oraret Deum <NOTE N="1160" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> dominum A.</NOTE> .</L></POEM> <P COM="0108"><COL N="0107C"></COL> Ad quem ille:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non est,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro incolomitate
orandum, quia ex hac convalle lacrimarum translatus
est jam in requiem beatorum.</HI>  At ille instat et rogat,
ut sibi dicat, unde hoc sciat. Et ille:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Hac,</HI>  inquit,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">proxima nocte, dum nec adeo vigilarem nec omnino
dormirem, sustulit me alta visio ad magnum campum
valde planum et nimis latum atque jocundum; et vidi
 <COL N="0108C"></COL> ibi malignos spiritus teterrimos, quorum ex ore et
naribus exibat sulfurea</HI> <NOTE N="1161" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> fulgurea
1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">flamma, qui imperatorem
Heinrichum per</HI> <NOTE N="1162" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> et 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">barbam invitum et quasi ad judicium</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1163" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> et—judicium  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">trahebant</HI> <NOTE N="1164" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> habebant 3.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">alii collum ejus furcis ferreis
inpingentes</HI> <NOTE N="1165" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> urgentes A. 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . inpingentes
urgentes 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">laeti clamabant</HI> <NOTE N="1166" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> dicentes  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt corrector</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> : « <HI REND="ITALIC">Noster est,
noster est.» Quos a longe sequebatur sancta Maria
et</HI> <NOTE N="1167" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0107" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0107"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">sanctus Georgius, quasi tristes et quasi eripere
 <COL N="0109A"></COL> eum volentes et cum eis litigantes, donec suspensa est
in medio campo trutina, cujus capacitas lacior fuit
quam duo milliaria</HI> <NOTE N="1168" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> milia 1.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad sinistram maligna pars
magna et immensa pondera et innumerabilia, quae
sunt</HI> <NOTE N="1169" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> quae sunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mala opera, inponebant. At contra sanctum
Georgium vidi monasterium magnum cum toto claustro
inponere, vidi aureas cruces preciosis lapidibus
graves, vidi tot plenaria gemmis et auro grandia, vidi
candelabra</HI> <NOTE N="1170" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. cand. argentea A. 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aurea et turibula atque pallia innumera</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1171" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et quicquid boni rex in vita fecerat. Sed
adhuc maligna pars praeponderabat et clamabat:
«Noster est, noster est</HI> <NOTE N="1172" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> noster est  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  1.</NOTE> .»  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tunc sancta Maria
accepit aureum calicem magnum de manu sancti
Georgii, et concutiens ter caput inquit: «Certe</HI> <NOTE N="1173" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">non vester, sed noster est</HI> <NOTE N="1174" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ;»  <HI REND="ITALIC">et cum magna indignatione
 <COL N="0109B"></COL> projecit calicem ad parietem ecclesiae, et</HI> <NOTE N="1175" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> ubi 3.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">fracta est una</HI> <NOTE N="1176" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> pars  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ansa calicis. Ad cujus tinnitum</HI> <NOTE N="1177" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> tremitum
3.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">mox evanuit agmen ignitum</HI> <NOTE N="1178" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et accepit sancta
Maria per manum dexteram et sanctus Georgius per
sinistram imperatorem</HI> <NOTE N="1179" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> Henricum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et eduxerunt</HI> <NOTE N="1180" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> duxerunt A. 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">secum,
ut credo, in coelestem</HI> <NOTE N="1181" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> patriam vel hab. A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">habitationem.</HI>  At ille Hierosolimita
corde revolvens ea quae dicta sunt, descendit
ad sarcinas et invenit fractam calicis ansam,
sicut praedixerat heremita. Qui usque hodie magni
miraculi pro testimonio habetur Bamberk sancti
Georgii <NOTE N="1182" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> martiris 4.</NOTE>  in monasterio <NOTE N="1183" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> in ecclesia S. Georgii A.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0109">Anno dominicae incarnationis 1003. Hic interfecti
sunt Wrissovici <NOTE N="1184" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> Wrisevici 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell. ut supra.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(403)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109C"></COL> Sine dubio crudelissima est illa clades Boleslavi
III jussu perpetrata, quam retulit Thietmarus
V, 18.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0109">38. Anno dominicae incarnationis 1004 <NOTE N="1185" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> sanctus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> . Benedictus
cum sociis suis martirizatus est <NOTE N="1186" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> quinque fratres martyrizati sunt 3.</NOTE> . Temporibus
 <COL N="0109C"></COL> <NOTE N="1187" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">sequentia omnia usque</HI>  atque Johannes
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5.</NOTE>  Henrici <NOTE N="1188" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> Heinridi 1.</NOTE>  imperatoris, qui post Ottonem
 <COL N="0110A"></COL> tercium rexit Romanum imperium, in partibus Poloniae
quinque fuere monachi et heremitae, veri <NOTE N="1189" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> viri A. 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE> 
Israelitae, Benedictus, Matheus, Johannes, Ysaac,
Cristinus <NOTE N="1190" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> Crispinus 3.</NOTE> , et sextus Barnabas: quorum non est
inventus in ore dolus nec in manibus pravum opus.
Horum de vita patrum scripturus multa, malui
pauca, quia semper dulcius sumitur quae parcius
apponitur esca <NOTE N="(404)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0110" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0110C"></COL> De iisdem viris sanctis egit Petrus Damiani
in Vita S. Romualdi supra SS. t. IV, p. 852.</NOTE> . Erat enim eorum <NOTE N="1191" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">appositum.</HI></NOTE>  conversatio
laudabilis, Deo acceptabilis, hominibus admirabilis
et eam sectari volentibus imitabilis <NOTE N="1192" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">quae sequuntur, usque ad verba:</HI>  Passi sunt autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt 3. Post verba tamen</HI>  sectari volentibus imitabilis
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addit:</HI>  Hactenus haec.</NOTE> .
Nam ad <NOTE N="1193" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> ob A.</NOTE>  hoc merita sanctorum <NOTE N="1194" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> eorum A.</NOTE>  ammiramur
 <NOTE N="1195" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> amiramur 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , ut eos imitando ipsi ammirabiles reddamur.
Hos quippe viros quinque non <NOTE N="1196" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Hunc locum ita dedit cod.</HI>  A.
Hos quippe viros V prudentibus virginibus oleo habundantibus misericordiae et eos ( <HI REND="ITALIC">expunctum</HI> ) non ( <HI REND="ITALIC">alia
manu superscriptum</HI> ) incongrue equipparare possumus sive V portionibus (onibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">expunct. superscr.</HI>  tibus)
probaticae piscine quia, etc.</NOTE>  incongrue
aequipparare possumus sive quinque porticibus probaticae
piscinae, sive quinque prudentibus virginibus
 <COL N="0110B"></COL> oleo habundantibus misericordiae <NOTE N="1196" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Hunc locum ita dedit cod.</HI>  A.
Hos quippe viros V prudentibus virginibus oleo habundantibus misericordiae et eos ( <HI REND="ITALIC">expunctum</HI> ) non ( <HI REND="ITALIC">alia
manu superscriptum</HI> ) incongrue equipparare possumus sive V portionibus (onibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">expunct. superscr.</HI>  tibus)
probaticae piscine quia, etc.</NOTE> , quia pauperes
ipsi pauperibus Christi, quos in suis confovebant
mansionibus <NOTE N="1197" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> eis  <HI REND="ITALIC">add</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , prout poterant, subministrabant
misericordiae sumptibus. Ipsis autem virtus talis erat
abstinentiae, ut alius bis, alius semel in sabbato,
nullus tamen dietim <NOTE N="1198" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> dictim 1.</NOTE>  sumeret cibum. Cibus autem
eis <NOTE N="1199" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> erat  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  holus propriis elaboratum manibus;
panem raro habuere, sed piscem <NOTE N="1200" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> pisces 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  nunquam, legumina
aut <NOTE N="1201" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> autem 1.</NOTE>  milium non <NOTE N="1202" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  nisi in <NOTE N="1203" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  pascha <NOTE N="1204" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> aut pentecosten  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
sumere licuit, lympham incorruptam, et hanc libant
ad mensuram, carnis esca eis abhominabilis <NOTE N="1205" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> habom. 1.</NOTE>  et
feminae visus execrabilis. Vestis hyrta et aspera <NOTE N="1206" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI> 
A.</NOTE> ,
contexta de cauda et equinis <NOTE N="1207" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> dequinis 1.</NOTE>  jubis. In lectulo
lapis pro sustentaculo capitis, et matta pro lectisternio,
et haec vetus nimis et singularis

 <POEM COM="0110"><L>Nec fuit ulla quies, stant tota nocte lugentes</L> <L>Tam proprium quam plebiculae scelus atque reatum.</L> <L><COL N="0109C"></COL> Nunc sonant pectora crebris tunsionibus livida,</L> <L>nunc <NOTE N="1208" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> tunc  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  nunc 1.</NOTE>  sudant <NOTE N="1209" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> fundant 1.</NOTE>  corpora <NOTE N="1210" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> pectora A.</NOTE>  innumeris genuflexionibus <NOTE N="1211" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. alia manu</HI>  A.</NOTE>  fessa,</L> <L>nunc manibus expansis et oculis erectis,</L> <L>vivat ut in coelis precibus unusquisque instat anhelis.</L> <L>Nunquam locuti sunt ad invicem, nisi venientem ad hospitem.</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0109C"></COL> et ad hunc paucis. Vere legis factores, non auditores
erant, vere semetipsos cum viciis et concupiscentiis
mundi crucifigentes, et crucem Christi mente et
corpore bajulantes, gratum Deo sacrificium non
 <COL N="0110C"></COL> ex <NOTE N="1212" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu</HI>  A.</NOTE>  pecore alieno, sed ex corpore proprio offerebant
 <NOTE N="1213" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0109" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0109"></COL> offerrebant A.</NOTE> , quia cottidie vicissim vapulabant. Talis
enim
 <COL N="0111A"></COL> Mos erat illorum simul unaquaque <NOTE N="1214" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> unaquaeque 1, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4.</NOTE>  dierum <NOTE N="1215" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> die A.</NOTE> ,
Post primam dorsum mollirier <NOTE N="1216" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> mollirier 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in textu. Alia manus, ducta per vocem hanc
linea, in margine adscripsit</HI>  detegunt. Mollire 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  usque deorsum.
In faciemque cadens ad fratrem frater <NOTE N="1217" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> frater fratri  <HI REND="ITALIC">omisso</HI>  ad 2.</NOTE>  aiebat:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Si parcis peccas, cum tangis, ne michi parcas,</HI> 
 <COL N="0112A"></COL> et stans cum flagello respondit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sicut
Vis, fiat,</HI>  Christumque rogat, fratremque flagellat,
dicens:

 <POEM COM="0112"><L INDENT=1><HI REND="ITALIC">Haec per facta</HI> <NOTE N="1218" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> perfecta 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . praefata
4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">pius solvat tua crimina</HI> <NOTE N="1219" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> tormina 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Christus,</HI></L> <L INDENT=1>Atque cadens iterum praebet sua terga vicissim.</L> <L INDENT=1>Nec  <HI REND="ITALIC">Doluit, frater,</HI>  dum <NOTE N="1220" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> cum A.</NOTE>  fratrem verberat alter,</L> <L INDENT=1>Sed  <HI REND="ITALIC">Miserere mei Deus</HI>  aut  <HI REND="ITALIC">Benedicite</HI>  cantat.</L> <L INDENT=1>Nam suffert leviter patitur quod quisque libenter.</L> <L INDENT=1><COL N="0111A"></COL> Horum Deus ex alto prospectans pacientiam</L> <L INDENT=1>et vitae innocentiam, atque fidei et operis perseverantiam,</L> <L INDENT=1>cum jam laborum sanctorum suorum <NOTE N="1221" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> ipsorum  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  sanctorum suorum 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE></L> <L INDENT=1>mercedem reddere vellet et ut per viam mirabilem</L> <L><COL N="0111"></COL> eos ad patriam reduceret <NOTE N="1222" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> perduceret
2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  exultabilem.</L> <L><COL N="0111A"></COL> Dux Mesco audiens bonam famam eorum et conversationem sanctam,</L> <L>venit cum paucis, ut se commendaret hominibus sanctis.</L> <L>Et ut eorum <NOTE N="1223" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> cum A.</NOTE>  cognovit inopiam, dat eis magnam census copiam <NOTE N="(405)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111C"></COL> Secundum Romualdum aurum eis datum
erat, ut Romam profecti coronam regiam sibi a
summo pontifice impetrarent.</NOTE> ,</L> <L>scilicet marsupium centum marcis plenum</L> <L>Et accipiens ab eis fraternitatem, et orationum communitatem,</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0111B"></COL> laetus abiit ad suam aulam <NOTE N="1224" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> aulam curiam 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed expuncta vox</HI>  curiam.</NOTE>  multum <NOTE N="1225" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> multis 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  rogans et
commendans se, ut sui habeant memoriam. At illi
nesciunt <NOTE N="1226" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> nescientes A.</NOTE> , quid faciant <NOTE N="1227" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> facerent A.</NOTE>  de pecunia, quia tale
 <COL N="0112B"></COL> quid nunquam habuerant. Stant stupefacti, et quia
jam per dimidium annum nihil fuerant ad invicem
locuti, unus ex illis aperuit os, et ait:

 <POEM COM="0112"><L><COL N="0111"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Est laqueus</HI> <NOTE N="1228" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> laqueus est A. 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mortis argenti pondus et auri,</HI></L> <L><COL N="0111B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">et quibus super</HI> <NOTE N="1229" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> semper 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">habundat mordax crumena,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">his non facile patebunt loca elysey amoena,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">sed horrore</HI> <NOTE N="1230" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> horroris 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">plena infernalis poena</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">illos cruciabit</HI> <NOTE N="1231" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> cruciabat 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in Ethna</HI> <NOTE N="1232" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> Hetna 1.</NOTE> .</L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nimirum haec est temptatio humani generis inimici,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">ut nos faciat inimicos Christi.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nam qui amicus est mundi, inimicus constituetur</HI> <NOTE N="1233" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> est A. constituitur 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Dei</HI> <NOTE N="1234" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">loco erasi verbi</HI>  1.</NOTE> .</L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Deo namque</HI> <NOTE N="1235" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> autem  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  namque A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">contradicunt, qui ejus mandata non custodiunt.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nam Deus dixit: «Nemo potest</HI> <NOTE N="1236" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> Non potestis A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">duobus dominis servire,»</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">et quasi exponens adjunxit: «Non potestis Deo servire et mammonae</HI> <NOTE N="(405*)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0112" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0112C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Matth.</HI>  VI, 24.</NOTE> .»</L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Jam mammonae erimus servi, qui hactenus fuimus parsymoniae liberi</HI></L> <L><COL N="0111"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">An non ad motum aurae portans aurum pavebit?</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">An non cantabit vacuus coram latrone viator</HI> <NOTE N="1237" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> cor. latr. viator A.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(406)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0112" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0112C"></COL> Juvenal., sat. X, 22.</NOTE> .</L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nonne multociens ad nos latrones venerunt</HI> <NOTE N="1238" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> veniunt 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> .</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0111C"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI> <NOTE N="1239" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ob quam rem nos interficerent non invenientes?
aliquando plagis nobis impositis, aliquando benedictionibus
acceptis abierunt? Certe jam volat fama per mundum
nos diligere mundum et ea quae sunt mundi. Clamat
contra nos et haec ipsa, quae nunquam scit tacere
pecunia, et jam jamque aderit improba manus latronum
in janua, quia quod faciunt domini sciunt plurimi, quin</HI> 
 <COL N="0112C"></COL> <NOTE N="1240" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> etiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">potius ejiciatur cicius mortis</HI> <NOTE N="1241" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> mortes A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fomentum, mali
nutrimentum, animae detrimentum, et referatur ad eum
cujus est hoc argentum.</HI>  Et mittunt unum de fratribus,
cui nomen Barnabas, qui semper exteriores
tractabat causas, ut haec <NOTE N="1242" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ex parte fratrum referat
duci:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Licet nos peccatores et indigni sumus</HI> <NOTE N="1243" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0111" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0111"></COL> indignissimi A. simus 4.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">tamen vestri memoriam in nostris orationibus habemus
 <COL N="0113A"></COL> continuam. Argentum nunquam habuimus, nec habere
volumus. Dominus enim noster Jesus Christus a nobis
non argentum, sed bonae operationis duplex exigit talentum
Monachus si habet obulum, non valet obulum.
Ecce quod tuum est accipe argentum, nobis illicita
possidere non est licitum</HI> <NOTE N="1244" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> licet A.</NOTE> . Illo abeunte ducis ad
curiam, mox in prima noctis vigilia affuit manus
inimica, et irrumpentes valvas <NOTE N="1245" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> walvas 1.</NOTE>  domus subito,
inveniunt eos cantantes et psallentes Domino. Quorum
adactis jugulo gladiis inquiunt:

 <POEM COM="0113"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Vivere si vultis cum pace bona, quod habetis</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Argentum nobis date nunc et parcite vobis.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Scimus enim vere vos censum regis habere.</HI></L></POEM></P> <P COM="0113">At illi teste Deo jurant, censumque negant constanter
et aiunt:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Pecunia, quam quaeritis, jam est
 <COL N="0113B"></COL> in camera ducis, quia non fuit necessaria nobis. Quod
si non creditis, ecce domus nostra, quaerite quantum
placet vobis, tantummodo nolite male facere nobis</HI> <NOTE N="1246" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> quicquam  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  A.</NOTE> .
At illi rigidiores saxis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non est opus,</HI>  inquiunt,  <HI REND="ITALIC">verbis,
aut nobis reddite ducis pecuniam, aut</HI> <NOTE N="1247" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">diram
mortis subibitis sentenciam,</HI>  et statim crudeliter eos
ligaverunt et per totam noctem diversis poenis affecerunt,
ad ultimum in ore gladii simul omnes interfecerunt.
Sicque furor impiorum transvexit eos ad
regna polorum. Passi sunt autem hi fratres quinque,
Benedictus, Matheus, Ysaac, Cristinus atque Johannes
 <NOTE N="1248" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">quinque haec nomina
propria desunt</HI>  3.</NOTE>  anno dominicae incarnationis 1004, 3 <NOTE N="1249" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> II. 2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Id. Nov. A.</NOTE>  Idus
Novembris.</P> <P COM="0113">39. Anno dominicae incarnationis 1005.</P> <P COM="0113">Anno dominicae incarnationis 1006 <NOTE N="1250" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">quae sequuntur, priori anno in</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP>   <HI REND="ITALIC">annexa sunt.</HI></NOTE>  princeps
 <COL N="0113C"></COL> Hemma, feminei sexus gemma, febre correpta <NOTE N="1251" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> correcta
1.</NOTE> ,
a vinculis carnis est <NOTE N="1252" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  erepta. Cujus epitaphium
his versiculis aut vidi, aut vidisse me <NOTE N="1253" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> me  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu 1. omissum</HI>  2.</NOTE>  memini
editum <NOTE N="1254" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  3.</NOTE> :
Quae fuit ut <NOTE N="1255" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> in 1.</NOTE>  gemma, vilis jacet en cinis Hemma.</P> <P COM="0113">Dic, precor,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Huic animae da veniam, Domine.</HI></P> <LIST COM="0113"><ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1007.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1008.*</ITEM> <ITEM>*Stephanus rex Ungarorum claruit. 2. 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1009.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1010.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1011.**</ITEM> <ITEM>** Dedicatio Babinbergensis ecclesiae 2. 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1012.</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="0114A"></COL> Anno dominicae incarnationis 1013.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1014.***</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1015. †</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1016.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1017. 4</ITEM></LIST> <P COM="0114">Junii
 <NOTE N="1256" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1.
2. IV. Id Junii  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(407)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113C"></COL> Consentit Thietmarus VII, 41, et Necrologium
Bohemicum.</NOTE>  obiit Teadagus, quartus episcopus <NOTE N="1257" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> sanctae  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
Pragensis ecclesiae. Fuit autem hic <NOTE N="1258" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4</NOTE>  Teadagus
sancti praesulis Adalberti successor <NOTE N="1259" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">in margine 1. al. man.</HI></NOTE>  idoneus,
corpore virgineus, moribus aureus, actibus purpureus,
sui antecessoris sequens vestigia, commissae
plebis persequens flagicia, et si non corpore, mente
tamen tulit martirium: nec obiit more <NOTE N="1260" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> morte
1.</NOTE>  hominum,
 <COL N="0114B"></COL> sed secutus Dominum in pace in idipsum dormit
 <NOTE N="1261" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> dormivit 4 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et requiescit, cui <NOTE N="1262" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> amen  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  cui 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . eodem anno 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  anno dom. inc. 1018
 <NOTE N="1263" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> mill. XIX. 1.</NOTE>  successit Heccardus <NOTE N="1264" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> Eccardus
1. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">a recentiori manu correctum</HI>  Erhardus. Ekkardus 2. Eckardus 4.</NOTE>  praesul <NOTE N="(408)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113C"></COL> Antea abbas Nienburgensis. Consecratus est
die 6 Oct. Thietmar. VII, 48.</NOTE> .

 <LIST COM="0114"><ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1019 <NOTE N="1265" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">desideratur haec lin.</HI>  1.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1020.</ITEM></LIST></P> <P COM="0114">40. Interea natus ducis Bracizlaus, de puericia
transcendens in juventutem, ibat de virtute in virtutem;
cui prae caeteris prosperitas operis <NOTE N="1266" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> opis 3.</NOTE> , proceritas
corporis et formae pulchritudine, ac virium
 <NOTE N="1267" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> virtutum 1.</NOTE>  sapientiaeque magnitudo, in adversis fortitudo,
in prosperis temperata inerat mansuetudo. Hisdem
temporibus Teuthonicis in partibus fuit quidam comes
valde potens, cognomine albus <NOTE N="1268" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> Albertus 3.</NOTE>  Otto, sanguine
de regio prodiens stemmate patrio. Unica huic
 <COL N="0114C"></COL> erat gnata <NOTE N="1269" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> nata A. 2, 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , nomine Judita <NOTE N="(409)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113C"></COL> Erat filia Heinrici et soror Ottonis marchionis
de Suinford. Vide stemma genealogicum quod
 <COL N="0114C"></COL> dedit Schwarz in adnotatione 108 ad Cosmam. Vide
etiam Pubitschka III, 265.</NOTE> . pulchritudine</P> <P COM="0114">Sub Phebo cunctis quae sunt praelata puellis:
quam bonus pater et ejus optima mater, quo addisceret
psalterium, tradiderant in caenobium quod dicitur
Zuinprod <NOTE N="1270" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> Zuinprid 1. Zumbrod 3. Zuinbrod
4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(410)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0114" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0114C"></COL> I. e. Suinford, ubi sanctimonialium monasterium
ab Eila, Judithae avia, conditum fuisse probat
Ann. Saxo ad a. 1015.</NOTE> , loci situ et moenibus munitissimum.
Sed quae <NOTE N="1271" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  turres, quamvis altissimae,
aut quae moenia firmissima <NOTE N="1272" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> fortissima 4.</NOTE>  amori resistere et
amantem possunt excludere <NOTE N="1273" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> extrudere 2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> ?</P> <P COM="0114">Omnia vincit amor <NOTE N="(411)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0114" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0114C"></COL> Virg., eclog. X, 69.</NOTE> : rex et dux cedit amori.
Igitur <NOTE N="1274" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> interea 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Bracizlaus, juvenum pulcherrimus, heros
acerrimus, multis referentibus audiens de nimia
pulchritudine et morum probitate ac generositate
parentelae supra dictae puellae, ultra non habebat spiritum
et intra semetipsum coepit cogitare, utrum eam
vi rapere <NOTE N="1275" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0113" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0113"></COL> capere A.</NOTE>  temptet, an dotalibus conubia paret.
 <COL N="0115A"></COL> Sed maluit viriliter agere quam supplicando colla
submittere. Perpendit enim innatam Teutonicis
superbiam, et quod semper tumido fastu habeant
despectui Sclavos et eorum linguam. Sed quanto fit
semper difficilis aditus ad amorem, tanto amanti
filius Veneris ignem <NOTE N="1276" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">verba</HI>  ignem—juvenis  <HI REND="ITALIC">desiderantur 2; manu recenti in margine apposita sunt.</HI></NOTE>  incutit validiorem. Fluctuat
 <NOTE N="1277" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> fluctuatque 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.</NOTE>  mens juvenis igne succensa Veneris
 <NOTE N="1278" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> cupidinis A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in 1. verbis</HI>  igne s. Ven.  <HI REND="ITALIC">manu coaeva superscriptum est</HI>  telo lesa cupidinis.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Eodem modo
in</HI>  2. 5. telo igne 4. telo igne,  <HI REND="ITALIC">subducta tamen voce</HI>  telo,  <HI REND="ITALIC">legit</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , velut ignibus aestuat Ethna. Et hanc <NOTE N="1279" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> ahuc. 1.</NOTE> 
apostropham <NOTE N="1280" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> apostrapham 3. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  eufonizat secum:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Aut ego conjugio
fungar egregio, aut ego</HI> <NOTE N="1281" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ludibrio mergar perpetuo,
fieri non poterit</HI> <NOTE N="1282" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> potuit 3.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut mea non fuerit Juditha, nobilibus
edita natalibus, virgo spectabilis, multum
amabilis, solis luce</HI> <NOTE N="1283" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> vice 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">clarior, vita mihi carior;
vivat ut superstes laus Deo sit perpes.</HI>  Et statim quos
inter <NOTE N="1284" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  suos novit manu promptiores et sibi fideliores,
 <COL N="0115B"></COL> jubet probatos et laboris patientiores aptari
equos, et fingit se ad imperatorem cito iturum et
cicius rediturum. Jussa viri faciunt, sed quid dominus
suus moliatur nesciunt. Mirantur inter se
quod tam celeriter vadunt, et quasi septem dierum
iter agentes, vice hospitum <NOTE N="1285" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> hospitii 3.</NOTE>  intrant praedicti
coenobii atrium. Interdixerat enim suis omnibus
ducis natus, ne alicui eum, quis vel <NOTE N="1286" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> et A. 2.</NOTE>  unde esset,
innotescerent, sed quasi unum ex ipsis se ipsum
haberent. Cedat Ithacus callido ingenio investigasse
natum Thethidis <NOTE N="1287" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> Tethidis 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Cheridis 3.
Thechidis 4. Tchechidis 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , <NOTE N="(412)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115C"></COL> Cfr. Statii Achill. II, 44.</NOTE>  nec se jactet <NOTE N="1288" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> jacet  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. recentiori manu</HI>  jactet 1.</NOTE>  Iliacus pastor
Tyndaridem <NOTE N="1289" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> i. Helenam  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">al.
manu.</HI></NOTE>  rapuisse Amiclis, quia hic juvenis
Bracizlaus ambos it prae <NOTE N="1290" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> praeit 3. 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et animositate et
au lacis facti immanitate. Nam postquam data est eis
ibi pernoctandi licentia, sicut lupus, quando obambulat
 <COL N="0115C"></COL> ovilia, quaerens qua parte irrumpat ut nitidam
rapiat agnam; sic et <NOTE N="1291" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> sicut 2. sic  <HI REND="ITALIC">omisso</HI>  et 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . 4.</NOTE>  heros Bracizlaus visu <NOTE N="1292" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> nisu 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
sagaci et animo illustri lustrans claustrum, vult vi
irrumpere sed non audet, quia secum tantam copiam
militum <NOTE N="1293" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  non habet. Forte fortuna affuit
dies festa, et ecce mille votis optata cum suis coaevulis
de claustro exit <NOTE N="1294" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> exiit 4.
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  virgo Juditha, sicut puellae
solebant <NOTE N="1295" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  tenellae ad vesperas pulsare campanas
 <COL N="0116A"></COL> in medio ecclesiae. Quam ut vidit audacissimus
raptor, sui prae gaudio factus <NOTE N="1296" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  immemor, ceu
lupus qui ex occulto irruit et rapit agnam, et conscius
facti fugit submittens caudam <NOTE N="1297" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> causam V 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed</HI>  s  <HI REND="ITALIC">erasum.</HI></NOTE> , petens
ulteriorem latebram, sic et ille rapta virgine fugit:
et ut venit ad portam, invenit eam catena <NOTE N="1298" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  molendinari
fune grossiori <NOTE N="1299" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  praestrictam et viam
exeundi praeclusam. Mox exempto gladio ut festucam
praecidit acuto, quae usque hodie cernitur sectio
fortissimi ictus pro testimonio. Caeteris autem sociis
id minime scientibus et adhuc in papilionibus manentibus,
ab irruentibus inimicis comprehensis,
aliorum erutis oculis et naribus abscisis, aliorum
manibus et pedibus truncatis, dux cum paucis et
virgine rapta per noctis vix evasit opaca. Rapta est
 <COL N="0116B"></COL> autem virgo Judita anno dominicae incarnationis
1021 <NOTE N="(413)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115C"></COL> Hunc annum a Cosma falso prolatum esse
sequentibus ipse probabit, quibus apparet Juditham
post Moraviam a Bohemis expugnatam raptam esse.
Moravia vero sine dubio eodem anno 1029 recepta
est, quo Conradus II imperator arma contra Polonos
movebat, quod probavit Dobner V, 156, et post eum
Roepell I, 166. De filio Bracizlai et Judithae anno
1031 nato cfr. infra.</NOTE> . Et ne daretur <NOTE N="1300" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> Et
ne justa A.</NOTE>  Teuthonicis justa
occasio calumpniandi Boemos, quasi, pro illata injuria,
ilico heros <NOTE N="1301" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  Bracizlaus cum nova <NOTE N="1302" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  nupta,
patre salutato duce Oudalrico <NOTE N="1303" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> Odaldrico 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic deinceps.</HI></NOTE> , recta via
proficiscitur in Moraviam <NOTE N="(414)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115C"></COL> Donatio quaedam apud Boczek cod. dipl.
Moraviae I, 111, sine notis chronologicis scripta est
 <HI REND="ITALIC">tempore quo dominus noster B. dux venit Olomucie
 <COL N="0116C"></COL> cum formosa sua contectali coram choro terrae suae
nobilium numeroso.</HI></NOTE> . Nam antea <NOTE N="1304" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> ante 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> 
pater sibi totam illam terram tradiderat in potestatem,
fugatis cunctis de civitatibus <NOTE N="1305" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> de civitatibus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Poloniis <NOTE N="1306" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> Polonis 1. 3.</NOTE> 
 <NOTE N="(415)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0116" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0116C"></COL> Non de Polonis solum, sed de Ungaris, qui
illis Moraviam eripuerant, Bracizlaum victoriam
reportasse, ipse testatur princeps ille in tabula quadam,
qua se ducem Moraviensem appellat apud
Boczek cod. dipl. Moraviae I, 112; sed desunt notae
chronologicae; actum est Olomuci. Quo loco Bracizlaum
a, 1031 cum conjuge sua et filiolo Spitigneo
habitasse probat alia tabula a. 1031 Boczek I, 114</NOTE> , ex quibus multos comprehensos, centenos et
centenos ordinatim catenatos vendi jusserat in
Ungariam et ultra; quia revera post obitum secundi
Bolezlai sicut urbem Pragam, ita totam Moraviam vi
obtinuerant Polonii,</P> <P COM="0116">Anno dominicae incarnationis 1022. in Polonia
 <COL N="0116C"></COL> facta est persecutio christianorum <NOTE N="1307" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> chr. pers. A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">nihil ad hunc annum</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(416)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0116" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0116C"></COL> Confirmat Necrologium Bohemicum.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0116">Anno dominicae incarnationis 1023. 6. Idus Augusti
Occardus <NOTE N="1308" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> Oggardus 2. Okkardus
2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Ekardus 3. Eccardus 4. Heccardus 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  quartus episcopus <NOTE N="1309" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> sanctae  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Pragensis
ecclesiae transivit <NOTE N="1310" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> transiit 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ab hac luce victurus perpete
vita <NOTE N="1311" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> perpetua V. A. perpetem vitam 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(417)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0116" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0116C"></COL> Hoc factum est anno 1034. post mortem
Miseconis II; cfr. Annales Hildesheim.</NOTE> . Fuit autem hic <NOTE N="1312" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4.</NOTE>  praesul <NOTE N="1313" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> Heccardus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  contra
potentes erectus, erga humiles et mansuetos <NOTE N="1314" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> mansuetus  <HI REND="ITALIC">omisso et</HI>  4.
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
pius <NOTE N="1315" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0115" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0115"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  3.</NOTE>  et modestus, facundissimus praedicator,
largus elemosinarum dator, dominicae familiae in
mensura tritici fidelis dispensator. Hic constituit ut
 <COL N="0117A"></COL> pro decimatione unusquisque, sive <NOTE N="1316" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> sive  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  potens sive
dives sive pauper, tantum qui de suo pheodo <NOTE N="1317" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE> 
vel allodio <NOTE N="1318" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> allidio 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  araturam haberet, duos modios quinque
palmarum et duorum digitorum, unum tritici et
alterum avenae episcopo solveret. Nam antea, sicut
primo episcopo Dethmaro <NOTE N="1319" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Diethmaro 1.</NOTE>  constitutum erat, pro
decimatione duos messis acervos dabant; dicimus
enim <NOTE N="1320" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A. 4.</NOTE>  acervum quinquaginta <NOTE N="1321" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  quinquaginta 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">videtur in suo codice fuisse</HI>  L  <HI REND="ITALIC">quod scriba legit</HI>  vel.</NOTE>  manipulos habentem.
Hujus post obitum Izo <NOTE N="1322" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Izzo 1. 2. 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  3.</NOTE>  obtinuit episcopium
 <NOTE N="1323" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> episcopatum A. 2. 3.</NOTE> , qui ordinatus est ab eodem anno <NOTE N="1324" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  4. Kal.
Januarii ab archiepiscopo Maguntino <NOTE N="1325" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> ab arch. Mog.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(418)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117C"></COL> Probant Annales Quedlinburg.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0117">41. Anno dominicae incarnationis 1024. 4. Idus
Julii obiit Heinrichus rex <NOTE N="1326" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> IV. Id, 4.
—rex  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  5. Theutonicorum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">transpositis aliquantum reliquis vocibus.</HI></NOTE> .</P> <LIST COM="0117"><ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1025. 15. Kal. Julii
obiit Boleslaus rex <NOTE N="1327" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> XV. Kal. I.—rex
 <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt 5. In</HI>  2  <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">subducto</HI>  rex  <HI REND="ITALIC">supra adscriptum est</HI>  dux.  <HI REND="ITALIC">In</HI>  4  <SUP>a</SUP> . rex  <HI REND="ITALIC">recentius erasum.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(419)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117C"></COL> Cfr. Roepell Gesch. Polens I, 162.</NOTE> .</ITEM> <ITEM><COL N="0117B"></COL> Anno dominicae incarnationis 1026*.</ITEM> <ITEM>(*Conradus rex Romae consecratur. 2, 2a., 2b.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1027.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1028.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1029.</ITEM></LIST> <P COM="0117">Anno dominicae incarnationis 1030. Hoc anno dux
Bracizlaus <NOTE N="1328" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Bolezlaus 1.</NOTE>  magna caede prostravit Ungaros et
terram eorum usque ad urbem Strigoniam <NOTE N="(420)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117C"></COL> Gran, ubi Grana in Danubium exundat. Illud
videtur bellum esse de quo vide supra not. 17.</NOTE> 
devastavit. Eodem anno 3. Kal. <NOTE N="1329" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. Kal.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  Id. A.</NOTE>  Februarii
Izo <NOTE N="(421)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117C"></COL> Consentit Necrologium Bohomicum.</NOTE> , quintus episcopus Pragensis ecclesiae,

 <POEM COM="0117"><L>Transit <NOTE N="1330" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> transiit 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ab hoc mundo bravio fruiturque <NOTE N="1331" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> frugiturque A.</NOTE> 
jocundo.</L></POEM> 

Hic fuit nobilis genere, sed nobilior opere, qui prior
fecit quae facienda praecepit. Nam nulli magis est
nota propria sedes, quam sibi carcer et infirmorum
 <COL N="0117C"></COL> erant aedes. Nec eum <NOTE N="1332" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> enim 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  latuit quot hominum capita
vitae sint reddita,

 <POEM COM="0117"><L>Vel quot mors animas ad furvas <NOTE N="1333" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> furias A. furnas 3.
4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  mitteret
umbras.</L></POEM> 

Praeterea solitus erat cottidie quater denos pauperes
pascere, quibus habunde procurans cibum et potum
ipse benedixit et ipse hilariter <NOTE N="1334" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> hylarum 1.</NOTE>  distribuit. Erat
enim et corporis ejus pulchritudo insignis, caput
capillo albius cigno, unde cognomen obtinuit, ut
diceretur albus atque blandus episcopus Izo. Post
hunc</P> <P COM="0117">Severus praesul successit in ordine sextus,
 <COL N="0118A"></COL> qui tempore juventutis mirae enituit decore agilitatis:
quia quotquot erant in curia ducis, omnes suis
praecellens obsequiis, sedulum suo domino et magis
gratum, quia <NOTE N="1335" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  quia 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  fidele, exhibebat servicium. Primus
enim fuit officiis <NOTE N="1336" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> iis  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  clericorum, nec minus
deditus studiis laicorum; semper aderat comes individuus
 <NOTE N="1337" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> individuis A.</NOTE>  duci in venationibus, primus enim
affuit in occisione silvatici apri, et abscidens ejus
 <NOTE N="1338" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
A.</NOTE>  caudam, purgat et parat, ut ducem velle norat,
paratamque venienti domino ad vescendum donat,
unde dux Oudalricus saepe sibi fertur dixisse:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">O Severe, dico tibi vere, pro hoc tam dulci edulio dignus
es episcopio.</HI>  His atque hujusmodi studiis habuit
gratiam ducis et placuit universis.</P> <LIST COM="0118"><ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1031 <NOTE N="1339" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> 1032 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  sanctorum
 <COL N="0118B"></COL> apostolorum Petri et Pauli in natalicio ordinatus est
Severus episcopus a Maguntino archiepiscopo. Eodem
anno natus est Spitigneu <NOTE N="1340" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Zpitigneu 1. 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . Zpitigneus 4. Spitigneus 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">et sic porro.</HI></NOTE>  filius Bracizlai
ducis.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1032.**</ITEM> <ITEM>**) Initium Sazaviensis ecclesiae <NOTE N="1341" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Ad sequentem annum</HI> 
2  <SUP>b</SUP> : Factum est initium  <HI REND="ITALIC">etc.</HI></NOTE> . 2. 2a</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1033.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1034.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1035.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1036.</ITEM> <ITEM>Anno dominicae incarnationis 1037. obiit dux Bolezlaus
 <NOTE N="1342" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Bolezaus 1.</NOTE> , quem Mesco <NOTE N="1343" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Mesko 2. 4.  <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE>  lumine privarat <NOTE N="1344" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> privavit 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> .</ITEM></LIST> <P COM="0118">42. Eodem anno 5. Idus Novembris <NOTE N="(422)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0118" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0118C"></COL> De turpi ejus morte vid. Annal. Hildesheim.
1034.</NOTE>  dux
Oudalricus,</P> <P COM="0118"><COL N="0118C"></COL> linquens terrena captat coelestia regna <NOTE N="(423)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0118" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0118C"></COL> Extrema Udalrici fata non bene nota fuisse
Cosmae docent Annales Hildeshemenses.</NOTE> .
Tunc Iaromir, de quo supra meminimus <NOTE N="1345" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> mem. Iaromir
A.</NOTE> , lumine
orbus, cui dux Oudalricus destinaverat <NOTE N="1346" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> destinarat 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , ut degeret
 <NOTE N="1347" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">expunct. et al. man. superscr.</HI>  daretur A.</NOTE>  Liza <NOTE N="1348" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> Licza 1. Lisza 2. 4. Lizza 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(424)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0118" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0118C"></COL> Lvsa castrum.</NOTE>  in viculo <NOTE N="1349" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> . vinculo  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE> , audiens quod
frater suus ab hoc migrasset seculo, surgit diluculo,
et imperat ut se deducant ad urbem Pragam veiculo.
Quo cum pervenit, jam fratrem suum ad ecclesiam
delatum <NOTE N="1350" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> monasterium A. ecclesiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu in margine appositum.</HI>  in eccl.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI> 
2. 2  <SUP>b</SUP> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed corr. addidit</HI>  ad monasterium</NOTE>  sancti Georgii <NOTE N="1351" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> martyris  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  invenit, ad cujus
funus stans juxta feretrum, omnium circa astancium
movit et concussit <NOTE N="1352" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0117" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0117"></COL> convertit 3</NOTE>  corda hujusmodi elogii lamento:

 <POEM COM="0118"><L><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">Ei mihi! quid dicam, nisi saepius: Heu mihi! dicam!</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Hei</HI> <NOTE N="1353" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> Heri 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mihi! germane, hey dira conditio mortis amarae!</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Mortuus ecce jaces, nec ego nec tu modo gaudes.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Hujus terreni fugitivo</HI> <NOTE N="1354" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> fruituri 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">culmine regni.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nudius tercius</HI> <NOTE N="1355" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> concius 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dux nobilis, hodie truncus inmobilis,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">cras vermibus esca, post tenuis favilla</HI> <NOTE N="1356" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> et jam es  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et inanis eris fabella.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Lumine privasti me, nec fratrem ut frater amasti,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Non fecisse modo quod fecisti mihi malles.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Nunc scio, si posses, mihi lumina reddere velles,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">cum tua sunt</HI> <NOTE N="1357" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> sint 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nuda et</HI> <NOTE N="1358" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> nuda et  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa</HI>  2  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">aperta seu bene seu male facta.</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Sed nunc ex toto tibi, frater, corde remitto,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Ut pietate sua Deus omnipotens tibi parcat,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">Spiritus atque</HI> <NOTE N="1359" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> utque 2  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tuus post hac in pace quiescat.</HI></L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0119A"></COL> Post expletis <NOTE N="1360" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> hexpl.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  expl. A.</NOTE>  rite funebriis <NOTE N="1361" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> funebriis A 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> . funebris  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  funeriis
1.</NOTE>  exequiis <NOTE N="1362" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> obsequiis 2  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  accipit
 <NOTE N="1363" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> accepit 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . 3. 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Bracizlaum fratruelem, et ducit eum ad
sedem principalem: et sicut semper in electione ducis
faciunt, per superioris <NOTE N="1364" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> superiores 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  aulae cancellos decem
milia nummorum aut plus per <NOTE N="1365" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> in 2  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  populum spargunt,
ne <NOTE N="1366" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> ut—non 2.</NOTE>  ducem in solio comprimant, sed potius sparsos
nummos rapiant. Mox duce locato in solio et
facto silentio, tenens dextram sui fratruelis Jaromir
dixit ad populum:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ecce dux vester!</HI>  At illi <NOTE N="1367" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> isti 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.</NOTE>  succlamant
ter <NOTE N="1368" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> subclamabant 4. 4  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Krilessu</HI> <NOTE N="1369" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> Kryelesu 1. Krlesu 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . Kirlessu 3. Krlessu 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , quod est Kyrieleyson
 <NOTE N="1370" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI> 
A.</NOTE> . Et iterum Jaromir ad populum:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Accedant,</HI> 
inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">de gente Muncia</HI> <NOTE N="1371" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> Muncina 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> !  <HI REND="ITALIC">accedant de gente
Tepea</HI> <NOTE N="1372" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> Tepea 2  <SUP>b</SUP></NOTE> ! <NOTE N="(425)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119B"></COL> Ex Palackii sententia I, 168 scribendum
est Munici; sunt posteri Mun et Tepta.</NOTE> ; et vocat eos nominatim, quos norat
armis potentiores, fide meliores, militia fortiores
et divitiis eminentiores. Quos ut sensit adesse,
 <COL N="0119B"></COL> dixit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quoniam me mea facta non sinunt ut sim
vester dux</HI> <NOTE N="1373" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> ducem  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  dux A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">hunc assignamus vobis in ducem</HI> <NOTE N="1374" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> judicem 3.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">et collaudamus, quo ei obediatis, ut dignum est duci,
et debitam fidelitatem exhibeatis, ut decet</HI> <NOTE N="1375" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita
1. manu coaeva in rasura.</HI>  par est  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">suo
principi. Te autem, fili, moneo, et repetens iterum</HI> <NOTE N="1376" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> atque  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  A.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">iterumque monebo, istos colas ut patres, hos diligas
ut fratres, et in omnibus negotiis tibi consiliarios
habeas. His urbes</HI> <NOTE N="1377" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et populum ad regendum committas,
per hos enim Boemiae regnum stat et stetit
atque stabit in sempiternum</HI> <NOTE N="1378" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> i. semp.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ast illos, qui sunt
Wrissovici, iniquorum patrum nequam</HI> <NOTE N="1379" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">filii, nostri
generis</HI> <NOTE N="1380" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> generi 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">hostes domestici, familiares inimici,
 <COL N="0120A"></COL> ut coenosam rotam devites et consortia eorum declines,
quia nobis nunquam fuere fideles. Ecce me innocen,
tem et suum principem inprimis ligaverunt et diversis,
affecerunt ludibriis, post sibi innatis versuciis et fraudulentis
consiliis id egerunt, ut frater fratrem me
hisce privaret oculis. Habeas, fili mi, semper in memoria
sancti Adalberti praeconia, qui eorum ob facta
crudelia ter ut fiant super eos excidia sancto ore confirmavit</HI> 
 <NOTE N="(426)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119B"></COL> Cf. Brunonis Vita S. Adalberti, c. 21.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et excommunicavit eos in</HI> <NOTE N="1381" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> ex  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  2  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ecclesia.
Quae nutu Dei jam bis sunt facta, tercio ut fiant super
eos excidia</HI> <NOTE N="1382" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita 1. desunt in rell. omnibus.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">adhuc sunt sollicita fata</HI> <NOTE N="1383" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> facta 1.</NOTE> . At
illi audientes haec dissecabantur <NOTE N="1384" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> discalceabantur
2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ab antiqua manu deletum ei in margine scriptum</HI>  dissecabantur.</NOTE>  cordibus, et
fremebant dentibus in eum ut leones: nec post multos
dies Kohan, de quo supra retulimus, misso lictore
 <NOTE N="1385" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> litore  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  lictore 1.</NOTE>  suo, dum ille caecus purgat ventrem in necessario
 <COL N="0120B"></COL> noctis <NOTE N="1386" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> notis  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  noctis A.</NOTE>  in hora, acutissima sica perforat
eum in posteriora usque ad cordis <NOTE N="1387" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> noctis A. 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscriptum</HI>  A. cordis.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2. corporis 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . ventris
3. 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE>  interiora.
Sicque justus vir, velut <NOTE N="1388" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  pridie  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. eadem man.</HI>  pridie A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>  Dei martir, dux Jaromir
obiit anno dominicae incarnationis 1038. pridie <NOTE N="1388" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> vel  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  pridie  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. eadem man.</HI>  pridie A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
Nonas Novembris <NOTE N="(427)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0120" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0120B"></COL> Confirmat Necrologium Bohemicum</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0120">Hactenus acta antiquitus liber continet primus.</P> <P COM="0120">Sed quia, sicut ait beatus Hieronimus <NOTE N="(428)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0120" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0120B"></COL> Opera Hier., ed. Vallarsi II, 521.</NOTE> , aliter
visa, aliter audita <NOTE N="1389" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> mandata  <HI REND="ITALIC">recenti manu superscr.</HI> 
audita A.</NOTE> , aliter narrantur ficta <NOTE N="1390" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manus in 2. supra</HI>  i  <HI REND="ITALIC">apposuit</HI>  A.</NOTE> ,
quae melius scimus, melius et <NOTE N="1391" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A</NOTE>  proferimus, nunc
 <NOTE N="1392" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> nam 1.</NOTE>  auxiliante Deo et sancto Adalberto ea fert animus
dicere, quae ipsimet vidimus, vel quae <NOTE N="1393" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> quia 3.</NOTE>  ab his
referentibus <NOTE N="1394" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0119" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0119"></COL> ferentibus
1.</NOTE>  qui viderunt, veraciter audivimus.</P> <CAPTION COM="0120"><COL N="0119"></COL> EXPLICIT LIBER PRIMUS DE CHRONICIS BOEMORUM.</CAPTION></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0119" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0119">INCIPIT PROEMIUM
AD CLEMENTEM BREUNOVENSIS <NOTE N="1395" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> Breunensis 1.</NOTE>  ECCLESIAE ABBATEM <NOTE N="1396" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> prohemium ad Clementem Breunensem abbatem 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE></HEAD> <COL N="0121"></COL> <P COM="0121"><COL N="0121A"></COL> Spiritaii <NOTE N="1397" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> Spirituali 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . 3. 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Breunensis <NOTE N="1398" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> Breunovensis 4.</NOTE>  coenobii patri Clementi,
sic ex re nomen habenti, semper theoriae <NOTE N="1399" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> theorice A.</NOTE> 
inhaerenti, Cosmas, haud dignus dici decanus, angelici
 <NOTE N="1400" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> angelica 3.</NOTE>  consorcia <NOTE N="1401" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> consortii 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  senatus. Cum multa mecum
revolvens supersederem, quid potissimum caritatis
viro tantae sanctitatis transmitterem, quippe cui pondera
auri et argenti sordent, solaque quae sunt spiritualia
placent, optimum fore <NOTE N="1402" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  duxi tuae tantummodo
voluntati obsequi. Intellexi enim per tuum
 <NOTE N="1403" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> tyrum 2.</NOTE>  clericum nomine Deocarum, qui mihi clam innotuit
familiariter, quod meas naenias, quas olim Gervasio
 <COL N="0122A"></COL> <NOTE N="1404" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> magistro  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  scripseram, velles videre libenter. Hac
oblata occasione roboratus, immo cari amici persuasione
conpulsus, non solum quod optasti <NOTE N="1405" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> optari 1.</NOTE> ,
verum etiam secundum ejusdem narrationis, ut ita
dicam, libellum, quem similiter prout scire licuit
 <NOTE N="1406" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> debuit 1.</NOTE>  a tempore Bracizlai, filii ducis Oudalrici, usque
ad ejus aequivocum filium regis Wratizlay digestum,
tuae paternitati pandere praesumo. Licet enim, pater
o venerande, divinas non cesses epotare scripturas,
et profundos philosophiae semper exhaurias fontes,
tamen hoc tam tenui liquore

 <POEM COM="0122"><L>Non dedigneris tua sacra proluere labra.</L> <L>Saepe enim fit, ut post fortia vina et soporifera <NOTE N="1407" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> sopifera 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  pocula,</L> <L>naturalis quandoque homini incidat <NOTE N="1408" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> incidit 2. 2  <SUP>b</SUP> . 3.</NOTE>  sitis,</L> <L>fitque <NOTE N="1409" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> sicque
1.</NOTE>  haustus puri <NOTE N="1410" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> purae 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  laticis suavior dulcibus poculis.</L> <L>Saepe fit ut Martis <NOTE N="1411" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> mortis  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  fortis 1.</NOTE>  miles qui sudat in armis <NOTE N="1412" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> mis  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. man. superscr.</HI>  1. arvis 2. 2  <SUP>a</SUP> . 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,</L> <L>Gaudeat <NOTE N="1413" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI> 
4. gaudet  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  virgineis se commiscere <NOTE N="1414" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> commiscens 1.</NOTE>  choreis,</L> <L>Aut juvat in circo <NOTE N="1415" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> in c.  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A. idcirco 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  puerili <NOTE N="1416" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> pueruli 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ludere throco <NOTE N="1417" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> trocho 3.</NOTE> .</L> <L>Sic tu, o sanctissime pater, jam grandia et sillogistica volumina linque,</L> <L>et haec mea opuscula sensu puerilia, stilo rusticalia, perlege:</L> <L>ubi nonnulla subsannatione et derisione <NOTE N="1418" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> irrisione 2  <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  digna invenie</L> <L>quae utique idcirco memoriae commendes,</L> <L>ut ea tibi a Deo collata sapientia quandoque ad unguem <NOTE N="1419" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> nem  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. man. superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  emendes.</L></POEM></P> <P COM="0122">Quod autem in quibusdam locis quasi metricos versus invenis, scias me scienter nescium fecisse,
dum feci versus. Vale.</P></DIV1> <DIV1 COM="0122" SECOND="NO"><HEAD COM="0122">INCIPIT LIBER SECUNDUS <NOTE N="1420" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> I. l. s. in chronica Boemorum 4.</NOTE> .</HEAD> <COL N="0121"></COL> <P COM="0121"><COL N="0121B"></COL> 1. Igitur dux Bracizlaus jam in paterna sede vigoratus,
quam Deo tam hominibus beneplacitis actibus
calcans vestigia <NOTE N="1421" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> vestigium 3.</NOTE>  patrum, et eos praecellens
contigua arce <NOTE N="1422" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> arte 3.</NOTE>  virtutum, sicut sol in <NOTE N="1423" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  virtute
sua sydereum <NOTE N="1424" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> syderum 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  lumen et lunae nimio splendore
 <COL N="0122B"></COL> occulit et ebetat <NOTE N="1425" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> ebethat l. hebetat 3.</NOTE> , sic novus Achilles, novus
Thitides <NOTE N="1426" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0121" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0121"></COL> Tithides 2. Tydides 2  <SUP>b</SUP> .
Tychides 4. 4  <SUP>a</SUP> . novus Tith.  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissa</HI>  3.</NOTE>  Bracizlaus novis triumphis fortia acta
et victoriosissimas atavorum palmas attenuat et
obscurat. Nam Deus talem sibi gratiam contulit, ut
quas singulis hominibus particulariter, has quoque
huic indeficientes virtutes largitus est generaliter.</P> <POEM COM="0122"><L>Quippe hanc virtutum obtinuit accumulationem,</L> <L>ut in rebus rebellicis strennuitate praecelleret Gedeonem</L> <L>corporis viribus exsuperaret Samsonem,</L> <L>quadam speciali praerogativa sapientiae praeiret Salomonem.</L> <L>Unde factum est, ut in omnibus praeliis victor existeret ceu Josue,</L> <L>auro et argento locuplecior esset regibus Arabiae,</L> <L>et undique inexhaustis affluens diviciis,</L> <L>atque in largiendis muneribus non deficiens.</L> <L><COL N="0123A"></COL> assimiletur aquae, quae nunquam deficit amne.</L> <L>Huic conjunx Juditha nobilissima genere, fecundissima prolis germine,</L> <L>genuit quinque juvenes, corpore insignes</L> <L>et supereminentes, ceu Ehematiae <NOTE N="1427" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> Hematiae 1. Hemacie 4.</NOTE>  montes,</L> <L>sapientia singulares, probitate nulli comparabiles,</L> <L>moribus acceptabiles, in delinquentes placabiles <NOTE N="1428" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> moribus—placabiles  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE> ,</L> <L>in universa virtutum honestate laudabiles.</L></POEM> <P COM="0123"><COL N="0123A"></COL> Fuit autem primogenitus <NOTE N="1429" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> primus A.</NOTE>  nomine Spitignev,
secundus natu Wratizlav, tercius stemmate Conradus
 <NOTE N="1430" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> Chonradus
1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Chonradus 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , quartus genitura Jaromir <NOTE N="1431" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> lanimir 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , quintus et
ultimus Otto pulcherrimus. Horum <NOTE N="1432" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> quorum A.</NOTE>  de vita et
gloria, prout affluet verborum copia, sufficienter in
suis locis explicabitur. Quos adhuc positos annis <NOTE N="1433" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> annis  <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  3.</NOTE> 
in puerilibus sed studiis pollere <NOTE N="1434" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> studere A.</NOTE>  virilibus pater
valde miratur:
Cernens egregium decus et par nobile fratrum <NOTE N="(429)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123B"></COL> Hor., serm. II, 3, 243.</NOTE> 
Nec minus angebant matrem sua gaudia laetam <NOTE N="1435" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> leta 1.</NOTE> 
de tanto provectu <NOTE N="1436" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> profectu 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  filiorum et magnificae gloriae
statu.</P> <P COM="0123">2. Ea <NOTE N="1437" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> vero  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  4.</NOTE>  tempestate <NOTE N="(430)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123B"></COL> Male confundit Cosmas res Polonorum;
Kazimir obiit post Bracizlaum a. 1058, neque reliquit
filios pueros, sed ipse relictus est puer a patre
Misecone II; cfr. Martinus Gallus I, 48, ed.
Bandikte.</NOTE>  Kazimir <NOTE N="1438" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> Cazimir 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Poloniensi
nobilissimo duce ab hac subtracto luce, filiis
ejus Bolezlao et Wladizlao <NOTE N="(431)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123B"></COL> Praeter hos duos alios habebat filios Kazimir
Miseconem et Ottonem. Cfr. Martin. Gall. I, 19.</NOTE>  adhuc in infantia
 <COL N="0123B"></COL> positis ad ubera lactis <NOTE N="1439" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE> , una <NOTE N="1440" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> nulla 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  erat spes
salutis in misera fuga fugientibus per diversa loca
Poloniensibus. Quod animadvertens <NOTE N="1441" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> igitur advertens 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  dux Bracizlaus,
quarto anno sui ducatus <NOTE N="(432)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123B"></COL> i. e. ex ipsius Cosmae computatione a. 1041;
cfr. supra I, 42; sed hoc loco errat, ut ex accuratioribus
notis de translatione S. Adalberti II, 5,
patet.</NOTE> , optimum fore
ratus ne differret oblatam occasionem calumpniandi
suis inimicis, immo ulciscendi de illatis injuriis,
quas olim dux Mesco <NOTE N="1442" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">erasum</HI>  1.</NOTE>  intulerat Boemis, quantocius
 <NOTE N="1443" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> quanto cicius A.</NOTE>  potuit, inito consilio cum suis, eos invadere
statuit, statimque <NOTE N="1444" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> dux Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI> 
4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  terribilem dictat sentenciam,
tocius Boemiae per <NOTE N="1445" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  provinciam <NOTE N="1446" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> provinciae A.</NOTE>  mittens
in signum suae jussionis torquem de subere <NOTE N="1447" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> subure 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
tortum, ut quicunque exierit in castra segnius dato
signaculo, sciret procul dubio tali torque se <NOTE N="1448" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> se  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
suspendendum in patibulo. Quibus in momento, in
ictu oculi congregatis in unum et usque ad unum,
 <COL N="0124A"></COL> intrat terram Poloniae suo viduatam principe et eam
hostiliter invasit, ac velut ingens tempestas furit,
saevit, sternit omnia; sic villas caedibus, rapinis,
incendiis devastavit, in <NOTE N="1449" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> vi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  in 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  municiones irrupit. Krakov
autem eorum metropolim ingressus a culmine
subvertit, et spolia ejus obtinuit <NOTE N="1450" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> ti  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. man.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">in rasura</HI>  1.</NOTE> ; insuper et veteres
thesauros ab antiquis ducibus in aerario absconditos
evolvit, scilicet aurum et argentum infinitum
nimis. Similiter et caeteras urbes igne succendit
et usque ad solum destruxit. Cumque pervenissent
ad castrum Gedec <NOTE N="(433)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0124" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0124B"></COL> Quod ubi situm fuerit non satis liquet; conjecerunt
nonnulli esse Giecz, quam ducalem quondam
arcem inter Gnesnam et Posnaniam sitam esse
scribit Dlugosz. Cfr. Roepell I, 177.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="1451" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  Gnezden. Gradec 1. Gdec 2,
2 <SUP>a</SUP> . Gdee 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Goec 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , castellani et
simul qui illuc confugerant villani <NOTE N="1452" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> ni  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. man. superscr.</HI>  2.</NOTE> , non valentes
ferre impetum ducis, exeunt ei obviam auream gestantes
virgam, quod erat signum dedicionis, et ut
eos pacifice cum suis peccoribus et caeteris <NOTE N="1453" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A. caeterum 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  rerum
 <COL N="0124B"></COL> appenditiis transferat in Boemiam, suppliciter
rogant. Quorum dux peticionibus adquiescens, postquam
perduxit <NOTE N="1454" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> duxit A.</NOTE>  eos in <NOTE N="1455" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> ad 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Boemiam, dat eis partem
silvae, quae vocatur Crinin <NOTE N="1456" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> Cirum 2.  <HI REND="ITALIC">quamvis et legi possit</HI>  Ciruin; Cirnin 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , 4. Ciruin 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(434)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0124" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0124B"></COL> Quae fuerit illa silva, non patet. Diversorum
sententias vide apud Pubitschkam III, 301.</NOTE> , non modicam,
constituens eis unum <NOTE N="1457" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> U. eis  <HI REND="ITALIC">A.</HI></NOTE>  ex ipsis praefectum
 <NOTE N="1458" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> perfectum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  praef. 1.</NOTE>  et judicem, et decernit, ut sub lege quam
in Polonia habuerant, tam ipsi quam eorum posteri
in sempiternum vivant, atque nomine ab urbe derivato
usque hodie nuncupantur Gedcane <NOTE N="1459" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> Gedeane 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(435)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0124" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0124B"></COL> Vel hodie duas exstare villas in circulo Raconicensi
Hedecko et Hecdany observat Palacky
I, 280.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0124">3. Nec <NOTE N="1460" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> non A.</NOTE>  longe a praedicta urbe ventum erat ad
metropolim Gnezden <NOTE N="(436)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0124" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0124B"></COL> Gnesen.</NOTE> , natura loci et antemurali
firmam, sed facilem <NOTE N="1461" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> facile 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> ,</NOTE>  capi ab hostibus, raris
 <NOTE N="1462" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> ratis  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI> 
paucis 1.</NOTE>  eam inhabitantibus civibus, ubi tunc temporis
 <NOTE N="1463" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>  in basilica sanctae Dei genitricis Mariae
perpetuae Virginis preciosissimus <NOTE N="1464" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0123" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0123"></COL> preciosissime 1.</NOTE>  quiescebat
 <COL N="0125A"></COL> thesaurus, scilicet beatissimi Adalberti martiris <NOTE N="1465" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE> 
corpus. Qua mox Boemii sine Marte <NOTE N="1466" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> morte 1.</NOTE>  potiuntur
urbe, et cum magna laeticia intrant <NOTE N="1467" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> adeunt intrant 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">supra</HI>  intrant  <HI REND="ITALIC">manus alia scripsit</HI>  adeunt 2.</NOTE>  sanctae ecclesiae
adita <NOTE N="1468" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> limina adita 1. adita  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu suprascript.</HI>  limina 2. adyta 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . limina 4.</NOTE> , atque omni praeda <NOTE N="1469" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. manu</HI>  1.</NOTE>  posthabita,
solam sibi poscunt dari pro Christo passam sacri
corporis preciosam massam. Quorum praesul Severus
ut vidit temeritatem, et <NOTE N="1470" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">rasum</HI>  2.</NOTE>  pronam in omne
fas <NOTE N="1471" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> fasque 4.</NOTE>  nefasque <NOTE N="(437)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125C"></COL> Lucan., Pharsal. V, 313; VI, 147.</NOTE>  sensit voluntatem, talibus alloquiis
temptat eos revocare ab illicitis ausis <NOTE N="1472" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  causis.</NOTE> :
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Fratres mei et filii ecclesiae Dei, non tam ex facili
constat, sicut vos aestimatis, ut sacram corporis glebam,
Dei virtutibus plenam, quis mortalium tam temere
praesumat tangere. Timeo enim valde, ne percellamur
aut mentis oblivione aut caecitate aut aliqua
membrorum debilitate, si id temere praesumpserimus</HI> 
 <COL N="0125B"></COL> <NOTE N="1473" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> praesumamus 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">agere. Quapropter</HI> <NOTE N="1474" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> karissimi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">prius triduo jejunate,
de peccatis vestris poenitenciam agite, et</HI> <NOTE N="1475" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> et poenitentiam agite ab omnibus 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ab omnibus
abhominationibus, quas ipse abhominatus est in
vobis, abrenunciate, et</HI> <NOTE N="1476" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ex toto corde, quod eas
ultra non faciatis, promittite. Spero enim in misericordia
Dei et nostri patroni sancti Adalberti, quod non
privabimur spe peticionis nostrae, si persistimus fidei</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1477" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> federi 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in</HI> <NOTE N="1478" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">devotione et precum assidua oratione.</HI> 
At illis visa sunt praesulis verba quasi deliramenta,
et continuo aures suas continentes <NOTE N="1479" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> continuentes A continnientes 2.</NOTE>  fecerunt
impetum ut raperent sacrum corpus, et quia post
altare <NOTE N="1480" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">litterae</HI>  ar  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  1</NOTE>  juxta parietem conditum fuerat, et aliter
evelli non poterat, nisi altare <NOTE N="1481" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> prius  <HI REND="ITALIC">add</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  destrueretur <NOTE N="1482" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> destrueret 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE> ,
manus <NOTE N="1483" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1, 2.</NOTE>  inproba cum mente ferina operantur profana;
sed non defuit ultio divina. Nam in ipso <NOTE N="1484" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  inpio.</NOTE> 
 <COL N="0125C"></COL> opere suae temeritatis steterunt sensibus obstupefactis
 <NOTE N="1485" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> obstupefacti 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , nec erat vox nec sensus nec visus per
trium fere horarum spacia, donec iterum propiciante
Dei gratia rehabuere pristina officia. Moxque
licet sero poenitencia ducti faciunt jussa episcopi,
et quanto erant divino nutu evidentius castigati,
tanto devotius perstabant precibus infatigati, triduo
jejunantes et veniam postulantes.</P> <P COM="0125">4. Tercia nocte Severo episcopo post matutinalem
synaxim quiescenti sanctus praesul in visione apparens
Adalbertus <NOTE N="1486" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> sanctus
Adalbertus in visione apparens 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Dic,</HI>  ait,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ista duci</HI> <NOTE N="1487" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Bracizlao  <HI REND="ITALIC">add</HI>  4, 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et ejus
comitibus: Pater de coelis dabit quod petitis, si non
 <COL N="0126A"></COL> repetitis mala, quibus abrenuntiastis in fonte</HI> <NOTE N="1488" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> fronte  <HI REND="ITALIC">eraso</HI>  r A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">baptismatis</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1489" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> in baptismate
A. A*.</NOTE> . Hoc mane cum praesul <NOTE N="1490" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Severus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  innotesceret
duci et ejus comitibus, mox exhilarati intrantes
ecclesiam sanctae Mariae, et ante sepulchrum <NOTE N="1491" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE> 
sancti Adalberti <NOTE N="1492" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> martyris  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  humi <NOTE N="1493" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> humo 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  prostrati, diu fusa
comuni oratione surgit dux <NOTE N="1494" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  dux 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , et stans in ambone
 <NOTE N="1495" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> umbone 3.</NOTE> , hac rupit silentia voce <NOTE N="1496" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> dicens  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Vultis praevaricationes
vestras emendare, et a pravis operibus resipiscere?</HI> 
At illi obortis clamant <NOTE N="1497" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> clamant  <HI REND="ITALIC">repetitum</HI>  1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed
erasum.</HI></NOTE>  cum lacrimis
 <NOTE N="1498" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> dicentes  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Emendare parati sumus quicquid in sanctum
Dei</HI> <NOTE N="1499" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Adalbertum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> :</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">patres nostri vel nos</HI> <NOTE N="1500" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> peccatores  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">praevaricati
sumus, et a pravo opere omni</HI> <NOTE N="1501" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> animo 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">cessare.</HI>  Tunc
dux <NOTE N="1502" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  extendens manum suam super sacram
tumbam, sic orsus <NOTE N="1503" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> exorsus A. A*.</NOTE>  est ad populi turbam <NOTE N="1504" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> tumbam  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  turbam 1. turmam 4. 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Extendite, fratres</HI> <NOTE N="1505" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> karissimi
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">simul</HI> <NOTE N="1506" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vestras ad Dominum</HI> 
 <COL N="0126B"></COL> <NOTE N="1507" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Deum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">dextras et ad meos attendite sermones, quos volo
ut vestrae fidei sacramento confirmetis. Ergo hoc meum
proximum</HI> <NOTE N="1508" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> maximum A. A*. 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et primum sit decretum, ut vestra conubia,
quae actenus habuistis ut lupanaria, et ceu</HI> <NOTE N="1509" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> sunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">brutis animalibus communia, amodo juxta canonum
scita sint legitima, sint privata, sint insolubilia, ita
duntaxat ut</HI> <NOTE N="1510" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">una vir conjuge et conjunx viro
uno contenti vivant. Si autem conjunx virum aut
vir conjugem spreverit, et rixa inter eos usque ad
discidium efferbuerit,</HI> <NOTE N="1511" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al. man. superscr.</HI>  A. efferuerit 2, 3.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">qui ex eis</HI> <NOTE N="1512" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> his
A. A*.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in priorem
copulam legitime celebratam redire noluerit, nolo ut
secundum ritum nostrae terrae hujus rei violator</HI> <NOTE N="1513" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> praevaricator 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">in servitutem redigatur, sed potius nostri inmutabilis
decreti per angariam, qualiscunque sit persona, redigatur
in Ungariam, et nequaquam liceat ut precio
 <COL N="0126C"></COL> se redimat aut in hanc terram redeat, ne unius contagio
oviculae totum Christi serpat per ovile.</HI>  Severus
episcopus dixit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quicunque aliter fecerit, anathema
sit. Eadem sententia sint plectendae virgines et viduae
et adulterae, quae nomen bonum amisisse et pudorem
corrupisse ac per scortum concepisse dinoscuntur. Nam
cum liberum nubendi habeant arbitrium, cur comittunt
adulterium et conceptus suos abortivant</HI> <NOTE N="1514" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> avorcivant A. 3.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">quod est pessimum scelus scelerum?</HI>  Tunc dux <NOTE N="1515" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4., 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
subjungens inquit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si vero mulier proclamaverit</HI> <NOTE N="1516" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> perclamaverit
1.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">pari vice non amari, sed inclementer a viro suo</HI> <NOTE N="1517" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> suo  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest.</HI>  3.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">affligi et profligari</HI> <NOTE N="1518" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0125" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0125"></COL> proafligari  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  A. 1, 2.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">detur inter eos judicium Dei,
 <COL N="0127A"></COL> et qui inventus fuerit reus, solvat poenas rei. Similiter
et de his, qui homicidiis infamantur archipresbyter
comiti illius civitatis nomina eorum ascribat, et
comes eos conveniat; et si sunt</HI> <NOTE N="1519" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">al manu superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">rebelles, in carcerem
redigat, donec aut poenitenciam dignam agant,
aut si negant, ignito ferro sive adjurata aqua, utrum
culpabiles sint examinentur; fratricidas autem et
parricidas sive sacerdotum interfectores et hujusmodi
capitalibus criminibus irretitos, archipresbiter assignet
eos comiti vel duci, sive</HI> <NOTE N="1520" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> vel—sive A. seu 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . sive 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">per manus et ventrem
ferratos de regno ejiciat, ut ad instar Cain</HI> <NOTE N="1521" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> canum 3.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">vagi et profugi circueant</HI> <NOTE N="1522" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> circuerant 1,  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed corr.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">terram.</HI>  Severus episcopus
dixit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Ista ducis deliberatio justa sit anathemate
firma. Nam ad hoc vobis ducibus</HI> <NOTE N="1523" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> dulcibus  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  ducibus A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">mucro pendet in
femore, ut manus vestras saepius</HI> <NOTE N="1524" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">lavetis peccatoris
 <COL N="0127B"></COL> in sanguine.</HI>  Iterum dux <NOTE N="1525" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> ait  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit.</HI>  4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Tabernam</HI> <NOTE N="1526" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> taberna A.</NOTE> ,
inquit <NOTE N="1527" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">quae est radix omnium malorum, unde
prodeunt furta, homicidia</HI> <NOTE N="1528" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> hunicidia 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">adulteria</HI> <NOTE N="1529" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> fornicationes, ebrietates  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et caetera
mala, et qui parat et qui paratum</HI> <NOTE N="1530" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> partam A. 1, 2.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">comparat,</HI> 
Severus episcopus dixit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Anathema sit.</HI>  Et dux
 <NOTE N="1531" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> iterum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4,
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Qui,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">comprehensus fuerit hujus violator
decreti tabernarius, in medio foro ad palum suspensus,
et usque ad fastidium praeconis caesus depiletur:
res tamen ejus non infiscentur</HI> <NOTE N="1532" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> confiscentur 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> ;  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed potus</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1533" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> potius A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tantum in terram projiciatur</HI> <NOTE N="1534" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> seu potius—projiciantur 3.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ne quis</HI> <NOTE N="1535" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> de  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">execrabili haustu</HI> <NOTE N="1536" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> haustu  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. 1, pro</HI>  hastu.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">polluatur. Potatores autem, si
deprehensi</HI> <NOTE N="1537" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> de presensi 1.  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fuerint, non prius de carcere exeant,
quam in fiscum ducis unusquisque 300 nummos componat.</HI> 
Severus episcopus dixit:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Quae dux judicat,
nostra auctoritas firmat.</HI>  Adhuc dux <NOTE N="1538" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  prosequitur
 <COL N="0127C"></COL> dicens:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Fora autem dominicis diebus omnino ne fiant
interdicimus, quae ideo maxime in his celebrant regionibus,
ut caeteris diebus suis vacent operibus. Si
quis autem quam dominicis tam festis</HI> <NOTE N="1539" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> tam
dominicis, quam festivis 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">diebus</HI> <NOTE N="1540" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> dom. diebus t. f. A.</NOTE> 
 <HI REND="ITALIC">publice ad ecclesiam feriari indictis in aliquo servili
opere inventus fuerit, ipsum opus et quod in opere est
inventum archipresbiter tollat jumentum</HI> <NOTE N="1541" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A. A*.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et 300
ducis</HI> <NOTE N="1542" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> duci 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">in fiscum solvat nummos. Similiter et qui in
agris sive in silvis suos sepeliunt mortuos, hujus rei
praesumptores archidiacono</HI> <NOTE N="1543" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> archidiaconus
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">bovem et 300 in fiscum
ducis</HI> <NOTE N="1544" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> duci 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">solvant</HI> <NOTE N="1545" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> solvat 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nummos</HI> <NOTE N="1546" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omissum</HI>  1, 2.</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">mortuum
tamen in poliandro</HI> <NOTE N="1547" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> r  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu superscr.</HI>  A. 1 polyando
2, 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fidelium humi condant denuo.
Haec sunt quae odit Deus, haec sanctus Adalbertus
 <COL N="0128A"></COL> pertesus</HI> <NOTE N="1548" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> perosus 2.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nos</HI> <NOTE N="1549" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> vos 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">suas deseruit oves et ad exteras
maluit ire docturus gentes. Haec ut ultra non faciamus,
nostrae simul et vestrae fidei sacramento confirmamus.</HI> 
Sic ait dux. Et praesul <NOTE N="1550" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> Severus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  sanctae Trinitatis
nomine invocato et malleo assumpto, caeteris <NOTE N="1551" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omittunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> 
clericis septem <NOTE N="1552" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> VI, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  psalmos et alias huic sancto <NOTE N="1553" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI> 
3.</NOTE> 
operi competentes orationes ymnizantibus, coepit
molliter destruere summa sepulchri, destruens eum
usque ad ima thesauri sacri, et cum aperuissent
sarcophagum, omnes qui in ecclesia aderant tanta flagrantia
 <NOTE N="1554" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> fraglancia 1, 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(438)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127C"></COL> I. q. fragrantia.</NOTE>  suavissimi odoris sunt referti, ut per
tres dies quasi opimis <NOTE N="1555" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> optimis A. 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ferculis referti obliviscerentur
cibo refici, quin etiam et <NOTE N="1556" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> et  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE>  infirmi sanati
sunt eadem ora <NOTE N="1557" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. die  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  quam plurimi. Tunc dux <NOTE N="1558" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> Bracizlaus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI> 
4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et
episcopus <NOTE N="1559" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> Severus  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et pauci comitum inspicientes, ut viderunt
 <COL N="0128B"></COL> sanctum Dei <NOTE N="1560" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> Adalbertum  <HI REND="ITALIC">add.</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ita vultu et habitu clarum, et
sic corpore integrum per omnia, ac si eadem die
sacra missarum celebrasset solempnia, clerici  <HI REND="ITALIC">Te
Deum laudamus,</HI>  laici  <HI REND="ITALIC">Kyrieleyson</HI> <NOTE N="1561" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> krilès A. kyrt 4.</NOTE>  modulantur,
et resonant voces eorum usque ad ethera <NOTE N="1562" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> heta 1.</NOTE> . His
ita peractis dux prae gaudio faciem perfusus lacrimis,
sic orat <NOTE N="1563" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> dicens
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">O</HI> <NOTE N="1564" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Christi martir, beate Adalberte</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1565" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> Adaberte 1.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">nostri semper et ubique miserate</HI> <NOTE N="1566" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> miserere 3.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">nunc solita nos respice pietate, et nobis peccatoribus
propiciare, atque ad</HI> <NOTE N="1567" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tuam sedem</HI> <NOTE N="1568" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> sanctae  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt.</HI>  4,
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">Pragensis
ecclesiae per nos quamvis peccatores referri non dedignare.</HI> 
Mira res et valde stupenda, cujus tumbam
nudius tercius contingere non poterant, continuo
dux et episcopus sine impedimento corpus ejus sarcophago
levant et serico cooperientes in superiori
 <COL N="0128C"></COL> altari locant, ut plebs sua vota solvat <NOTE N="1569" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> solvant  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  solvat A.</NOTE> , quae Deo
et ejus sancto voverat, atque eadem die <NOTE N="1570" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  compositae
sunt 200 marcae altaris in arce <NOTE N="1571" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> alt. in arce  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI>  A.</NOTE> .

 <POEM COM="0128"><L>O Deus omnipotens, mundum per secla revolvens,</L> <L>Qui semper regnas, solus qui cuncta gubernas,</L> <L>Nil fit, nec fuit in mundo nec erit, bone Christe,</L></POEM> 

tuo sine nutu. Quisnam mortalis hoc unquam credere
posset, ut ad gentes apostatrices jam in celesti
regno laureatus corpus suum referri sineret, quarum
 <NOTE N="1572" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> quorum 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  aspernatus facinora aufugit <NOTE N="1573" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> aufugerat
2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  consortia, cum
adhuc viveret. Sed si majora Dei et antiqua miracula
 <NOTE N="1574" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0127" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0127"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al. manu</HI>  A.</NOTE>  perpendimus, quomodo populus Israeliticus sicco
 <COL N="0129A"></COL> vestigio transivit mare, qualiter de sicca rupe
fluxerunt <NOTE N="1575" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> fluxerint 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  aquae, vel qualiter factor orbis apparuit
in orbe natus ex Maria Virgine, non ammirari,
sed potius Deo, qui fecit et facere potest quae vult,
nos decet humiliari et ejus gratiae totum assignare;
cujus gratia inspirante ascendit in cor ducis, ut
similiter transferret <NOTE N="1576" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> transferat A. 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  corpus archipraesulis ejusdem
civitatis, nomine Gaudencii <NOTE N="(439)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129B"></COL> Hujus ossa loco reliquiarum S. Adalberti a
Polonis pia fraude data et a Bohemis translata esse
probare conatus est Dlugosz et post eum alii; sed e
parte Cosmae Polonus stat auctor Martinus Gallus
I, 19. Cfr. Balbini Epitome rer. Bohem. III, 4. Dobner
ad Haiec. V. 235. Meinert Wiener Jahrbucher
 <COL N="0130B"></COL> XLVIII. Anz., p. 48.</NOTE>  qui in eadem
forte <NOTE N="1577" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> fere A.</NOTE>  ecclesia quiescebat. Hic utique <NOTE N="1578" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. uti  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  superius
retulimus, non solum carnali verum et spirituali <NOTE N="1579" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> spiritali 1.</NOTE> 
conjunctione <NOTE N="1580" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> conjuncione 1. compunctione 4.</NOTE>  frater sancti Adalberti et comes
individuus in omni labore et erumna fuit, et si cum
eo non corpore martirium <NOTE N="1581" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> sustinuit  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , mentis tamen compassione
tulit. Nec enim fieri poterat ut <NOTE N="1582" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>  gladius
animam ejus non petransiret, cum germanum suum
 <COL N="0129B"></COL> rompheis paganorum in frusta <NOTE N="1583" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> frustra  <HI REND="ITALIC">erasa</HI>  r  <HI REND="ITALIC">littera</HI> 
A. 1.</NOTE>  concidi videret,
et ipse pariter occidi valde optaret <NOTE N="1584" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> optarat  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  optaret A.</NOTE> . Item <NOTE N="1585" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> iterum 1.</NOTE> 
visum est <NOTE N="1586" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> nobilissimo  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  duci <NOTE N="1587" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Bracizlao
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  et episcopo, ut <NOTE N="1588" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> sanctorum martyrum  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  quinque
fratrum reliquias sancto corpori adjunctas, quorum
de vita ac passione satis supra retulimus <NOTE N="1589" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Deo donante relaturi sumus 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(440)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0130" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0130B"></COL> Cf. I, 38.</NOTE> ,
qui <NOTE N="1590" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> non  <HI REND="ITALIC">al
manu superscr.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  in eadem civitate sed in alia ecclesia quiescebant,
pariter <NOTE N="1591" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> par. q. A.</NOTE>  eum summa diligentia transferant.
Quid multa?</P> <P COM="0129">5. Ventum erat cum omni sacra sarcina in prosperitate
et laetitia Boemiam, et in vigilia <NOTE N="1592" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> vigiliis 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  sancti
Bartholomei apostoli prope metropolium Pragam
 <COL N="0130A"></COL> castra metati sunt circa rivulum Rokitnicam <NOTE N="1593" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Kocitnicam 2, Rokitniczam 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> 
 <NOTE N="(441)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0130" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0130B"></COL> Rokytnice.</NOTE> , ubi lucescente die clerus et universa plebs
cum processione occurrit, cujus longam seriem latus
vix explicuit campus. Talis enim processio fuit?
Dux ipse et episcopus humeris subnixi dulce pondus
portant martiris Christi Adalberti; post simul
abbates ferebant reliquias quinque <NOTE N="1594" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> sanctorum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  fratrum,
deinde archipresbiteri gaudent onere Gaudentii archiepiscopi,
quos electi 12 <NOTE N="1595" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> XX, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  presbiteri, vix sustentantes
pondus <NOTE N="1596" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> corpus 2.</NOTE>  aurei crucifixi, secuntur—
nam dux Mesco ter <NOTE N="1597" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1.</NOTE>  semetipsum hoc apponderarat
auro,—quinto <NOTE N="1598" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> to  <HI REND="ITALIC">superscr. al man.</HI>  A.</NOTE>  loco ferunt tabulas tres
graves auro quae circa altare, ubi sanctum corpus
 <NOTE N="1599" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> positum
 <HI REND="ITALIC">inserit</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  quievit, positae fuerant. Erat enim major tabula
quinque ulnarum in longitudine et decem palmarum
 <COL N="0130B"></COL> in latitudine, valde adornata lapidibus preciosis et
cristallinis sachis <NOTE N="(442)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0130" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0130B"></COL> I. e. rebus?</NOTE> . Cujus inscriptus fuit hic in
margine versus:

 <POEM COM="0130"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Ter centum libras apponderat hoc opus auri.</HI></L></POEM> 

Postremo plus quam centum plaustris ducunt inmensas
campanas et omnes Poloniae gazas, quas sequitur
innumera nobilium virorum turma, asstricti
 <NOTE N="1600" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> astrictis 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  manicis ferreis et contriti colla bagis <NOTE N="1601" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> bogis 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(443)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0130" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0130B"></COL> I. e. circulis forteis.</NOTE> ,
inter quos, heu! male captus, adductus est meus
attavus <NOTE N="1602" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> meus atavus  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt in</HI>  A. 1, 2, 2 <SUP>a</SUP> , 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">legunt</HI>  4,
4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> .

 <POEM COM="0130"><L INDENT=1>Consors in clero, presbiter officio.</L> <L INDENT=1>O dies illa, dies <NOTE N="1603" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> dies  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Boemis honoranda et per saecula memoriae commendanda</L> <L INDENT=1>sacris mysteriis frequentanda, dignis praeconiis celebranda,</L> <L INDENT=1>laudibus devotissime <NOTE N="1604" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> devotissimae 1.</NOTE>  veneranda,</L> <L INDENT=1>divitibus laetabunda, debilibus exoptanda,</L> <L>pauperibus jocunda, datione elemosinarum decoranda,</L> <L>et omnibus bonis <NOTE N="1605" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  studiis excolenda, in qua festis festa</L> <L>refulgent accumulata. O nimium <NOTE N="1606" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> omnium A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">sed. corr.</HI>  2.</NOTE>  felix metropolis Praga,</L> <L>olim sacro duce <NOTE N="1607" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Wencezlao
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  sublimata, nunc beato praesule <NOTE N="1608" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Adalberto  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  decorata,</L> <L>a Domino Deo tibi collata excipis gaudia geminata,</L> <L>et per has binas misericordiae olivas</L> <L>fama volas <NOTE N="1609" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> volat 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  ultra Soromatas <NOTE N="1610" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  1. Solamatas A. Foramatas 2, 2 <SUP>a</SUP> .
Sarmatas 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , Sauromatas 3. Soramatas 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  atque Sarigas <NOTE N="1611" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Iazygas 3.</NOTE> .</L></POEM> 

 <COL N="0129B"></COL> Facta est autem haec translatio beatissimi Christi
martiris Adalberti anno dominicae incarnationis
 <COL N="0130B"></COL> 1039. <NOTE N="(444)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0130" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0130B"></COL> Consentiunt Annales Pragenses.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="1612" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> 1030. 9. K. Sept. 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . VIII. 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  Kal. Septembris <NOTE N="1613" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> regnante Domino nostro Jesu Christo, cui est honor et imperium in secula seculorum. Amen.  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI> 
4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0130">6. Sed his prosperis a Deo <NOTE N="1614" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0129" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0129"></COL> Domino A.</NOTE>  concessis improbus
 <COL N="0131A"></COL> delator non defuit <NOTE N="1615" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> destitit 3.</NOTE> , qui apostolico uti gesta
haec erant retulit <NOTE N="1616" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE> , divinas sanctiones et sanctorum
patrum traditiones violasse ducem Boemiae et
episcopum promulgavit; et si hoc inultum domnus
papa <NOTE N="(445)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131C"></COL> Benedictus qui sedit a. 1033-1048.</NOTE>  praetermitteret, jura apostolicae sedis per
totum mundum observanda imminueret. Continuo
sacer conventus celebratur, canones recitantur,
sacrae Scripturae scrutantur. Dux et episcopus,
quamvis absens, de praesumptione arguitur: alii
ducem omni dignitate privatum per tres annos in
exilium decernunt, alii episcopum ab omni pontificali
officio suspensum, quoad usque vivat, in claustro
monachorum degere judicant, alii ambos gladio
anathematis feriendos clamant.</P> <P COM="0131">7. Interea legati ducis et episcopi Boemorum ex
 <COL N="0131B"></COL> parte tocius populi et ipsorum Roman adveniunt,
ferentes mandata magis muneribus oblita <NOTE N="1617" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> oblata A.</NOTE>  quam
facundiae verbis <NOTE N="1618" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> facundia verborum 3.</NOTE>  polita. Quibus ubi data est copia
fandi, in conspectu <NOTE N="1619" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> conspectum 2, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  apostolici et sacri concilii
tali sermone causam suae legationis sunt prosecuti
 <NOTE N="1620" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> persecuti 3.</NOTE> .  <HI REND="ITALIC">O fidei catholicae et sedis apostolicae sanctissime
rector, et o patres in libro vitae</HI> <NOTE N="1621" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">conscripti,
quibus a Deo collata est potestas judicandi simul et
miserendi, miseremini peccasse confitentibus, parcite
paenitentibus simul et veniam postulantibus. Fatemur
enim quod illicita et contra canonum statuta egimus,
quia de tam</HI> <NOTE N="1622" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> terra 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">longinquis partibus ob tam breve
temporis spacium ad tam sanctum negotium vestrum</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1623" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">omittunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">nequivimus habere nuncium. Sed quicquid est illud,
quod fecimus, sciatis, o patres, sciatis</HI> <NOTE N="1624" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita 1. deest in rell.</HI></NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">conscripti,
 <COL N="0131C"></COL> nos non ex temeritate, sed pro magna utilitate
Christianae religionis atque bona intentione id
recisse. Aut, si unquam bona intencio cadit in vitium,
o sanctissimi patres, secundum vestrum judicium
parati sumus nostrum emendare flagicium.</HI>  Ad
haec apostolicus paucis:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Si poenitet,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">haud
nocet error.</HI>  Mox legati summoti a concilio <NOTE N="1625" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita</HI>  A. ad
concilio 1. negotio 2. concilio  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  potiuntur
hospicio, sequenti die reddituri rationem in
judicio. Illa autem nocte ducis missi et episcopi,
circueuntes <NOTE N="1626" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> circuientes A.</NOTE>  corruperunt pecunia cardinalium
astuciam, auro subplantant justiciam, mercantur
precio clementiam, muneribus leniunt <NOTE N="1627" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> emunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  judicialem
sentenciam. Postera autem die iterum legatis sacri
concilii in capitolio <NOTE N="1628" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> capitulo 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  praesentatis, domnus apostolicus
 <COL N="0132A"></COL> os aperuit sacrum, ponderosis verbis et
auctoritate plenum.  <HI REND="ITALIC">Sicut,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">pertinacibus in
impietatis culpa</HI> <NOTE N="1629" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> impietatibus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">pro</HI>  culpa 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">est saevior exerenda</HI> <NOTE N="1630" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> exercenda 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">vindicta,
ita reatum suum recognoscentibus et poenitenciam
desiderantibus facilem praebemus assensum</HI> <NOTE N="1631" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> asensum 1.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et ab
hoste</HI> <NOTE N="1632" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> hostibus 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">inflictis vulneribus misericordiae adhibemus</HI> 
 <NOTE N="1633" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> h.  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu
superscr. 1. ut saepius.</HI></NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">antidotum. Magnum enim peccatum est aliena
rapere, sed majus christianos non solum spoliare,
verum etiam captivare et captivos</HI> <NOTE N="1634" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> captivatos 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ceu bruta animalia
vendere, nimis est abhominabile: quod vos
perpetrasse in Polonia, nobis relatum est per veridica
nuncia. Quod autem nulli liceat sine nostra permissione
de loco ad locum sacrum transferre corpus,
testantur canones, prohibent</HI> <NOTE N="1635" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> perhibent 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">patrum decreta, et
praesumptores hujuscemodi</HI> <NOTE N="1636" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> hujusmodi 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">rei divina jubent eloquia
 <COL N="0132B"></COL> gladio anathematis ut feriantur. Sed quia vos
sive per ignorantiam sive bonae intentionis ob gratiam
hanc rem fecistis, praecipimus</HI> <NOTE N="1637" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> per sanctam
obedientiam  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">ut pro hac tam
temeri</HI> <NOTE N="1638" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> temera 3.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">praesumptione dux vester et episcopus coenobium
omnibus ecclesiasticis usibus et honoribus sufficienter
amplificatum in competenti</HI> <NOTE N="1639" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> compenti  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  competenti A.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">loco construant,
probatasque personas ac officia servientium clericorum
ex more constituant, ubi Deo sedulum servicium tam
pro vivis fidelibus quam pro defunctis in sempiternum
exhibeatur, ut saltem vel sic in conspectu Dei reatus
vestri transgressio deleatur.</HI>  Mox legati valde <NOTE N="1640" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  2.</NOTE> 
exhylarati proficiscuntur et referunt duci jussa apostolici.
Quibus dux, velut divinis jussis obtemperans,
sub honore sancti Wencezlai martiris in urbe Boleslau
 <NOTE N="1641" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> Boleslaw 2. Boleslai 3. Bolezlai 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  juxta flumen Labe <NOTE N="(446)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131C"></COL> Al-Bunzlau ad Albim.</NOTE> , ubi idem sanctus
 <COL N="0132C"></COL> <NOTE N="1642" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> Wencezlas  <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  olim feliciter consummavit martirium, venustissimum
fabricavit coenobium, in quo, sicut et
hodie cernitur, Deo servit caterva fratrum numerosa,
et habetur praepositura et basilica valde religiosa
 <NOTE N="(447)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131C"></COL> Haec res anno demum 1046 diiudicata est.</NOTE> .</P> <P COM="0132">8. Anno domin. incarn. 1040. Fama, qua nullum
pejus malum viget in mundo <NOTE N="(448)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0132" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0132C"></COL> Virg. Aen. IV, 174, 175.</NOTE> , et quae mendaciis
pinguescit, et miscens plura paucis, falsa veris,
volando crescit, perfert ad aures imperatoris secundi
Heinrici <NOTE N="(449)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0132" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0132C"></COL> Heinricos imperatores numerat Cosmas.</NOTE>  cencies plus, quam verum fuit, pondus
auri et argenti Boemos de Polonia asportasse.
Tunc imperator <NOTE N="1643" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> Henricus
 <HI REND="ITALIC">addunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  coepit quaerere occasiones adversus
eos, quoquomodo <NOTE N="1644" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> quomodo 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4.</NOTE>  ab eis quod sibi dictum
fuerat <NOTE N="1645" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0131" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0131"></COL> ut  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  A.</NOTE>  eriperet aurum. Et mandans per quaestionarios,
 <COL N="0133A"></COL> ut argentum, quod in Polonia rapuerant,
nisi infra statutum terminum usque ad unum obulum
 <NOTE N="1646" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> obolum 1.</NOTE>  sibi mittant, minatur bellum. Ad haec Sclavi
inquiunt:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Semper salvo tenore nostrae legis fuimus et
hodie sumus sub imperio Karoli regis et ejus successoribus,
nostra gens nunquam extitit rebellis, et tibi
in omnibus bellis mansit et semper manebit fidelis, si
justiciam nobis tantum</HI> <NOTE N="1647" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> t. n. A. tantummodo 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">facere velis. Talem enim
nobis legem instituit Pippinus</HI> <NOTE N="(450)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133C"></COL> Carolus erat, Caroli Magni filius, qui a. 805
expeditionem in Boemos fecit teste Einhardo in
Annalibus.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">magni Karoli
regis filius, ut annuatim imperatorum successoribus
120 boves electos et 500 marcas solvamus—marcam
nostrae monetae 200 nummos dicimus</HI> <NOTE N="(451)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133C"></COL> Dobner ad Haiec. II, 433, docet nummum
unum illorum temporum idem valuisse quod nostris
diebus quatuor et dimidium nummos cruce signatos
(Kreuzer), Bohemicum igitur censum fuisse
7500 florenos nostrae monetae.</NOTE> — <HI REND="ITALIC">hoc
testatur nostratum aetas in aetatem</HI> <NOTE N="1648" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> nostrarum etas etatum A. aetate 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ;  <HI REND="ITALIC">hoc omni
anno sine refragatione</HI> <NOTE N="1649" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> reflagratione A. 1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">tibi solvimus et tuis successoribus
solvere volumus. At si aliquo praeter solitum
 <COL N="0133B"></COL> legis</HI> <NOTE N="1650" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> regis 4.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">jugo nos aggravare volueris, mori
potius prompti sumus, quam insuetum ferre onus.</HI> 
Ad haec imperator respondit <NOTE N="1651" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> respondens dixit 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE> :  <HI REND="ITALIC">Regibus hic mos
est semper aliquid novi legi addere anteriori, neque
enim omnis lex est constituta tempore in uno, sed per
successores regunt crevit series legum. Nam qui regunt
leges non reguntur legibus, quia lex, ut aiunt
vulgo, cereum habet nasum</HI> <NOTE N="1652" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> quia ut—lex nasum  <HI REND="ITALIC">desunt</HI> 
A.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">et rex ferream marum
et longam, ut eam flectere queat, quo sibi placeat.
Pippinus rex</HI> <NOTE N="1653" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> Franciae  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">fecit quod voluit; vos autem nisi
quod volo faciatis, ostendam vobis, quot</HI> <NOTE N="1654" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr.</HI>  quot A. 1. quot  <HI REND="ITALIC">super</HI>  quod 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">pictos
habeam clipeos aut quid bello valeam.</HI></P> <P COM="0133">9. Et statim mittens litteras per totum regnum,
valde fortem colligit exercitum <NOTE N="(452)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133C"></COL> Primam Bohemicam expeditionem Heinrici
III, a. 1039, auctor silentio transiit, qua Bretislaus
filium primogenitum obsidem dedit. Cfr,
Hermann. Aug. a. 1039.</NOTE> . Altera via qua
itur per <NOTE N="1655" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> ad 2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  Zribiam <NOTE N="1656" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> Zrbiam 3.</NOTE> , et est exitus de silva in
 <COL N="0133C"></COL> istam terram per castrum Hlumec <NOTE N="1657" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> Hlymec 1. Hlymee 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP>  Hlumer 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(453)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133C"></COL> Nomen servatum esse in odierne Kuml,
castrique rudera in monte Geyersberg superesse
 <COL N="0134C"></COL> conjicit Dobner V, 256. Vide quoque commentationem
Kropfii in Monatschrift der Gesellschaft des vaterländischen
Museums in Böhmen I, Decemb.,
p. 37.</NOTE> , jussit
Saxones intrare Boemiam, quorum tunc temporis
dux <NOTE N="1658" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> princeps 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  erat Occardus <NOTE N="1659" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> Okkardus 2. Okardus 3.  <HI REND="ITALIC">semper.</HI></NOTE>   <NOTE N="(454)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0134" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0134C"></COL> Marchio Misnensis.</NOTE> , cui omnis Saxonia
tanquam regi paruit per omnia. Fuit enim vir
magni consilii, et in ordinandis <NOTE N="1660" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> ordinandi
4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  regni negotiis
 <COL N="0134A"></COL> singulari sollertia praeditus et rebus bellicis a puericia
deditus, sed nunquam belli felices obtinuit successus.
Ipse autem caesar castra metatus est ex
utraque parte fluminis Rezne <NOTE N="1661" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> Rezene 1.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(455)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0134" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0134C"></COL> Regen.</NOTE> . Postera autem
 <NOTE N="1662" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> vero A.</NOTE>  die pertransiens castrum Kanb <NOTE N="1663" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  A. Kamb 1, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Kamba 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(456)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0134" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0134C"></COL> Kamb in Bavaria.</NOTE>  cum
admoveret aquilas silvae quae dirimit Bawariam atque
Boemiam <NOTE N="(457)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0134" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0134C"></COL> De loco quo haec Bohemorum victoria reportata
sit fusius disseruit Dobner l. l. In limitibus
Bavariae et provinciae Pilsensis, haud procul ab urbe
Tauss, praelium commissum esse putat.</NOTE> , ut <NOTE N="1664" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> quod  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserit</HI> 
2.</NOTE>  cognovit quod obstruerent
Boemii vias per silvam <NOTE N="1665" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> silvas 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> , indignatus parum
tacuit, concuciensque caput ter concipit iras <NOTE N="(458)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0134" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0134C"></COL> Cf. Ovid., Metamorph. II, 50; I 166;
181.</NOTE> 
caesare <NOTE N="1666" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> caesari 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  dignas <NOTE N="1667" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">haec verba a correctore in</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">ita mutata:</HI>  cepit irasci,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">syllabis</HI>  con  <HI REND="ITALIC">et</HI>  sare  <HI REND="ITALIC">erasis, vox</HI>  dignas  <HI REND="ITALIC">expuncta est.</HI></NOTE> , atque in haec verba solvit ora:
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Licet exstruant muros silvis</HI> <NOTE N="1668" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. al. man.</HI>  1.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">altiores, licet elevent
turres sublimes usque ad nubes, uti frustra jacitur
rete ante oculos pennatorum, sic nichil valent contra
Teutonicos obpugnacula Boemorum</HI> <NOTE N="1669" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> Boemii pugnare A.</NOTE> 

 <POEM COM="0134"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Aut si ascendent super nubila, aut si includant</HI> <NOTE N="1670" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> includent
A.</NOTE> ,</L> <L><COL N="0134B"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">se inter sidera,</HI></L> <L INDENT=1><HI REND="ITALIC">perditam et miseram gentem nihil ista juvabunt.</HI></L> <L INDENT=1>Sic ait et jussit cunctos irrumpere silvam,</L></POEM> 

et ipse <NOTE N="1671" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> super  <HI REND="ITALIC">addit</HI>  A.</NOTE>  eos praecedens ascendit montem <NOTE N="1672" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> magnum et  <HI REND="ITALIC">inserunt</HI>  4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  altum
in media silva situm, sedensque in tripode dixit
 <NOTE N="1673" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> dux 1. dixit  <HI REND="ITALIC">corr. man. recentior.</HI></NOTE>  ad astantes tocius regni principes:

 <POEM COM="0134"><L><HI REND="ITALIC">Hac in valle cohors ignava latet Boemorum,</HI></L> <L><HI REND="ITALIC">quasi mus agrestis in suis receptaculis</HI></L></POEM> 

 <HI REND="ITALIC">antrorum.</HI>  Sed fefellit caesarem sua opinio <NOTE N="1674" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> oppinio A.</NOTE> , nam
ultra alterum montem fuit illorum munitio. Tunc
unumquemque caesar appellans nomine, prius marchiones,
dehinc quosque nobiliores armatos praemittens,
jubet pedestres ire in pugnam, his verbis pollicitans
eis victoriam:  <HI REND="ITALIC">Non est,</HI>  inquit,  <HI REND="ITALIC">vobis opus
laborioso certamine; tantum descendite, certe ipsi
 <COL N="0134C"></COL> fugient</HI> <NOTE N="1675" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> fugiunt 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">prae timore, nequeunt enim vestrum impetum
ferre. Ite mei, ite, falcones, pavidas capite palumbes,
et ut feroces leones, more luporum, qui dum
irrumpunt ovilia ovium</HI> <NOTE N="1676" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0133" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0133"></COL> omnium 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">non curant de numero,
et non nisi toto grege mactato pociuntur edulio.</HI></P> <P COM="0134"><COL N="0135A"></COL> 10. Mox secundum jussum regis ruunt loricata
 <NOTE N="1677" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> ta  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  agmina; de primo loco pugnae certant proceres,

 <POEM COM="0135"><L>Conspicuae <NOTE N="1678" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> prospicuae A.</NOTE>  nitent acies ut lucida glacies,</L></POEM> 

et ut sol refulsit eorum in arma, resplendent frondes
silvarum ab eis et cacumina montium. Descendentes
autem in vallem neminem inveniunt, quia hinc et
illinc spissa silva et inpenetrabilia sunt loca; et
sicut solet in omni certamine fieri, subsequentes
etiam invitos inpellunt ad pugnam praecedentes, sic
jam fatigati proceres iterum conpelluntur <NOTE N="1679" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">ita corr.</HI>  1, coguntur  <HI REND="ITALIC">rell.</HI></NOTE>  a
subsequentibus transcendere alterum montem. Sed
jam aestu <NOTE N="1680" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  3.</NOTE>  et siti sicco <NOTE N="1681" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> sicca
2 <SUP>b</SUP> .</NOTE>  lingua adhaeret palato;
vires deficiunt, dexterae languescunt, anhelitus
aegros de pectore trahunt, nec tamen sistere queunt
 <NOTE N="1682" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> queunt  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu superscript.</HI>  A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  1, 2, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> , 3; valent 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  gradum. Alii super scuta suas <NOTE N="1683" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> sua A.</NOTE>  loricas dejiciunt,
 <COL N="0135B"></COL> alii stant appodiati arboribus, frustra inanem
auram captantes, alii jacuere ut trunci, homines
crassi et insueti itinere certamine pedestri, et cum
applicuissent munitioni, exoritur undique clamor,
 <NOTE N="(459)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135C"></COL> Virg., Aen. XII, 756.</NOTE> , ascendit ut nebula super silvam fatigato de
corpore vapor. Quod videntes Boemi ad breve tempus
haesitaverunt, moxque, ut intellexerunt viribus
eos defecisse, audacter prosiliunt <NOTE N="1684" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> unt  <HI REND="ITALIC">al. manu
superscr.</HI>  1.</NOTE>  de munitione.
Audatiam

 <POEM COM="0135"><L>Dabat eis invicta soror fortunae Bellona</L> <L>O fors <NOTE N="1685" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> sors 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  fortuna! nunquam es perpetuo bona</L> <L>Instabilique rota magnates mergis in ima.</L> <L>Fortunatorum en ora <NOTE N="1686" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> opera A.  <HI REND="ITALIC">alia manu superscr.</HI>  t,  <HI REND="ITALIC">ut sit</HI>  operta.</NOTE>  verenda virorum</L> <L>Ungula ferrata <NOTE N="1687" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0135" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0135"></COL> ferrea 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> .</NOTE>  saltantium foedat equorum,</L></POEM> 

