1, 2 <SUP>b</SUP> . Chowati 3, Crouati 4. Chowati 7.</NOTE>   <HI REND="ITALIC">et altera Chrowati</HI> <NOTE N="2421" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0169"></COL> <HI REND="ITALIC">deest</HI>  A. 1, Chrowati 2, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . Hrouati 3.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(581)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0170C"></COL> Chrowatia.</NOTE> ,
 <HI REND="ITALIC">Slasane</HI> <NOTE N="2422" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0169"></COL> Zlasane
1, 2, 4.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(582)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0170C"></COL> Silesia ad montem Zobten.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Trebowane</HI> <NOTE N="2423" TYPE="Variae Lectiones" ANCHORED=Y COM="0169" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0169"></COL> Trebouane 2, 3, 4, 4 <SUP>a</SUP> . Trewobane 7.</NOTE>   <NOTE N="(583)" TYPE="Notae" ANCHORED=Y COM="0170" BLOCK="NO"><COL N="0170C"></COL> Dobnero videbatur territorium Goerlicense.
In nomine Trebouane latere opinabatur Drenow de
quo contin. Cosmae ad 1131; quod num stare possit
dubito. Kropfio est Triebel in Lusatia inferiori.</NOTE> ,  <HI REND="ITALIC">Bobrane</HI> 
